  ('ccf4e416-983f-55ca-9eb8-a91fb4398e2d', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12Q2O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'Sergeants must attend BLC to be eligible for promotion to Staff Sergeant. Sergeants may attend ALC. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to SSG with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead squad sized units.', '05bf131c2a9df590a57bc26993cb08a2220e362bcda08d9c48d3b4efc2ae16e5', 29, 29, null, 298, null, null, false, null),
  ('acb3d57a-bdc3-5c6d-89cc-abd6af3fdc9f', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12Q2O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'SGTs should focus on building a strong base of technical expertise in TOE assignments, developing Soldier leadership skills, and honing technical skills as an Exterior Electrician Lineman. At every opportunity NCOs should seek positions that allow them to gain leadership experience.', '75e0ff22fb8db18f291d37d59fb9127b80c67dbd5f535c495be11e01f41183ca', 29, 29, null, 299, null, null, false, null),
  ('6941dea2-bb73-559d-aecf-0a2b255d02a2', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12Q2O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3', '1ca32777587d687d163e0d1b8bd44c12fe2deac5d09cf6c9ae654c3e0545251a', 29, 29, null, 300, null, null, false, null),
  ('3a03781e-d300-5e2b-b935-57aa88c3fa03', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12Q2O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'Sapper Leader Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Basic Combatives Course (Level I), Expert Soldier Badge, Ranger School, Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', '0e89765b04fce6ab4b5d0f24f2226d0606f4a9acde793cfb15b2b833b29f97f1', 29, 29, null, 301, null, null, false, null),
  ('7af51a20-f3ea-5eed-91a0-c38ce9941415', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12Q2O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'Defense Attaché System (DAS).', 'a8937ffd4f22d7b51b12645bc2e2a5450914b28a379853e6dbf376cf5c10c37f', 29, 29, null, 302, null, null, false, null),
  ('fcf3e99f-377e-5d7c-a9d5-8c761cafdccf', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12Q3O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'Staff Sergeants must attend ALC to be eligible for promotion to Sergeant First Class. Staff Sergeants may attend the Senior Leaders Course. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to SFC with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead platoon sized units.', 'd51472e1c777eff2eef273c047a9e23305adc8818162e4a92f2df3a90132e05e', 29, 29, null, 303, null, null, false, null),
  ('56452355-f72a-52dd-aee7-2741884cd785', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12Q3O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'The critical key developmental (KD) assignment focus during this phase of career should be in an operational assignment as an Assistant Team Chief for a minimum of 30-36 rated months. Other duty assignments in operational units that will increase the technical expertise and develop the leadership attributes of the NCOs are Senior Exterior Electrician and Senior Lineman. SSGs who successfully complete at least 30-36 rated months followed by a successful broadening assignment are considered most qualified for promotion. Note: 30-36 month timelines are not set in stone and used primarily as a guide for HRC to assess when an NCO could be moved to the next position. The strength of the NCO’s file should be the determining factor when that NCO has successfully completed their time in that current position. For example, NCOs who have 48 months in a developmental position, but are rated as ‘Qualified’ on NCOERs would not meet the threshold of ‘Most Qualified.’ Soldiers serving in a KD position commensurate to the next higher rank (consecutively or nonconsecutively) will receive credit towards their KD requirement for both positions, provided that the KD time is captured and documented on the rated Soldier’s NCOER.', '4ea85403d014e83c0c402693e56443bd9b8018ce28047f2ae50391ef08d108b0', 29, 30, null, 304, null, null, false, null),
  ('8fa9656f-3bda-5652-bf70-e5e2d52fa018', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12Q3O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.', '32bc56e18deec4e4e2756e37e4e41005c0d53971cd1ea15b8c2322c1db2b2ec0', 30, 30, null, 305, null, null, false, null),
  ('d2c518b8-98eb-5860-b08f-1bb15bc8e0ef', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12Q3O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'Sapper Leader Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Basic Combatives Course, (Level I), Battle Staff NCO Course, Combatives Master Trainer Course (Level III), Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA), Expert Soldier Badge, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course, Master Resilience Training (MRT) Course, Ranger School, Rappel Master Course, and the Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', '95f86b0801881e7120be9f4a189fb736f69caa2d61466d5035f44c625377a356', 30, 30, null, 306, null, null, false, null),
  ('de64a833-1c14-5a0e-b672-3466ff1a06b5', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12Q3O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'Defense Attaché System (DAS).', 'a8937ffd4f22d7b51b12645bc2e2a5450914b28a379853e6dbf376cf5c10c37f', 30, 30, null, 307, null, null, false, null),
  ('3d185549-d443-55b4-9fc8-e6fd2b522b39', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12Q4O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'Sergeants First Class must attend SLC to be eligible for promotion to Master Sergeant. Sergeants First Class may attend the Master Leaders Course. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to MSG/1SG with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead company sized units.', 'ca69daf7a4e58a9ff20bf2bd7d5f465fdc4c8ce4e22b1ad0e0982d058f126c8b', 30, 30, null, 308, null, null, false, null),
  ('05ed962b-7eba-5758-90b1-1a8ee94fcec0', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12Q4O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'The critical key developmental (KD) assignment focus during this phase of their career should be in an engineer battalion serving as an Electrical Team Chief (12Q) for a minimum of 30-36 rated months. Additional operational assignments that will enhance technical expertise and develop the leadership skills of NCOs are Operations Sergeant, Detachment Sergeant, and Platoon Sergeant. SFCs who successfully complete at least 30-36 rated months followed by a successful broadening assignment are considered most qualified for promotion. Note: 30-36 month timelines are not set in stone and used primarily as a guide for HRC to assess when an NCO could be moved to the next position. The strength of the NCO’s file should be the determining factor when that NCO has successfully completed their time in that current position. For example, NCOs who have 48 months in developmental position, but are rated as ‘Qualified’ on NCOERs would not meet the threshold of ‘Most Qualified.’ Soldiers serving in a KD position commensurate to the next higher rank (consecutively or nonconsecutively) will receive credit towards their KD requirement for both positions, provided that the KD time is captured and documented rated Soldier’s NCOER.', '9fa2c585ca9b2675ca47996baefe849160974a109c8cf102a3f7c436a36d02e9', 30, 30, null, 309, null, null, false, null),
  ('a0057604-fb30-5105-9cae-795c34ffcaa9', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12Q4O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3', '1ca32777587d687d163e0d1b8bd44c12fe2deac5d09cf6c9ae654c3e0545251a', 30, 30, null, 310, null, null, false, null),
  ('7167295f-d4a3-5fed-83e2-9c1a4ce94b0f', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12Q4O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Basic Combatives Course (Level I), Battle Staff NCO Course, Combatives Master trainer Course (Level III), Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA), Expert Soldier Badge, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course, Master Resilience Training (MRT) Course, Rappel Master Course, Joint Engineer Operations Course (JEOC), Ranger School, and the Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', 'e57902a5986201a30555d88f565a8ddee2617b7cc04c44c82448359f82c7402e', 30, 30, null, 311, null, null, false, null),
  ('b4a7cdc3-cfa4-5ed1-923d-319f766a75bd', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12Q4O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 33. Military Occupational Specialty 12Q, Transmission and Distribution', 'Sexual Assault Response Coordinator (SARC), Brigade Victim Advocate (VA), Equal Opportunity Advisor (EO), Assistant Inspector General, and White House Fellowship.', '911d6ace50482c0ca2ae3de1c8248a30f4913f1a0ab03bcd5259640b164da5c3', 30, 30, null, 312, null, null, false, null),
  ('fd09c3a1-3a9d-5810-9991-4d3af74cd688', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12R', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 35. Military Occupational Specialty 12R, Interior Electrician.', 'To ensure the Engineers remain the bedrock of the Nation’s fighting force and continue to provide dynamic and flexible NCOs to the force who are prepared to win on any battlefield across the full range of military operations.', 'ee9786acabca544d09caf84d1ca2d2a09dc188d3897c8b14e808bdadb59cfda3', 31, 31, null, 313, null, null, false, null),
  ('a66e73a3-569a-58db-b55a-04b988e8e700', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12R', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12R1O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 35. Military Occupational Specialty 12R, Interior Electrician.', 'SPCs may attend the Basic Leaders Course. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to SGT with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead team sized units.', '47f0d03cb2a6d9ec643c1a34e2539c22e0e170c7185e97f4f0dc9bb78d096680', 31, 31, null, 314, null, null, false, null),
  ('0bf03b1b-fa53-5109-9388-f5bc08669aff', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12R', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12R1O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 35. Military Occupational Specialty 12R, Interior Electrician.', 'The focus during the early years of a career should be on building a strong base of technical expertise in vertical construction, basic MOS skills, and common Warrior Tasks and Drills. This can be accomplished with assignments to an engineer battalion serving as an Interior Electrician. Soldiers should seek responsibility and take advantage of opportunities to display their leadership skills, initiative, and motivation.', '0f129424b022d902829363adb6b41517903939b098a35054c6c997b7702ec62a', 31, 31, null, 315, null, null, false, null),
  ('b1f3ffb2-5f15-5846-bba0-b016a0a8cd3f', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12R', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12R1O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 35. Military Occupational Specialty 12R, Interior Electrician.', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.', '32bc56e18deec4e4e2756e37e4e41005c0d53971cd1ea15b8c2322c1db2b2ec0', 31, 31, null, 316, null, null, false, null),
  ('8b425a27-d666-5fd6-a4f3-fac62cf67cd3', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12R', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12R1O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 35. Military Occupational Specialty 12R, Interior Electrician.', 'Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Basic Combatives Course (Level I), and the Expert Soldier Badge.', 'f5f6afe3b3f87ad2e239986a152ffa5aae5951e48d092f84b659a3aa90576e2d', 31, 31, null, 317, null, null, false, null),
  ('b75439de-37c5-5540-b6d4-c51fdea318cc', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12R', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12R1O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 35. Military Occupational Specialty 12R, Interior Electrician.', 'Special assignments are those broadening assignments that provide a purposeful expansion of knowledge, capability, and understanding through assignment opportunities internal and external to the Army. These assignments are fundamental to the continued growth throughout the Soldier’s career life cycle. At this level the Soldier’s focus should be technical and tactical proficiency. Broadening assignments are crucial in developing leaders with a wider range of experiences and skills who can operate in ever-changing environments.', '77671bca0054da241155b1c8e88ea450c07cd8604b711e96de268ec3e912e50b', 31, 31, null, 318, null, null, false, null),
