  ('9a44f299-94fd-5e32-8951-2180df8f4ffc', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12T2O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.', '32bc56e18deec4e4e2756e37e4e41005c0d53971cd1ea15b8c2322c1db2b2ec0', 32, 32, null, 332, null, null, false, null),
  ('9bf3fde7-98b1-5be3-b67f-0ffbcd764d25', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12T2O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'Sapper Leader Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Basic Combatives Course (Level I), Expert Soldier Badge, Ranger School, and the Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', 'f119a96762e49b0a90fbbc96615c5d8c749365fc40ab5d5bcbb285de1fb5c6ae', 33, 33, null, 333, null, null, false, null),
  ('886bc5cb-532c-523f-a279-1b17f45b5044', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12T2O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'Recruiter, Defense Attaché System (DAS), and Training Management NCO.', '6edba3b98c1c20be5a87a94c0f26fb8c117e7befab91b27d76ba3086783dbc27', 33, 33, null, 334, null, null, false, null),
  ('b10c51f1-f3fb-576d-9535-6fed2345be07', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12T3O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'Staff Sergeants must attend ALC to be eligible for promotion to Sergeant First Class. Staff Sergeants may attend the Senior Leaders Course. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to SFC with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead platoon sized units.', 'd51472e1c777eff2eef273c047a9e23305adc8818162e4a92f2df3a90132e05e', 33, 33, null, 335, null, null, false, null),
  ('ac793c80-0c86-52fd-9c02-ee539ef6ed92', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12T3O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'The critical key developmental (KD) assignment focus during this phase of a career should be in an operational assignment as a Technical Engineer NCO or a Technical Topographic Survey NCO for a minimum of 30-36 rated months. Other duty assignments in operational units that will increase the technical expertise and develop the leadership attributes of a Technical Engineering Specialist is a Technical Topographic Survey NCO. SSGs who successfully complete at least 30-36 rated months followed by a successful broadening assignment are considered most qualified for promotion. Note: 30-36 month timelines are not set in stone and used primarily as a guide for HRC to assess when an NCO could be moved to the next position. The strength of the NCO’s file should be the determining factor when that NCO has successfully completed their time in that current position. For example, NCOs who have 48 months in a developmental position, but are rated as ‘Qualified’ on NCOERs would not meet the threshold of ‘Most Qualified. Soldiers serving in a KD position commensurate to the next higher rank (consecutively or nonconsecutively) will receive credit towards their KD requirement for both positions, provided that the KD time is captured and documented on the rated Soldier’s NCOER.', '9052146e30d65180777fef5c52231e38c3ad0a87d771e9956070047002d81127', 33, 33, null, 336, null, null, false, null),
  ('239c3630-4ad1-5423-92da-1f306246caee', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12T3O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.', '32bc56e18deec4e4e2756e37e4e41005c0d53971cd1ea15b8c2322c1db2b2ec0', 33, 33, null, 337, null, null, false, null),
  ('bb0faf1f-2d1c-5784-823e-b69e704f1fb0', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12T3O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'Sapper Leader Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course (Level I), Expert Soldier Badge, Pathfinder Course, Ranger School,), Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA) Course, Jumpmaster School, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course, Master Resilience Training (MRT) Course, Rappel Master Course, and the Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', '10c575513ef0fbdd481051b0147eae8defe184d0ada1d739274f95b39d656059', 33, 33, null, 338, null, null, false, null),
  ('c8e09745-143e-5038-9e19-b79e72cd00a3', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12T3O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'Drill Sergeant may fulfill the NCO’s requirement for a key developmental leadership position if the NCO has not had an opportunity to serve in the capacity of Technical Engineer NCO in the Operating Force. Note, however, that NCOs who complete drill sergeant duties should try to complete other operational KD assignments to stay competitive with their peers. Defense Attaché System (DAS), Security Force Assistance Brigade (SFAB), Small Group Leader, Instructor, Drill Sergeant, Training Developer, and Horizontal Construction OC/T, while a career enhancing, generally do not allow for the same level of leadership development and should not be considered appropriate alternatives to key leadership developmental positions. Commanders and CSMs must ensure SSGs being placed on special duty or temporary duty are considered for promotion and are serving in appropriate positions. Soldiers who are serving in isolated areas require special consideration from the United States Army Engineer School (USAES) and HRC for assignment back to the operational force.', 'cecc0df32d26be4e61332354cdf009a095e65f7bcdfdd8f3bc4ca3d87a1b4163', 33, 33, null, 339, null, null, false, null),
  ('2aacd6d7-6816-53cb-ac36-ebaef9653a8a', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12T4O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'Sergeants First Class must attend SLC to be eligible for promotion to Master Sergeant. Sergeants First Class may attend the Master Leaders Course. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to MSG/1SG with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead company sized units.', 'ca69daf7a4e58a9ff20bf2bd7d5f465fdc4c8ce4e22b1ad0e0982d058f126c8b', 33, 33, null, 340, null, null, false, null),
  ('390be51f-581f-5256-ba1a-4c9c498fd1a8', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12T4O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'The critical key developmental (KD) assignment focus during this phase of their career should be serving as a Senior Technical Engineer NCO or a Senior Topographic Survey NCO for a minimum of 30-36 rated months. who successfully complete at least 30-36 rated months followed by a successful broadening assignment are considered most qualified for promotion. Note: 30-36 month timelines are not set in stone and used primarily as a guide for HRC to assess when an NCO could be moved to the next position. The strength of the NCO’s file should be the determining factor when that NCO has successfully completed their time in that current position. For example, NCOs who have 48 months in a developmental position, but are rated as ‘Qualified’ on NCOERs would not meet the threshold of ‘Most Qualified.’ Soldiers serving in a KD position commensurate to the next higher rank (consecutively or nonconsecutively) will receive credit towards their KD requirement for both positions, provided that the KD time is captured and documented on the rated Soldier’s NCOER.', '68ad0771edc51af3c3ebd377bb9cc28ade8977e904632e5fa36aa187c11389cf', 34, 34, null, 341, null, null, false, null),
  ('20fd34c3-f62a-57a9-9af0-a36de364b5e5', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12T4O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.', '32bc56e18deec4e4e2756e37e4e41005c0d53971cd1ea15b8c2322c1db2b2ec0', 34, 34, null, 342, null, null, false, null),
  ('311370fb-2d87-5262-af09-305f7d3f29d2', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12T4O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'Sapper Leader Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course (Level I), Battle Staff NCO Course, Equal Opportunity Advisor Course (EOA), Expert Soldier Badge, Joint Engineer Operations Course (JEOC), Jumpmaster School, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course, Master Resilience Training (MRT) Course, Operational Contract Support Course, Rappel Master Course Ranger School, and the Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', '3383c0bf29f52a5e88507b6c6056d28e4bd933e0fa02136b4982996a059c34a7', 34, 34, null, 343, null, null, false, null),
  ('0137579d-2793-5d0f-b731-d93d523368b3', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12T', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12T4O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 38. Military Occupational Specialty 12T, Technical Engineering Specialist.', 'Senior Drill Sergeant may fulfill the NCO’s requirement for a key developmental leadership position if the NCO has not had an opportunity to serve in the capacity of Senior Technical Engineer in the Operating Force. Note, however, that NCOs who complete drill sergeant duties should try to complete other operational KD assignments to stay competitive with their peers. Sexual Assault Response Coordinator (SARC), Sr. Drill Sergeant, Sr. Small Group Leader (SGL), Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA), Inspector General Assistant, White House Fellowship, Instructor, Training Developer, and Senior Training Management NCO, while career enhancing, generally do not allow for the same level of leadership development and should not be considered appropriate alternatives to key leadership development positions. Commanders and CSMs must ensure SFCs being placed on special duty or temporary duty are considered for promotion and are serving in appropriate positions. Soldiers who are serving in isolated areas require special consideration from the United States Army Engineer School (USAES) and HRC for assignment back to the operational force.', 'c752e0d35ecd6cfdaa1bf4ffadf78cb8ba796d6da25e00912e5708be9cd81af0', 34, 34, null, 344, null, null, false, null),
  ('0e61a3ed-feb1-5661-b59a-bd7859e83cc8', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12W', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 41. Military Occupational Specialty 12W, Carpentry and Masonry Specialist.', 'To ensure the Engineers remain the bedrock of the Nation’s fighting force and continue to provide dynamic and flexible NCOs to the force who are prepared to win on any battlefield across the full range of military operations.', 'ee9786acabca544d09caf84d1ca2d2a09dc188d3897c8b14e808bdadb59cfda3', 35, 35, null, 345, null, null, false, null),
  ('94a44f9a-2671-59ae-a78c-7368c01745fa', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12W', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12W1O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 41. Military Occupational Specialty 12W, Carpentry and Masonry Specialist.', 'SPCs/CPLs may attend the Basic Leaders Course. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to SGT with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead team sized units.', 'ff00ff3f194d21bb6879656ae14a9e6bfcf06d8ee8dbc013fd96c84fbd1b0277', 35, 35, null, 346, null, null, false, null),
  ('4f740055-46cd-5210-9557-ea6458781867', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12W', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12W1O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 41. Military Occupational Specialty 12W, Carpentry and Masonry Specialist.', 'The focus during the early years of a career should be on building a strong base of technical expertise in vertical construction, basic MOS skills, and common Warrior Tasks and Drills. This can be accomplished with assignments to an engineer battalion serving as a Carpentry and Masonry Specialist. Soldiers should seek responsibility and take advantage of opportunities to display their leadership skills, initiative, and motivation.', 'a817d6f4c370813f0f0354adf698b10fb4f8e5d8db2683508eada64b8c9ff4e0', 35, 35, null, 347, null, null, false, null),
  ('c462d356-f2fd-5696-9231-4d1b28ce10f6', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12W', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12W1O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 41. Military Occupational Specialty 12W, Carpentry and Masonry Specialist.', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.', '32bc56e18deec4e4e2756e37e4e41005c0d53971cd1ea15b8c2322c1db2b2ec0', 35, 35, null, 348, null, null, false, null),
  ('4331454f-bf19-5bf7-b4b3-a53b05c65d6c', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12W', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12W1O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 41. Military Occupational Specialty 12W, Carpentry and Masonry Specialist.', 'Sapper Leader Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, and Basic Combatives Course (Level I), and the Expert Soldier Badge.', 'c215507f8b0f5ca1bf6b8c937e318e747b491e1a4775e7f7a4cee81d93acf79c', 35, 35, null, 349, null, null, false, null),
  ('260146a9-7fbf-571d-8177-0d613c363ac5', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12W', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12W1O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 41. Military Occupational Specialty 12W, Carpentry and Masonry Specialist.', 'Special assignments are those broadening assignments that provide a purposeful expansion of knowledge, capability, and understanding through assignment opportunities internal and external to the Army. These assignments are fundamental to the continued growth throughout the Soldier’s career life cycle. At this level the Soldier’s focus should be technical and tactical proficiency. Broadening assignments are crucial in developing leaders with a wider range of experiences and skills who can operate in ever-changing environments.', '77671bca0054da241155b1c8e88ea450c07cd8604b711e96de268ec3e912e50b', 35, 35, null, 350, null, null, false, null),
  ('7f172b3e-7ba2-5ec6-a67f-88403e790a07', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12W', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12W2O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 41. Military Occupational Specialty 12W, Carpentry and Masonry Specialist.', 'Sergeants must attend BLC to be eligible for promotion to Staff Sergeant. Sergeants may attend ALC. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to SSG with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead squad sized units.', '05bf131c2a9df590a57bc26993cb08a2220e362bcda08d9c48d3b4efc2ae16e5', 35, 35, null, 351, null, null, false, null),
  ('07ea4f90-bbba-546f-8a9f-c8ff6a859a43', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12W', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12W2O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 41. Military Occupational Specialty 12W, Carpentry and Masonry Specialist.', 'SGTs should focus on building a strong base of technical expertise in TOE-unit assignments, developing Soldier leadership skills, and honing technical skills a Carpentry and Masonry Sergeant. Additional duty assignments that will increase the technical expertise and develop the leadership attributes of the NCOs are Construction Operations Sergeant and S3 NCO. At every opportunity NCOs should seek positions that allow them to gain leadership experience.', 'ff7e8b475e841a5d742238014cacb2b4a45085ee8037929cad0e66568710704d', 35, 35, null, 352, null, null, false, null),
  ('f7dae5f0-862e-545d-a558-ee6feb7f2f67', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12W', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12W2O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 41. Military Occupational Specialty 12W, Carpentry and Masonry Specialist.', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.', '32bc56e18deec4e4e2756e37e4e41005c0d53971cd1ea15b8c2322c1db2b2ec0', 35, 35, null, 353, null, null, false, null),
  ('1dcab566-17f9-573f-a8c5-ef9e20dc8d0c', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12W', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12W2O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 41. Military Occupational Specialty 12W, Carpentry and Masonry Specialist.', 'Sapper Leader Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Basic Combatives Course (Level I), Expert Soldier Badge, Ranger School, and the Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', 'f119a96762e49b0a90fbbc96615c5d8c749365fc40ab5d5bcbb285de1fb5c6ae', 35, 35, null, 354, null, null, false, null),
  ('a80e6923-5cc2-57cf-8668-931cb54f2c07', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12W', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12W2O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 41. Military Occupational Specialty 12W, Carpentry and Masonry Specialist.', 'Recruiter, Defense Attaché System (DAS), Operations NCO, and Training Management NCO.', 'ffa6b4848c62b59e81d7fac653ef800f474e0b51969126bf2f539154eff1a8ca', 35, 35, null, 355, null, null, false, null),
  ('c72aead4-fe86-51aa-b55a-3a7f16fa95fb', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12X', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 44. Military Occupational Specialty 12X, General Engineering Supervisor.', 'To ensure the Engineers remain the bedrock of the Nation’s fighting force and continue to provide dynamic and flexible NCOs to the force who are prepared to win on any battlefield across the full range of military operations.', 'ee9786acabca544d09caf84d1ca2d2a09dc188d3897c8b14e808bdadb59cfda3', 36, 36, null, 356, null, null, false, null),
  ('089d9ce6-488e-587e-b130-e08d11d93275', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12X', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12X5O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 44. Military Occupational Specialty 12X, General Engineering Supervisor.', 'MSG must complete MLC to be considered for the SGM-A and promotion to SGM.', '305895050e0e3675f5025fa36cb49bfc0c1cc5fd437d4fdbe699c6dc1331f84e', 36, 36, null, 357, null, null, false, null),
  ('e59de6b6-d43e-5e19-99b0-2ec3f7257c97', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12X', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12X5O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 44. Military Occupational Specialty 12X, General Engineering Supervisor.', 'The critical key developmental (KD) assignment focus during this phase of their career should be an assignment as First Sergeant for a minimum of 30-36 months. Without a tour as First Sergeant, the opportunity for promotion to Sergeant Major is limited. First Sergeants who successfully complete at least 30-36 rated months followed by a successful broadening assignment are considered most qualified for promotion. Note: 30-36 month timelines are not set in stone and used primarily as a guide for HRC to assess when an NCO could be moved to the next position. The strength of the NCO’s file should be the determining factor when that NCO has successfully completed their time in that current position. For example, NCOs who have 48 months in a developmental position, but are rated as ‘Qualified’ on NCOERs would not meet the threshold of ‘Most Qualified.’ Soldiers serving in a KD position commensurate to the next higher rank (consecutively or nonconsecutively) will receive credit towards their KD requirement, provided that the KD time is captured and documented on the rated Soldier’s NCOER. Other operational assignments for Master Sergeants are Operations Sergeant, Construction Operations Sergeant, General Engineering Supervisor, Construction Inspector, and Maintenance Supervisor.', '2b9524ae363991bf0f32a71facf9a6346c5ae55c49130ba2d3986ea8c4e77ad6', 36, 36, null, 358, null, null, false, null),
  ('d1414132-92f2-5adc-b837-bad3eb89c04d', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12X', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12X5O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 44. Military Occupational Specialty 12X, General Engineering Supervisor.', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.', '32bc56e18deec4e4e2756e37e4e41005c0d53971cd1ea15b8c2322c1db2b2ec0', 36, 36, null, 359, null, null, false, null),
  ('3f5c8538-1fe1-5da8-a3fa-62c9c352855d', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12X', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12X5O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 44. Military Occupational Specialty 12X, General Engineering Supervisor.', 'Air Assault School, Sapper Leader Course, Pathfinder Course, Basic Airborne Course, Battle Staff NCO Course, Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA) Course, Expert Soldier Badge, Joint Engineer Operations Course (JEOC), Jumpmaster School, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course, Master Resilience Training (MRT) Course, Ranger School, Rappel Master Course, and the Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', '1b1dd9853924db51ac4d3546d62ea47c8a1b1c216d7faf97fdec7f4b81c6a747', 36, 36, null, 360, null, null, false, null),
  ('d3fd128b-98ee-55f7-9aef-606970083f7c', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12X', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12X5O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 44. Military Occupational Specialty 12X, General Engineering Supervisor.', 'Senior Career Management NCO, White House Fellowship, Senior Engineer NCO (Special Operations Aviation Command), Sexual Assault Response Coordinator (SARC),), Assistant Inspector General, Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA), Senior Research Development Test & Evaluation (RDTE) NCO, Operational Advisor, Defense Attaché System, Brigade Engineer Battalion (BEB) Senior Construction Engineer Observer- Coach/Trainer (OC/T), Senior Instructor, and Senior Combat Development NCO Operations Sergeant.', 'ab95a2d7b25185981eca068a8079af4ca30fde7b2d72985e2a103dc45f20acce', 36, 36, null, 361, null, null, false, null),
  ('e772c92d-b05b-5add-8b66-07444f82e8bf', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12X', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12X5O) — GI Jobs', 'Chapter 44. Military Occupational Specialty 12X, General Engineering Supervisor.', 'See COOL website.
(2) Engineer Senior Sergeant (12A6O). See MOS 12A.', '9c8b2d662ee3f4316e3bcfa9cdde63ad14db46b51be420424fd6fb5a0312f3ae', 37, 37, null, 362, null, null, false, null),
  ('d147b614-ca39-5e38-a483-ffac345db37d', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12Y1O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'SPCs may attend the Basic Leaders Course. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to SGT with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead team sized units.', '47f0d03cb2a6d9ec643c1a34e2539c22e0e170c7185e97f4f0dc9bb78d096680', 37, 37, null, 363, null, null, false, null),
  ('ba555d79-1dd5-50a2-9b56-f28e8259a17d', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12Y1O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'The focus during the early years of a career should be on building a strong base of technical expertise in equipment, basic MOS skills, and common Warrior Tasks and Drills. This can be acquired in TOE (tactical) assignments serving as a Geospatial Engineer by collecting and processing military geographic information from remote sensed imagery, digital data, existing geospatial products, and other collateral data sources. Soldiers should seek responsibility and take advantage of opportunities to display their leadership skills, initiative, and motivation.', '05dbbd61f3d03b969e036133aba144814bac92006cccf31853eb1d2a286d6f31', 37, 37, null, 364, null, null, false, null),
  ('31571e8d-173a-5ad1-a336-1f0e64e32368', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12Y1O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.', '32bc56e18deec4e4e2756e37e4e41005c0d53971cd1ea15b8c2322c1db2b2ec0', 37, 37, null, 365, null, null, false, null),
  ('db807e13-4ec4-5c00-8074-40a29d65cd39', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12Y1O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Sapper Leader Course, Basic Airborne Course, Air Assault School, Basic Combatives Course (Level I), Expert Soldier Badge, and Ranger School', 'b363005d1d45cba4fbed0ce6c6ea481cae82a1416146d405fec28097a8f23bff', 37, 37, null, 366, null, null, false, null),
  ('89d73a7b-e125-5806-bd40-0b6f249641f3', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E–1–Specialist/Corporal (12Y1O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Special assignments are those broadening assignments that provide a purposeful expansion of knowledge, capability, and understanding through assignment opportunities internal and external to the Army. These assignments are fundamental to the continued growth throughout the NCOs career life cycle. At this level the Soldier’s focus should be technical and tactical proficiency. Broadening assignments are crucial in developing leaders with a wider range of experiences and skills who can operate in ever-changing environments.', '66d07a4c2c924cbe32f2bf56e3ff807013fd3e17b3fbefdec7e48f284d6cd4e3', 37, 38, null, 367, null, null, false, null),
  ('c6cc7ed9-d9aa-58f6-8e56-3eb316cd037e', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12Y2O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Sergeants must attend BLC to be eligible for promotion to Staff Sergeant. Sergeants may attend ALC. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to SSG with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead squad sized units.', '05bf131c2a9df590a57bc26993cb08a2220e362bcda08d9c48d3b4efc2ae16e5', 38, 38, null, 368, null, null, false, null),
  ('1e92cf17-d40e-5ec6-bb02-d0cd22960eba', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12Y2O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Sergeants should focus on developing tactical and technical leadership skill sets, serving as a Geospatial Engineer Sergeant in the operational Army, honing technical expertise, and building a foundation of tactical knowledge. Duty assignments at brigade, division, corps geospatial teams, or at a Geospatial Planning Cell (GPC) at the Army Service Component Command (ASCC) level should be sought out to hone technical expertise and build a foundation of tactical knowledge.', 'b659b03ff3407db07ef41fa0a16218989e76072688c78296a59c3f2449d8db9e', 38, 38, null, 369, null, null, false, null),
  ('76e22f1e-8a37-5ea5-884c-9ae3b825f31c', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12Y2O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.', '32bc56e18deec4e4e2756e37e4e41005c0d53971cd1ea15b8c2322c1db2b2ec0', 38, 38, null, 370, null, null, false, null),
  ('d6241d43-d9ee-53ab-98f2-53681d0a9ec9', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12Y2O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Sapper Leader Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Basic Combatives Course (Level I), Expert Soldier Badge, Ranger School, and the Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', 'f119a96762e49b0a90fbbc96615c5d8c749365fc40ab5d5bcbb285de1fb5c6ae', 38, 38, null, 371, null, null, false, null),
  ('ec498460-488b-5ffe-bae6-3d97391db8af', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (12Y2O) — Special Assignments', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Drill Sergeant, Defense Attaché System (DAS), and Training Management NCO. Drill Sergeant may fulfill the NCO’s requirement for a KD leadership position if the NCO has not had an opportunity to serve in the capacity of Geospatial Engineer Sergeant in the Operating Force. Note, however, that NCOs who complete drill sergeant duties should try to complete other KD assignments to stay competitive with their peers.', 'e9b8ea7172a6fcd819120146fab5c5e303cfcbc7e3d820026c4db18ac4f55a62', 38, 38, null, 372, null, null, false, null),
  ('dfed0e75-7658-500d-8ba4-c8d90820c1f8', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12Y3O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Staff Sergeants must attend ALC to be eligible for promotion to Sergeant First Class. Staff Sergeants may attend the Senior Leaders Course. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to SFC with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead platoon sized units.', 'd51472e1c777eff2eef273c047a9e23305adc8818162e4a92f2df3a90132e05e', 38, 38, null, 373, null, null, false, null),
  ('893bf1e1-9b11-5183-8ea8-d15846c1501c', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12Y3O) — Operating assignments', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'The critical key developmental (KD) assignment focus during this phase of their career should be in operational assignment as a Squad Leader or Senior Geospatial Engineer Sergeant for a minimum of 30-36 rated months. Staff Sergeants must continue to develop and refine their leadership skills, tactical, and technical expertise. SSGs who successfully complete at least 30-36 rated months followed by a successful broadening assignment are considered most qualified for promotion. Note: 30-36 month timelines are not set in stone and used primarily as a guide for HRC to assess when an NCO could be moved to the next position. The strength of the NCO’s file should be the determining factor when that NCO has successfully completed their time in that current position. For example, NCOs who have 48 months in a developmental position, but are rated as ‘Qualified’ on NCOERs would not meet the threshold of ‘Most Qualified.’ Soldiers serving in a KD position commensurate to the next higher rank (consecutively or nonconsecutively) will receive credit towards their KD requirement for both positions, provided that the KD time is captured and documented on the rated Soldier’s NCOER.', 'afc107a60eabd6713319d9e5b8f4d9b25a859f916e11d119375a0cf2f066fa6f', 38, 38, null, 374, null, null, false, null),
  ('51a1d6a3-6fdf-58d3-b0e3-8339c39a54dc', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12Y3O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3.', '32bc56e18deec4e4e2756e37e4e41005c0d53971cd1ea15b8c2322c1db2b2ec0', 38, 38, null, 375, null, null, false, null),
  ('05437713-f324-5295-aa67-b777fb7760c6', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12Y3O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Sapper Leader Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA) Course, Expert Soldier Badge, Jumpmaster School, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course, Master Resilience Training (MRT) Course, Pathfinder Course, Ranger School, Rappel Master Course, and the Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', 'a70a86a25614acbfd28793427c7ce1150faf4ba3dd16ed6b7336da8ab24c65a9', 38, 38, null, 376, null, null, false, null),
  ('01e5ebe3-4d25-58f7-bb81-2e59cd33f016', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (12Y3O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Drill Sergeant may fulfill the NCO’s requirement for a KD leadership position if the NCO has not had an opportunity to serve in the capacity of Squad Leader or Senior Geospatial Engineer Sergeant in the Operating Force. Note, however, that NCOs who complete drill sergeant duties should try to complete other operational KD assignments to stay competitive with their peers. Defense Attaché System (DAS), White House Fellowship Program, Drill Sergeant, Small Group Leader (SGL), Recruiter, Instructor, and Training Developer, while career enhancing, generally do not allow for the same level of leadership development and should not be considered appropriate alternatives to key leadership development positions. Commanders and CSMs must ensure SSGs being placed on special duty or temporary duty are considered for promotion and are serving in appropriate positions. These positions should impart knowledge and skills for equipping SSGs to serve on brigade, division, and corps staff.', '389da050410e6f79d508808afe21e5443b0d30f4bc03c592edfb9d896d32b150', 38, 39, null, 377, null, null, false, null),
  ('a06fa31d-117f-55dc-9c7f-afe5ca550fa9', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12Y4O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Sergeants First Class must attend SLC to be eligible for promotion to Master Sergeant. Sergeants First Class may attend the Master Leaders Course. This course provides Soldiers selected for promotion to MSG/1SG with an opportunity to acquire the leadership, technical and tactical skills, and knowledge and experience needed to lead company sized units.', 'ca69daf7a4e58a9ff20bf2bd7d5f465fdc4c8ce4e22b1ad0e0982d058f126c8b', 39, 39, null, 378, null, null, false, null),
  ('e74b4286-11ca-551f-ad3a-5381d29f9aa8', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12Y4O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'The critical Key and Developmental (KD) assignment focus during this phase of a career should be in tactical assignments as the Senior Geospatial Engineer for a minimum of 30-36 rated months. SFCs who successfully complete 30-36 months as a Senior Geospatial Engineer followed by a successful broadening assignment are considered most qualified for promotion. Note: 30-36 month timelines are not set in stone and used primarily as a guide for HRC to assess when an NCO could be moved to the next position. The strength of the NCO’s file should be the determining factor when that NCO has successfully completed their time in that current position. For example, NCOs who have 48 months in a developmental position, but are rated as ‘Qualified’ on NCOERs would not meet the threshold of ‘Most Qualified.’ Soldiers serving in a KD position commensurate to the next higher rank (consecutively or nonconsecutively) will receive credit towards their KD requirement for both positions, provided that the KD time is captured and documented on the rated Soldier’s NCOER.', '647fd263b4e8f7847325d896a9f28a5258384b07b64488e39a2ace264c56de2d', 39, 39, null, 379, null, null, false, null),
