  ('9fe499d6-1e44-5823-ade2-a1edd80434c4', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12Y4O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Sapper Leader Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Basic), Battle Staff NCO Course, Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA), Expert Soldier Badge, Joint Engineer Operations Course (JEOC), Jumpmaster School, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course, Master Resilience Training (MRT) Course, Ranger School, Rappel Master Course, and the Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', '3c31a4b2da30ac4e59aa87f71ff549c27c772cef1130deeb8168777674eae62c', 39, 39, null, 381, null, null, false, null),
  ('fe7473b0-8628-55f0-b7b5-dfdd9145b59c', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (12Y4O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Senior Drill Sergeant may fulfill the NCO’s requirement for a KD leadership position if the NCO has not had an opportunity to serve in the capacity of Senior Geospatial Engineer Sergeant in the Operating Force. Note, however, that NCOs who complete drill sergeant duties should try to complete other KD assignments to stay competitive with their peers. Sr. Drill Sergeant, Observer-Coach/Trainer (OC/T), Recruiter, Defense Attaché System, White House Fellowship, Senior Small Group Leader, Sr. Instructor, and Training Developer, while career enhancing, generally do not allow for the same level of leadership development and should not be considered appropriate alternatives to key leadership development positions. Commanders and CSMs must ensure SFCs being placed on special duty or temporary duty are considered for promotion and are serving in appropriate positions. These positions should impart knowledge and skills for equipping SFCs to serve on corps, division, and brigade staffs.', 'a3da5e86568e810017219aced0da83b3f39981eebbcf19672e75c168d3d3cc1d', 39, 39, null, 382, null, null, false, null),
  ('157d5580-e73b-5a90-8480-5e8b43b6763e', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12Y5O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'MSG must complete MLC to be considered for the SGM-A and promotion to SGM.', '305895050e0e3675f5025fa36cb49bfc0c1cc5fd437d4fdbe699c6dc1331f84e', 39, 39, null, 383, null, null, false, null),
  ('c04de306-acbd-5eff-9f7c-11a2af0bbf93', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12Y5O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'The critical key developmental (KD) assignment focus during this phase of their career should be an assignment as First Sergeant for a minimum of 30-36 months. Without a tour as First Sergeant, the opportunity for promotion to Sergeant Major is limited. First Sergeants who successfully complete at least 30-36 rated months followed by a successful broadening assignment are considered most qualified for promotion. Note: 30-36 month timelines are not set in stone and used primarily as a guide for HRC to assess when an NCO could be moved to the next position. The strength of the NCO’s file should be the determining factor when that NCO has successfully completed their time in that current position. For example, NCOs who have 48 months in a developmental position, but are rated as ‘Qualified’ on NCOERs would not meet the threshold of ‘Most Qualified. Soldiers serving in a KD position commensurate to the next higher rank (consecutively or nonconsecutively) will receive credit towards their KD requirement, provided that the KD time is captured and documented on the rated Soldier’s NCOER.', '69ac9bf853b29f4093d717a914fb54c7a72e471f50c9e9b51a496eca083984f8', 39, 40, null, 384, null, null, false, null),
  ('c5d45af2-0bef-506a-947a-e99024fc53e2', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12Y5O) — Self-development', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to Chapter 3. -', 'db961ebc5f4d8cbd08a5334bfd2b75dc1f2eb9ff245d95c73fec952fe9d6fb46', 40, 40, null, 385, null, null, false, null),
  ('bbb71d0e-d6ef-51ec-8ad3-17c058ba4ae1', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12Y5O) — Additional training', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Air Assault School, Sapper Leader Course, Basic Airborne Course, Battle Staff NCO Course, Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA) Course, Expert Soldier Badge, Jumpmaster School, Ranger School, Rappel Master Course, Joint Engineer Operations Course (JEOC), Master Fitness Trainer (MFT) Course, Master Resilience Training (MRT) Course, and the Tactical Combatives Course (Level II).', '19ec4e45e58fed8f9c9fa9deb331a5b9fd8223e1409bdc6bc18fd6f747fe9399', 40, 40, null, 386, null, null, false, null),
  ('f81d18a1-0a8d-5ad4-a7e2-c4fe126502b8', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12Y5O) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'Senior Instructor, Senior Career Management NCO, Senior Combat Development NCO, Defense Attaché System, White House Fellowship, Assistant Inspector General, and Equal Opportunity Advisor (EOA). Sr. Geospatial Engineer Operations Sergeant.', 'ead35f79446bd374966ebfba951dccfb549d7d2f90e2c4f8a751a260a8e7f1ec', 40, 40, null, 387, null, null, false, null),
  ('a796a2c8-0fc5-57b6-97d4-fc54877635a7', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Y', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12Y5O) — GI Jobs', 'Chapter 47. Military Occupational Specialty 12Y, Geospatial Engineer.', 'See COOL website.
(6) Engineer Senior Sergeant (12A6O). See MOS 12A.', '1f775ba5ba5ab19df729f2533239ff8ce64dab164e5963429da4f1a3ef70c398', 40, 40, null, 388, null, null, false, null),
  ('c98f4dbc-8ce9-5d29-b448-17ca3f0a437d', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Z', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12Z5O) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 50. Military Occupational Specialty 12Z, Combat Engineering Senior Sergeant.', 'MSG must complete MLC to be considered for the SGM-A and promotion to SGM.', '305895050e0e3675f5025fa36cb49bfc0c1cc5fd437d4fdbe699c6dc1331f84e', 40, 40, null, 389, null, null, false, null),
  ('275c791c-c797-513f-9168-55dbf0250334', 'b0498927-bd35-5106-96c9-4cabc0932ac1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '12Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant/First Sergeant (12Z5O) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 50. Military Occupational Specialty 12Z, Combat Engineering Senior Sergeant.', 'The critical Key and Developmental (KD) assignment focus during this phase of their career should be an assignment as First Sergeant for a minimum of 30-36 months. Without a tour as First Sergeant, the opportunity for promotion to Sergeant Major is limited. First Sergeants who successfully complete at least 30-36 rated months followed by a successful broadening assignment are considered most qualified for promotion . Note: 30-36 month timelines are not set in stone and used primarily as a guide for HRC to assess when an NCO could be moved to the next position. The strength of the NCO’s file should be the determining factor when that NCO has successfully completed their time in that current position. For example, NCOs who have 48 months in a developmental position, but are rated as ‘Qualified’ on NCOERs would not meet the threshold of ‘Most Qualified.’ Soldiers serving in a KD position commensurate to the next higher rank (consecutively or nonconsecutively) will receive credit towards their KD requirement, provided that the KD time is captured and documented on the rated Soldier’s NCOER. Other operational assignments for Master Sergeants are Operations Sergeant, Intel Sergeant, Chief Bridge NCO, and Senior Engineer NCO.', '9dd34e76e858e9c4e5a1cbecad5613d0d80144f841323da9616fa2a30244acec', 40, 41, null, 390, null, null, false, null),
