  ('02fc8eb0-24d2-51e8-9b5a-1374d4b6b64b', '5a74e8de-3083-5aab-a6d3-b8cb61ab7910', 'Army', 'enlisted', '13M', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 8. MOS 13M - Multiple Launch Rocket System (MLRS) / High Mobility Artillery Rocket', 'Staff Sergeants who proactively pursue continuous learning and development cultivate essential leadership skills and practical knowledge. Earning distinctions like the Expert Soldier Badge (ESB) and participation in competitive events such as NCO of the Quarter/Year demonstrate significant potential and a commitment to self-development. Functional training enhances both individual MOS proficiency and overall unit capabilities. While all Soldiers will not be able to attend all key training courses, they should prioritize courses that align with their unit METL and TOE requirements. Such courses consist of Jumpmaster School, Master Drivers Course, Jungle School, Arctic Soldier Course, Arctic Leaders Course, Air Assault School, Basic Airborne Course, Holistic Health and Fitness Integrator Course, TC-AIMS II Unit Movement I & II, TC-AIMS System Administrator/Database Administrator, Unit Movement Officer, Equal Opportunity Leaders Course (EOLC), Rappel Master, Tactical Combatives Course Level II, ACE/SI. Self-development opportunities that support individual educational objectives include correspondence courses, professional certifications, and civilian education.', 'dd3d6f4cfb1d96323252f286f47a9886cedd6e93e3de694d92aa3932c2f37da7', 29, 29, null, 107, null, null, false, null),
