(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)
4. ASIs / Professional Development Proficiency Codes (PDPCs) associated with CMF 18 SGM/CSM: 6C Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6K Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 6P Post Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6S Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Experience 6U Post Battalion Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 6X Post Brigade Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 7C Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 7K Primary Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 7P Post Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience', 'c04fef49c87c4c370f3b71a052c2cace5704232b4d96246849607e6b237dc0d1', 21, 22, null, 51, null, null, false, null),
  ('ec06b79b-7244-5bc8-a16b-a938f92ab482', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'Special Forces branch guidance is for Noncommissioned Officers to serve in Key Development positions to be considered minimally MOS qualified (MMQ). SF NCOs should serve in a variety of institutional and operational billets throughout their career to increase their development. Professional Development Models for MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z are available at https://actnow.army.mil; and on the Army HRC website at https://www.hrc.army.mil/content/CMF%2018%20Information. NOTE: Proponent guidance should not be construed as a simplified checklist for promotion selection. It does not guarantee promotion or a competitive Order of Merit (OML) number following the Evaluation Boards. NCOs who have completed assignments in Key Development positions and consistently outperformed their peers with supporting rater and senior rater comments are viewed more favorably by board members.', 'd9b38e3ce8e2986a030eb301a72203b91af801f0d5dc60b159e736da156a01be', 11, 11, null, 52, null, null, false, null),
  ('276b6854-d815-5d7a-8f07-ff6f75e29e12', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — There are no authorized CMF 18 Sergeant positions in the Regiment', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'All Soldiers who graduate the Special Forces Qualification Course (SFQC) and meet the requirements outlined in AR 600- 8- 19: Chapter 3-1 para. (a) Regular Army will be promoted to the rank of Sergeant. These Sergeants will fill Staff Sergeant positions and follow the career path of Staff Sergeants as outlined below. NOTE: In accordance with the exception to policy from USAJFKSWCS to the Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff, G1 to current promotion policy AR 600-8-19 authorizes automatic promotion to Sergeant without regard to TIG or TIS, an appearance to a decentralized promotion board effective upon graduation from the Special Forces Qualification Course (SFQC). A Soldier who is otherwise qualified in accordance with paragraphs 1–11. Non- promotable status, AR 600-8- 19, one rank up to the rank of SGT.', 'baa12fb028573d34b62970c7d7e4b89dde129452377920ec433e0a2c0a83ef21', 12, 12, null, 53, null, null, false, null),
  ('ea2359c9-ad5a-57c2-af34-8ded31b36578', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'Must be a Basic Leader Course Graduate.', 'bc3706c896b99304d932b16572f09ae95c80869edbadfef92c2338d34a4e37b1', 12, 12, null, 54, null, null, false, null),
  ('45e4a99d-d03d-53d6-8831-55be22244202', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18B3, 18C3, 18D3, 18E3 Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, and Communications Sergeants CMF18 Staff Sergeants are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “6H” with a total of 24 months key development time as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. Only service as a SSG will be counted towards the 24-month requirement.', 'ab61e8eca78a09a05ac50fd72d4df8153a945f57fbf6fb1acdc39af58189f046', 13, 13, null, 55, null, null, false, null),
  ('8d90870c-95b3-53a0-9683-da67915c4158', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SSG should possess PDPC-ASI “6H”. Must have 24 months on an SFOD-A or PDPC-ASI 6H from CMF 11, 13, 19, 37, or 38; and rated time in a nominative position. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A NOTE: Special Consideration for SSGs filling a senior position on an SFOD-A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3E)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be an Advanced Leader Course Graduate. Special consideration for Ranger qualified. Must have one or more advanced skill (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in an associate degree program
(g) Military Supervisory Skill: Special consideration given to those SSGs who have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SSG should possess PDPC-ASI “6H”. Must have 24 months on an SFOD-A or PDPC-ASI 6H from CMF 11, 13, 19, 37, or 38. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A NOTE: Special Consideration for SSGs filling a senior position on an SFOD-A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3E)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be an Advanced Leader Course Graduate. Special consideration for Ranger qualified. Must have one or more advanced skill (See Appendix B). Special consideration should be given to those SSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in an associate degree program
(g) Military Supervisory Skill: Special consideration given to those SSGs who have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SSG. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet GED, BASD, and DOB as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER SSG Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: N/A
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '6019323141bafa9370d80dc5f44a2c27b1bfb78163632e8673fe1ab70dbf28a0', 13, 14, null, 56, null, null, false, null),
  ('0aceeb5b-e19d-542d-b2e5-1e400c00bd77', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18B4, 18C4, 18D4, 18E4, 18F4 Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, and Intelligence Sergeants CMF18 Sergeants First Class are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “7H” with a total of 24 months key development time as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. Only service as a SFC will be counted towards the 24-month requirement.', 'f2918f803a6103f2e4a35be38b2d2ea47d4f8afbd6dc9ef7ec8cc6406c5aa715', 15, 15, null, 57, null, null, false, null),
  ('9e3c95d6-08f1-5e90-90f4-44f42af76b53', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SFC should possess PDPC-ASI “7H.” Must have 24 months KD time. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The MQ SFC must have 48 months of collective time on a SFOD-A/E/G, or SMU; and rated time in a nominative position.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PSDI L3C)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Senior Leader Course Graduate. Must have two or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses. Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who are qualified in more than one CMF 18 MOS.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
(f) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(g) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing an associate degree.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SFC should possess PDPC-ASI “7H.” Must have 24 months KD time. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The HQ SFC should meet one of the following criteria:
(1) 48 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU, and rated time in a mission critical position.
(2) 60 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU.
(3) 24 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU, and prior service in a combat arms MOS with operational leadership.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3D)
(3) Special Operations Recruiting Battalion (SORB): Special Consideration for SFCs who consistently far exceed the standard while assigned to SORB.
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Senior Leader Course Graduate. Must have one or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses. Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who are qualified in more than one CMF 18 MOS.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
(f) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(g) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing an associate degree.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SFC. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER SFC Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: N/A
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '978d28ca63d2393fc2264f774312a131d284f7a9753059a087b5239395851379', 15, 17, null, 58, null, null, false, null),
  ('bf567fa3-29c2-5cd5-8d5d-969e0ca57acf', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18Z5 Special Forces Team Sergeant CMF18 Master Sergeants are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “8H” with a total of 24 months key development as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. 12 months must be served as a MSG. NOTE: While NCOs who have served as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant as a SFC have demonstrated progression ahead of their peers, up to one year of SFC Team Sergeant time can be considered as Key Developmental time. Example: A NCO served 18 months as a SFC Team Sergeant and promotes to MSG. The NCO must complete an additional 12 months as a Team Sergeant to be awarded the PDPC-ASI “8H” and be considered Key Development complete.', '12ccf6498844cf2fca2172febee9b310174066a8033e6e4b070801c65a76cfa6', 18, 18, null, 59, null, null, false, null),
  ('961a2178-ac94-5ae0-bb1c-ce7ae6ad6570', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ MSG should possess PDPC-ASI “8H.” Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater. Must have 24 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant; and rated time in a nominative position. NOTE: The SMU SF MSG must successfully serve no less than 60 months within the SMU and possess SQI-T or serve as a SMU Case Officer.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3A)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate. Must have two or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those MSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in bachelor’s degree.
(g) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring a 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ MSG should possess PDPC-ASI “8H.” Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The HQ MSG should meet one of the following criteria:
(1) 24 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant; and rated time in a mission critical position.
(2) 36 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant. NOTE: The SMU SF MSG must successfully serve no less than 48 months within the SMU and possess SQI-T or serve as a SMU Case Officer.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3B)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate for Sergeants Major Academy selection. Must have one or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those MSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in bachelor’s degree.
(g) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring a 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a MSG. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER MSG Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate for Sergeants Major Academy selection
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '3684172ea90fc56c4ac247a44141ade13d4a6422dfd3ca9ba431a942018e0b3f', 18, 20, null, 60, null, null, false, null),
  ('f08868f3-68b4-5358-946b-39cf3404bc72', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) and Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18Z6 Special Forces Operations Sergeant', 'e0489219ccb48cc98158c3dac6ae6b4ad7effb40cdb654bcb964c7828fefd809', 21, 21, null, 61, null, null, false, null),
  ('1984f2b9-b49c-58cb-af17-3445b898bc00', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18D', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) and Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SGM must have 24 months KD time; or must have PDSI “D5G” with additional rated time in a nominative position. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
(e) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing a bachelor’s degree.
(f) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SGM must have 24 months KD time; or must have PDSI “D5G” with additional rated time in a mission critical position. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
(e) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing a bachelor’s degree.
(f) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SGM. Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER CSM/SGM Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)
4. ASIs / Professional Development Proficiency Codes (PDPCs) associated with CMF 18 SGM/CSM: 6C Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6K Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 6P Post Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6S Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Experience 6U Post Battalion Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 6X Post Brigade Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 7C Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 7K Primary Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 7P Post Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience', 'c04fef49c87c4c370f3b71a052c2cace5704232b4d96246849607e6b237dc0d1', 21, 22, null, 62, null, null, false, null),
  ('19bf596b-1611-584e-abcd-c5112075f377', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18E', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'Special Forces branch guidance is for Noncommissioned Officers to serve in Key Development positions to be considered minimally MOS qualified (MMQ). SF NCOs should serve in a variety of institutional and operational billets throughout their career to increase their development. Professional Development Models for MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z are available at https://actnow.army.mil; and on the Army HRC website at https://www.hrc.army.mil/content/CMF%2018%20Information. NOTE: Proponent guidance should not be construed as a simplified checklist for promotion selection. It does not guarantee promotion or a competitive Order of Merit (OML) number following the Evaluation Boards. NCOs who have completed assignments in Key Development positions and consistently outperformed their peers with supporting rater and senior rater comments are viewed more favorably by board members.', 'd9b38e3ce8e2986a030eb301a72203b91af801f0d5dc60b159e736da156a01be', 11, 11, null, 63, null, null, false, null),
  ('a4df1b8c-7033-562d-a76f-ae1ae163d3f3', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18E', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — There are no authorized CMF 18 Sergeant positions in the Regiment', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'All Soldiers who graduate the Special Forces Qualification Course (SFQC) and meet the requirements outlined in AR 600- 8- 19: Chapter 3-1 para. (a) Regular Army will be promoted to the rank of Sergeant. These Sergeants will fill Staff Sergeant positions and follow the career path of Staff Sergeants as outlined below. NOTE: In accordance with the exception to policy from USAJFKSWCS to the Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff, G1 to current promotion policy AR 600-8-19 authorizes automatic promotion to Sergeant without regard to TIG or TIS, an appearance to a decentralized promotion board effective upon graduation from the Special Forces Qualification Course (SFQC). A Soldier who is otherwise qualified in accordance with paragraphs 1–11. Non- promotable status, AR 600-8- 19, one rank up to the rank of SGT.', 'baa12fb028573d34b62970c7d7e4b89dde129452377920ec433e0a2c0a83ef21', 12, 12, null, 64, null, null, false, null),
  ('724d3950-a1aa-5a36-bd47-6d88921a0c11', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18E', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'Must be a Basic Leader Course Graduate.', 'bc3706c896b99304d932b16572f09ae95c80869edbadfef92c2338d34a4e37b1', 12, 12, null, 65, null, null, false, null),
  ('5b71005b-fc84-56fd-baa0-9faa2917dbe3', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18E', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18B3, 18C3, 18D3, 18E3 Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, and Communications Sergeants CMF18 Staff Sergeants are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “6H” with a total of 24 months key development time as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. Only service as a SSG will be counted towards the 24-month requirement.', 'ab61e8eca78a09a05ac50fd72d4df8153a945f57fbf6fb1acdc39af58189f046', 13, 13, null, 66, null, null, false, null),
  ('aeeca359-d4bb-5a7a-ab60-e4eee9ee4e00', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18E', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SSG should possess PDPC-ASI “6H”. Must have 24 months on an SFOD-A or PDPC-ASI 6H from CMF 11, 13, 19, 37, or 38; and rated time in a nominative position. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A NOTE: Special Consideration for SSGs filling a senior position on an SFOD-A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3E)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be an Advanced Leader Course Graduate. Special consideration for Ranger qualified. Must have one or more advanced skill (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in an associate degree program
(g) Military Supervisory Skill: Special consideration given to those SSGs who have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SSG should possess PDPC-ASI “6H”. Must have 24 months on an SFOD-A or PDPC-ASI 6H from CMF 11, 13, 19, 37, or 38. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A NOTE: Special Consideration for SSGs filling a senior position on an SFOD-A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3E)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be an Advanced Leader Course Graduate. Special consideration for Ranger qualified. Must have one or more advanced skill (See Appendix B). Special consideration should be given to those SSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in an associate degree program
(g) Military Supervisory Skill: Special consideration given to those SSGs who have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SSG. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet GED, BASD, and DOB as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER SSG Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: N/A
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '6019323141bafa9370d80dc5f44a2c27b1bfb78163632e8673fe1ab70dbf28a0', 13, 14, null, 67, null, null, false, null),
  ('0823642a-64f0-5e18-8ac7-6d9d5fa0f2a9', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18E', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18B4, 18C4, 18D4, 18E4, 18F4 Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, and Intelligence Sergeants CMF18 Sergeants First Class are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “7H” with a total of 24 months key development time as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. Only service as a SFC will be counted towards the 24-month requirement.', 'f2918f803a6103f2e4a35be38b2d2ea47d4f8afbd6dc9ef7ec8cc6406c5aa715', 15, 15, null, 68, null, null, false, null),
  ('1be43e1d-0c17-5665-8d1c-1e60e1aa8062', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18E', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SFC should possess PDPC-ASI “7H.” Must have 24 months KD time. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The MQ SFC must have 48 months of collective time on a SFOD-A/E/G, or SMU; and rated time in a nominative position.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PSDI L3C)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Senior Leader Course Graduate. Must have two or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses. Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who are qualified in more than one CMF 18 MOS.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
(f) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(g) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing an associate degree.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SFC should possess PDPC-ASI “7H.” Must have 24 months KD time. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The HQ SFC should meet one of the following criteria:
(1) 48 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU, and rated time in a mission critical position.
(2) 60 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU.
(3) 24 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU, and prior service in a combat arms MOS with operational leadership.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3D)
(3) Special Operations Recruiting Battalion (SORB): Special Consideration for SFCs who consistently far exceed the standard while assigned to SORB.
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Senior Leader Course Graduate. Must have one or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses. Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who are qualified in more than one CMF 18 MOS.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
(f) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(g) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing an associate degree.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SFC. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER SFC Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: N/A
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '978d28ca63d2393fc2264f774312a131d284f7a9753059a087b5239395851379', 15, 17, null, 69, null, null, false, null),
  ('0fc42580-e848-557e-a798-21e638f402a9', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18E', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18Z5 Special Forces Team Sergeant CMF18 Master Sergeants are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “8H” with a total of 24 months key development as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. 12 months must be served as a MSG. NOTE: While NCOs who have served as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant as a SFC have demonstrated progression ahead of their peers, up to one year of SFC Team Sergeant time can be considered as Key Developmental time. Example: A NCO served 18 months as a SFC Team Sergeant and promotes to MSG. The NCO must complete an additional 12 months as a Team Sergeant to be awarded the PDPC-ASI “8H” and be considered Key Development complete.', '12ccf6498844cf2fca2172febee9b310174066a8033e6e4b070801c65a76cfa6', 18, 18, null, 70, null, null, false, null),
  ('acd105b7-4808-5dfb-8d70-8417727ad958', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18E', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ MSG should possess PDPC-ASI “8H.” Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater. Must have 24 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant; and rated time in a nominative position. NOTE: The SMU SF MSG must successfully serve no less than 60 months within the SMU and possess SQI-T or serve as a SMU Case Officer.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3A)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate. Must have two or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those MSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in bachelor’s degree.
(g) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring a 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ MSG should possess PDPC-ASI “8H.” Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The HQ MSG should meet one of the following criteria:
(1) 24 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant; and rated time in a mission critical position.
(2) 36 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant. NOTE: The SMU SF MSG must successfully serve no less than 48 months within the SMU and possess SQI-T or serve as a SMU Case Officer.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3B)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate for Sergeants Major Academy selection. Must have one or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those MSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in bachelor’s degree.
(g) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring a 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a MSG. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER MSG Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate for Sergeants Major Academy selection
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '3684172ea90fc56c4ac247a44141ade13d4a6422dfd3ca9ba431a942018e0b3f', 18, 20, null, 71, null, null, false, null),
  ('fe8c9620-69be-51dc-8c99-cdf282d23942', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18E', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) and Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18Z6 Special Forces Operations Sergeant', 'e0489219ccb48cc98158c3dac6ae6b4ad7effb40cdb654bcb964c7828fefd809', 21, 21, null, 72, null, null, false, null),
  ('109d2056-877b-57a0-9763-b4a7b064b7d9', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18E', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) and Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SGM must have 24 months KD time; or must have PDSI “D5G” with additional rated time in a nominative position. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
(e) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing a bachelor’s degree.
(f) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SGM must have 24 months KD time; or must have PDSI “D5G” with additional rated time in a mission critical position. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
(e) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing a bachelor’s degree.
(f) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SGM. Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER CSM/SGM Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)
4. ASIs / Professional Development Proficiency Codes (PDPCs) associated with CMF 18 SGM/CSM: 6C Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6K Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 6P Post Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6S Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Experience 6U Post Battalion Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 6X Post Brigade Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 7C Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 7K Primary Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 7P Post Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience', 'c04fef49c87c4c370f3b71a052c2cace5704232b4d96246849607e6b237dc0d1', 21, 22, null, 73, null, null, false, null),
  ('524941c7-e1b2-5e6a-8933-3d2b7bf2adc0', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18F', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'Special Forces branch guidance is for Noncommissioned Officers to serve in Key Development positions to be considered minimally MOS qualified (MMQ). SF NCOs should serve in a variety of institutional and operational billets throughout their career to increase their development. Professional Development Models for MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z are available at https://actnow.army.mil; and on the Army HRC website at https://www.hrc.army.mil/content/CMF%2018%20Information. NOTE: Proponent guidance should not be construed as a simplified checklist for promotion selection. It does not guarantee promotion or a competitive Order of Merit (OML) number following the Evaluation Boards. NCOs who have completed assignments in Key Development positions and consistently outperformed their peers with supporting rater and senior rater comments are viewed more favorably by board members.', 'd9b38e3ce8e2986a030eb301a72203b91af801f0d5dc60b159e736da156a01be', 11, 11, null, 74, null, null, false, null),
  ('87053afc-c446-57af-96fe-7796c654490f', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18F', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — There are no authorized CMF 18 Sergeant positions in the Regiment', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'All Soldiers who graduate the Special Forces Qualification Course (SFQC) and meet the requirements outlined in AR 600- 8- 19: Chapter 3-1 para. (a) Regular Army will be promoted to the rank of Sergeant. These Sergeants will fill Staff Sergeant positions and follow the career path of Staff Sergeants as outlined below. NOTE: In accordance with the exception to policy from USAJFKSWCS to the Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff, G1 to current promotion policy AR 600-8-19 authorizes automatic promotion to Sergeant without regard to TIG or TIS, an appearance to a decentralized promotion board effective upon graduation from the Special Forces Qualification Course (SFQC). A Soldier who is otherwise qualified in accordance with paragraphs 1–11. Non- promotable status, AR 600-8- 19, one rank up to the rank of SGT.', 'baa12fb028573d34b62970c7d7e4b89dde129452377920ec433e0a2c0a83ef21', 12, 12, null, 75, null, null, false, null),
  ('ad03581e-e07f-5144-ad88-d65637d09015', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18F', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'Must be a Basic Leader Course Graduate.', 'bc3706c896b99304d932b16572f09ae95c80869edbadfef92c2338d34a4e37b1', 12, 12, null, 76, null, null, false, null),
  ('51db7502-a15c-5c0f-9163-9761b1ca5f25', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18F', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18B3, 18C3, 18D3, 18E3 Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, and Communications Sergeants CMF18 Staff Sergeants are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “6H” with a total of 24 months key development time as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. Only service as a SSG will be counted towards the 24-month requirement.', 'ab61e8eca78a09a05ac50fd72d4df8153a945f57fbf6fb1acdc39af58189f046', 13, 13, null, 77, null, null, false, null),
  ('f3df96b0-e618-5da8-ba52-549c4bc3aa3d', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18F', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SSG should possess PDPC-ASI “6H”. Must have 24 months on an SFOD-A or PDPC-ASI 6H from CMF 11, 13, 19, 37, or 38; and rated time in a nominative position. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A NOTE: Special Consideration for SSGs filling a senior position on an SFOD-A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3E)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be an Advanced Leader Course Graduate. Special consideration for Ranger qualified. Must have one or more advanced skill (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in an associate degree program
(g) Military Supervisory Skill: Special consideration given to those SSGs who have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SSG should possess PDPC-ASI “6H”. Must have 24 months on an SFOD-A or PDPC-ASI 6H from CMF 11, 13, 19, 37, or 38. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A NOTE: Special Consideration for SSGs filling a senior position on an SFOD-A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3E)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be an Advanced Leader Course Graduate. Special consideration for Ranger qualified. Must have one or more advanced skill (See Appendix B). Special consideration should be given to those SSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in an associate degree program
(g) Military Supervisory Skill: Special consideration given to those SSGs who have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SSG. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet GED, BASD, and DOB as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER SSG Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: N/A
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '6019323141bafa9370d80dc5f44a2c27b1bfb78163632e8673fe1ab70dbf28a0', 13, 14, null, 78, null, null, false, null),
  ('da2dc58f-da1a-5ee2-8965-59251ccc62c5', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18F', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18B4, 18C4, 18D4, 18E4, 18F4 Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, and Intelligence Sergeants CMF18 Sergeants First Class are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “7H” with a total of 24 months key development time as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. Only service as a SFC will be counted towards the 24-month requirement.', 'f2918f803a6103f2e4a35be38b2d2ea47d4f8afbd6dc9ef7ec8cc6406c5aa715', 15, 15, null, 79, null, null, false, null),
  ('dd0afc88-3c28-54f7-b125-77386277e10e', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18F', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SFC should possess PDPC-ASI “7H.” Must have 24 months KD time. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The MQ SFC must have 48 months of collective time on a SFOD-A/E/G, or SMU; and rated time in a nominative position.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PSDI L3C)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Senior Leader Course Graduate. Must have two or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses. Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who are qualified in more than one CMF 18 MOS.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
(f) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(g) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing an associate degree.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SFC should possess PDPC-ASI “7H.” Must have 24 months KD time. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The HQ SFC should meet one of the following criteria:
(1) 48 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU, and rated time in a mission critical position.
(2) 60 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU.
(3) 24 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU, and prior service in a combat arms MOS with operational leadership.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3D)
(3) Special Operations Recruiting Battalion (SORB): Special Consideration for SFCs who consistently far exceed the standard while assigned to SORB.
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Senior Leader Course Graduate. Must have one or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses. Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who are qualified in more than one CMF 18 MOS.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
(f) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(g) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing an associate degree.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SFC. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER SFC Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: N/A
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '978d28ca63d2393fc2264f774312a131d284f7a9753059a087b5239395851379', 15, 17, null, 80, null, null, false, null),
  ('1b1519e1-4fcb-5d28-88ab-72fe9b6ae689', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18F', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18Z5 Special Forces Team Sergeant CMF18 Master Sergeants are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “8H” with a total of 24 months key development as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. 12 months must be served as a MSG. NOTE: While NCOs who have served as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant as a SFC have demonstrated progression ahead of their peers, up to one year of SFC Team Sergeant time can be considered as Key Developmental time. Example: A NCO served 18 months as a SFC Team Sergeant and promotes to MSG. The NCO must complete an additional 12 months as a Team Sergeant to be awarded the PDPC-ASI “8H” and be considered Key Development complete.', '12ccf6498844cf2fca2172febee9b310174066a8033e6e4b070801c65a76cfa6', 18, 18, null, 81, null, null, false, null),
  ('93feabab-a266-5d8b-a292-45286eedc682', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18F', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ MSG should possess PDPC-ASI “8H.” Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater. Must have 24 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant; and rated time in a nominative position. NOTE: The SMU SF MSG must successfully serve no less than 60 months within the SMU and possess SQI-T or serve as a SMU Case Officer.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3A)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate. Must have two or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those MSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in bachelor’s degree.
(g) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring a 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ MSG should possess PDPC-ASI “8H.” Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The HQ MSG should meet one of the following criteria:
(1) 24 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant; and rated time in a mission critical position.
(2) 36 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant. NOTE: The SMU SF MSG must successfully serve no less than 48 months within the SMU and possess SQI-T or serve as a SMU Case Officer.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3B)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate for Sergeants Major Academy selection. Must have one or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those MSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in bachelor’s degree.
(g) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring a 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a MSG. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER MSG Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate for Sergeants Major Academy selection
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '3684172ea90fc56c4ac247a44141ade13d4a6422dfd3ca9ba431a942018e0b3f', 18, 20, null, 82, null, null, false, null),
  ('69014a66-54dd-5a4f-9717-bfd54d434829', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18F', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) and Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18Z6 Special Forces Operations Sergeant', 'e0489219ccb48cc98158c3dac6ae6b4ad7effb40cdb654bcb964c7828fefd809', 21, 21, null, 83, null, null, false, null),
  ('410ff313-919b-503e-a8ee-b145cb92a95c', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18F', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) and Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SGM must have 24 months KD time; or must have PDSI “D5G” with additional rated time in a nominative position. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
(e) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing a bachelor’s degree.
(f) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SGM must have 24 months KD time; or must have PDSI “D5G” with additional rated time in a mission critical position. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
(e) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing a bachelor’s degree.
(f) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SGM. Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER CSM/SGM Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)
4. ASIs / Professional Development Proficiency Codes (PDPCs) associated with CMF 18 SGM/CSM: 6C Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6K Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 6P Post Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6S Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Experience 6U Post Battalion Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 6X Post Brigade Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 7C Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 7K Primary Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 7P Post Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience', 'c04fef49c87c4c370f3b71a052c2cace5704232b4d96246849607e6b237dc0d1', 21, 22, null, 84, null, null, false, null),
  ('6013cb12-3ce0-5fac-bb23-fe082ae91f89', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18Z', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'Special Forces branch guidance is for Noncommissioned Officers to serve in Key Development positions to be considered minimally MOS qualified (MMQ). SF NCOs should serve in a variety of institutional and operational billets throughout their career to increase their development. Professional Development Models for MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z are available at https://actnow.army.mil; and on the Army HRC website at https://www.hrc.army.mil/content/CMF%2018%20Information. NOTE: Proponent guidance should not be construed as a simplified checklist for promotion selection. It does not guarantee promotion or a competitive Order of Merit (OML) number following the Evaluation Boards. NCOs who have completed assignments in Key Development positions and consistently outperformed their peers with supporting rater and senior rater comments are viewed more favorably by board members.', 'd9b38e3ce8e2986a030eb301a72203b91af801f0d5dc60b159e736da156a01be', 11, 11, null, 85, null, null, false, null),
  ('33e79db4-b7f9-55db-bd5c-4c5e6fd0f540', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18Z', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — There are no authorized CMF 18 Sergeant positions in the Regiment', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'All Soldiers who graduate the Special Forces Qualification Course (SFQC) and meet the requirements outlined in AR 600- 8- 19: Chapter 3-1 para. (a) Regular Army will be promoted to the rank of Sergeant. These Sergeants will fill Staff Sergeant positions and follow the career path of Staff Sergeants as outlined below. NOTE: In accordance with the exception to policy from USAJFKSWCS to the Office of the Deputy Chief of Staff, G1 to current promotion policy AR 600-8-19 authorizes automatic promotion to Sergeant without regard to TIG or TIS, an appearance to a decentralized promotion board effective upon graduation from the Special Forces Qualification Course (SFQC). A Soldier who is otherwise qualified in accordance with paragraphs 1–11. Non- promotable status, AR 600-8- 19, one rank up to the rank of SGT.', 'baa12fb028573d34b62970c7d7e4b89dde129452377920ec433e0a2c0a83ef21', 12, 12, null, 86, null, null, false, null),
  ('142baecc-a79a-5282-b1df-c62bd3bd3f0f', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18Z', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Professional Military Education', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'Must be a Basic Leader Course Graduate.', 'bc3706c896b99304d932b16572f09ae95c80869edbadfef92c2338d34a4e37b1', 12, 12, null, 87, null, null, false, null),
  ('b5762d6f-1b6c-529b-8184-377f3946450b', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18Z', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18B3, 18C3, 18D3, 18E3 Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, and Communications Sergeants CMF18 Staff Sergeants are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “6H” with a total of 24 months key development time as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. Only service as a SSG will be counted towards the 24-month requirement.', 'ab61e8eca78a09a05ac50fd72d4df8153a945f57fbf6fb1acdc39af58189f046', 13, 13, null, 88, null, null, false, null),
  ('a939a88c-d344-5bed-be6b-3c9e3bc1302c', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18Z', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SSG should possess PDPC-ASI “6H”. Must have 24 months on an SFOD-A or PDPC-ASI 6H from CMF 11, 13, 19, 37, or 38; and rated time in a nominative position. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A NOTE: Special Consideration for SSGs filling a senior position on an SFOD-A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3E)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be an Advanced Leader Course Graduate. Special consideration for Ranger qualified. Must have one or more advanced skill (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in an associate degree program
(g) Military Supervisory Skill: Special consideration given to those SSGs who have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SSG should possess PDPC-ASI “6H”. Must have 24 months on an SFOD-A or PDPC-ASI 6H from CMF 11, 13, 19, 37, or 38. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A NOTE: Special Consideration for SSGs filling a senior position on an SFOD-A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3E)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be an Advanced Leader Course Graduate. Special consideration for Ranger qualified. Must have one or more advanced skill (See Appendix B). Special consideration should be given to those SSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in an associate degree program
(g) Military Supervisory Skill: Special consideration given to those SSGs who have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SSG. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet GED, BASD, and DOB as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER SSG Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: N/A
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '6019323141bafa9370d80dc5f44a2c27b1bfb78163632e8673fe1ab70dbf28a0', 13, 14, null, 89, null, null, false, null),
  ('312bc3f0-cc66-547a-9798-8a3ec7ccf68a', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18Z', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18B4, 18C4, 18D4, 18E4, 18F4 Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, and Intelligence Sergeants CMF18 Sergeants First Class are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “7H” with a total of 24 months key development time as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. Only service as a SFC will be counted towards the 24-month requirement.', 'f2918f803a6103f2e4a35be38b2d2ea47d4f8afbd6dc9ef7ec8cc6406c5aa715', 15, 15, null, 90, null, null, false, null),
  ('f83a1ee9-0c8c-55d9-b329-3eaa43aaafbb', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18Z', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SFC should possess PDPC-ASI “7H.” Must have 24 months KD time. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The MQ SFC must have 48 months of collective time on a SFOD-A/E/G, or SMU; and rated time in a nominative position.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PSDI L3C)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Senior Leader Course Graduate. Must have two or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses. Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who are qualified in more than one CMF 18 MOS.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
(f) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(g) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing an associate degree.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SFC should possess PDPC-ASI “7H.” Must have 24 months KD time. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The HQ SFC should meet one of the following criteria:
(1) 48 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU, and rated time in a mission critical position.
(2) 60 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU.
(3) 24 months of collective time on an SFOD-A/E/G or SMU, and prior service in a combat arms MOS with operational leadership.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3D)
(3) Special Operations Recruiting Battalion (SORB): Special Consideration for SFCs who consistently far exceed the standard while assigned to SORB.
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Senior Leader Course Graduate. Must have one or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses. Special consideration should be given to those SFCs who are qualified in more than one CMF 18 MOS.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2.
(f) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
(g) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing an associate degree.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SFC. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER SFC Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: N/A
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '978d28ca63d2393fc2264f774312a131d284f7a9753059a087b5239395851379', 15, 17, null, 91, null, null, false, null),
  ('dd109bf2-66eb-545c-8e87-edb6f0f1123a', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18Z', null, 'development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18Z5 Special Forces Team Sergeant CMF18 Master Sergeants are considered minimally MOS Qualified (MMQ) and eligible to be awarded PDPC-ASI “8H” with a total of 24 months key development as defined in Appendix A: Key Developmental Assignments. 12 months must be served as a MSG. NOTE: While NCOs who have served as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant as a SFC have demonstrated progression ahead of their peers, up to one year of SFC Team Sergeant time can be considered as Key Developmental time. Example: A NCO served 18 months as a SFC Team Sergeant and promotes to MSG. The NCO must complete an additional 12 months as a Team Sergeant to be awarded the PDPC-ASI “8H” and be considered Key Development complete.', '12ccf6498844cf2fca2172febee9b310174066a8033e6e4b070801c65a76cfa6', 18, 18, null, 92, null, null, false, null),
  ('3e92cf95-f451-52dc-bb1b-d09db00f0947', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18Z', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ MSG should possess PDPC-ASI “8H.” Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater. Must have 24 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant; and rated time in a nominative position. NOTE: The SMU SF MSG must successfully serve no less than 60 months within the SMU and possess SQI-T or serve as a SMU Case Officer.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3A)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 475 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate. Must have two or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those MSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in bachelor’s degree.
(g) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring a 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ MSG should possess PDPC-ASI “8H.” Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater. The HQ MSG should meet one of the following criteria:
(1) 24 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant; and rated time in a mission critical position.
(2) 36 months as a SFOD-A/E/G or SMU Team Sergeant. NOTE: The SMU SF MSG must successfully serve no less than 48 months within the SMU and possess SQI-T or serve as a SMU Case Officer.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A (PDSI L3B)
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate for Sergeants Major Academy selection. Must have one or more advanced skills (See Appendix B1). Special consideration should be given to those MSGs who achieve Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Commandant’s List, or is the Leadership Awardee at PME and MOS enhancing courses.
(e) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
(f) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of enrolling in bachelor’s degree.
(g) Language: Should meet the language proficiency standard (per AR 11-6, 1-15 m and USASOC Reg 350-1, 4-5 a) by scoring a 1+ on the Oral Proficiency Interview (16 in Speaking) or 1+/1+ on the Defense Language Proficiency Test (16 in Reading and 16 in Listening) within 12 months as reflected on the Soldier Talent Profile.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a MSG. Must be serving in a Mission Essential Billet (See Appendix A). Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER MSG Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: Must be a Master Leader Course Graduate for Sergeants Major Academy selection
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)', '3684172ea90fc56c4ac247a44141ade13d4a6422dfd3ca9ba431a942018e0b3f', 18, 20, null, 93, null, null, false, null),
  ('fa93b7a1-137e-5bce-9e1b-cf0067660e1e', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18Z', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) and Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — overview', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', 'MOS 18Z6 Special Forces Operations Sergeant', 'e0489219ccb48cc98158c3dac6ae6b4ad7effb40cdb654bcb964c7828fefd809', 21, 21, null, 94, null, null, false, null),
  ('812d6a97-c308-577e-bf9c-2b93ff6a2bb2', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18Z', null, 'promotion_criteria', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) and Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — promotion consideration', 'Chapter 4. MOS 18B, 18C, 18D, 18E, 18F, and 18Z: Special Forces Weapons, Engineer, Medical, Communications, Intelligence, Team, and Operations Sergeants', '1. Most Qualified (Superior Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The MQ SGM must have 24 months KD time; or must have PDSI “D5G” with additional rated time in a nominative position. Must have pattern of superior performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Nominative Assignments: See Appendix A
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
(e) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing a bachelor’s degree.
(f) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
2. Highly Qualified (Outstanding Performance and Potential)
(a) Leadership: The HQ SGM must have 24 months KD time; or must have PDSI “D5G” with additional rated time in a mission critical position. Must have pattern of outstanding performance and potential by the Senior Rater.
(b) Assignments
(1) Key Developmental Assignments: See Appendix A
(2) Mission Critical Assignments: See Appendix A
(c) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 450 or more. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(d) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
(e) Civilian Education: Should set their educational goal of completing a bachelor’s degree.
(f) Military Supervisory Skill: Must have one supervisory skillset in Appendix B2. Should be a Jumpmaster.
3. Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Must be a SGM. Must meet criteria as outlined in corresponding FY HRC MILPER CSM/SGM Evaluation Board Announcement Message.
(b) Physical Fitness: Must pass the AFT with a total score of 410 or be on a current profile. Must score 80 points on the MDL, HRP, SDC, and PLK, and 90 points in the 2MR in the M/C category in the soldier’s age group. Must meet Height and Weight IAW AR 600-9.
(c) Military Education: Must be a United States Army Sergeants Major Academy (USASMA), Joint Special Operations Forces Senior Enlisted Academy (JSOFSEA) Graduate, or equivalent course.
4. Not Fully Qualified
(a) Leadership: Received one of the following in the last 12 months in current grade:
(1) General Officer Memorandum of Reprimand (GOMAR)
(2) Relief for Cause NCOER
(3) Annotation of “Did Not Meet Standard” in Part IV (Performance Evaluation, Professionalism, Attributes, and Competencies), block c (Character)
(4) Annotation of “Not Qualified” in Part V (Senior Rater Overall Potential), block a (Rated Noncommissioned Officer’s Potential)
4. ASIs / Professional Development Proficiency Codes (PDPCs) associated with CMF 18 SGM/CSM: 6C Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6K Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 6P Post Battalion Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 6S Initial Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Experience 6U Post Battalion Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 6X Post Brigade Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Broadening Experience 7C Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience 7K Primary Level Sergeant Major (SGM) Key Billet Experience (CSL) 7P Post Brigade Level Command Sergeant Major (CSM) Experience', 'c04fef49c87c4c370f3b71a052c2cace5704232b4d96246849607e6b237dc0d1', 21, 22, null, 95, null, null, false, null),
  ('97fbb57c-bf26-5f0b-9f55-38debee40afc', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18B', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 4-app1. Appendix A – Assignments', '(All assignments are in order of precedence)', '4d13dbbe24bda04a781c1c1d6735b85b5221cc5f69735b2815a65b48336a23a9', 23, 23, null, 96, null, null, false, null),
  ('009c6d8f-9725-5899-948a-df030e361110', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18B', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — assignments (appendix; applies to every MOS in this chapter)', 'Chapter 4-app1. Appendix A – Assignments', '(a) Key Developmental (ASI 6H): - 24 months as a SSG on a SFOD-A
(b) Nominative (PDSI L3E): - Recruiter - Drill Sergeant
(c) Mission Critical (PDSI L3F): - SFOD-B Assistant Operations SGT
(d) Mission Essential: - All other SSG positions not previously listed', 'd807f7a9726c88593a4dbc8d4085727fa43762f7f044e3a4db3938e2acb6b461', 23, 23, null, 97, null, null, false, null),
  ('89b2192e-ba45-5cd4-8844-1e2813eadd53', 'ef906047-2061-5aac-9b72-c7c5df2e2a60', 'Army', 'enlisted', '18B', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class — assignments (appendix; applies to every MOS in this chapter)', 'Chapter 4-app1. Appendix A – Assignments', '(a) Key Developmental (ASI 7H): - 24 months as a SFC on a SFOD-A/E/G, SMU, SWCS SR INSTR/WTR, Nominative, and/or Mission Critical Position (Note: above positions can be combined to total 24 months)
