  ('294376ad-8b4a-5849-9d5c-5dec9527f20c', '56bef1ab-8e6e-5b41-829b-732be0249ceb', 'Army', 'enlisted', '27D', null, 'development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) (SL4) — Physical Fitness', 'Chapter 4. Military Occupational Specialty 27D Paralegal Specialist for Active Component', 'A Sergeant First Class’s sustained dedication to physical fitness underscores their commitment to personal readiness, a critical aspect of their role as a seasoned senior leader. Maintaining peak physical fitness allows a senior paralegal NCO to mentor Soldiers and to operate in austere environments, contributing to the overall readiness of their team, including other paralegal NCOs, which directly affects their tactical proficiency. By consistently demonstrating their commitment, a senior paralegal NCO inspires their subordinates to prioritize physical fitness and maintain a warrior ethos.
(1) MQ: AFT score 450 or above, with a score of 90 in each event.
(2) HQ: AFT score 400 or above, with a score of 80 in each event.
(3) Q: Minimum AFT score of 300, with a score of 60 in each event and meets AR 600-9 qualifications.', '7a29fa76446acfb104cf22f011c6cebadc6eeeb0dc0975ec9df59a7d41152c8a', 27, 28, null, 36, null, null, false, null),
