  ('55a8ec86-07c1-50d3-8c53-d6a2ef67c010', '648e1a41-1d8a-53b5-8353-c635aca4b0f2', 'Army', 'enlisted', '46V', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major (SGM/CSM/E-9) — recommended career management (applies to every MOS in this career management field)', 'Chapter 1. Public Affairs (Career Management Field 46) Career Progression Plan', '(1) The goal of the SGM is to continually advise commanders, staffs, and Public Affairs officers. They also provide expertise for all enlisted matters and enforce standards, discipline, and adherence to Army policy and doctrine. Outstanding communication skills are required by SGMs due to their scope of influence and often represent the command or Army in civic functions and must be skilled in community and public relations. SGMs should continually seek personal and professional development through a college education, from a degree- producing institution, related to their MOS. SGMs display mastery of Army and PA policy, programs, and processes. SGMs advise command/organization leaders on all aspects of information advantage activities. SGMs mentor, advise, and develop junior officers, NCOs, and civilians to employ communication strategies and plans consistent with the seven core Public Affairs responsibilities. They demonstrate mastery of strategic leadership by extending their influence across units/organizations, commands, and across the joint service, as applicable.
