  ('ec3486b9-51cd-5194-a706-e22088fbf659', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68L', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Self-development', 'Chapter 13. 68L – Occupational Therapy Specialist', 'It is recommended SFC’ complete the EJPME II course in addition to information listed in paragraph (13-6c).', 'a41c4b39420fe41d2bdeee48aa0741aa145dfcebc74a1a693133ba1a8f5e632f', 49, 49, null, 461, null, null, false, null),
  ('5dc433b8-4b07-5c03-b757-4a1023c597b1', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68L', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Additional training', 'Chapter 13. 68L – Occupational Therapy Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-9d) and (2-9e).', '4dbd76a5d851c56043a053d34a327f63c242cb1ec07c7995d93b9beafe72be21', 49, 49, null, 462, null, null, false, null),
  ('c5723ae2-d99f-54c0-bee0-be3ff668dcbe', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68L', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Broadening', 'Chapter 13. 68L – Occupational Therapy Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, Detachment Sergeant, DS, EO Advisor (EOA), IG NCO, Instructor, Joint positions, OC/T, NCOIC positions, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, Platoon Sergeant (PSG), MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Senior DS, Senior DS Leader, Senior SGL, SRU PSG, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Training Developer.', '40ca9313ee737b26a75742433cf967826a0ad7292659f488e8c7ce4a497a5086', 49, 49, null, 463, null, null, false, null),
  ('27180f67-94ea-546d-8c55-591c52e4ce26', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68L', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 13. 68L – Occupational Therapy Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'f55071b398a6906dfc3418f08533f9fd34ffbc29a25fff4cdf464ebdd54e4073', 49, 49, null, 464, null, null, false, null),
  ('d981a6d5-007c-551e-a3de-3f1fd12db88e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'The Nutrition Care Specialist assists in the supervision of medical nutrition care operations, or plans, prepares, cooks, and serves food for regular or modified diets in field and fixed hospitals. 14–1. Position Titles with MOS, SQI and ASI Codes 68M titles include - 68M1O Nutrition Care Spec; 68M2O Nutrition Care SGT; 68M3O Nutrition Care NCO; 68M34 Recruiter; 68M34L Recruiter; 68M38 Instructor; 68M38 SGL; 68M4O Nutrition Care NCO; 68M48 Instructor; 68M48 Instructor/Writer; 68M5O Sr Nutrition Care NCO; 68M5M First Sergeant.', '8d0327c7550f0dbb6a44c52d516437557409b3c9871fd75fe47950af1cb30b1a', 49, 50, null, 465, null, null, false, null),
  ('71c41038-4e4b-58b5-a35e-947551bfca08', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'A combination of assignments in both Table of Organization and Equipment (TOE) OF units and Table of Distribution and Allowances (TDA) GF units provide the ideal promotion foundation for normal career progression. TOE assignments provide the basis for training and competence in common tasks, tactical expertise, essential medical support, repair tasks, and leadership. TDA assignments provide more in-depth and specialized training. Although successive assignments and extended TOE or TDA assignment periods are not recommended; it is important to note that limited TOE positions may result in lengthier durations within the TDA. Soldiers should concentrate on developing their medical support technical and leadership skills in these assignments. Advancement recommendations are determined on mastering these skills and displaying the aptitude and attitude consistent with the "whole Soldier" concept.', 'd624cab794ee10e2a0c71cb5327787ab3c7117ac1500645987d1b5520fd08e08', 50, 50, null, 466, null, null, false, null),
  ('4edff920-f4b2-5352-847c-cdd2e7aa6099', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'The 7-week, 2-day MOS AIT is conducted at the JBSA-FSH, METC followed by an assignment in the newly established specialized skill set. This comprehensive program is designed to train enlisted personnel in nutrition care operations to include basic nutrition concepts, clinical nutrition concepts and functions, performance nutrition for warriors, therapeutic and regular patient diet preparation, assembly and service, and Army Medical Field Feeding concepts and functions in a mobile environment. See Ch. 2 (2-5b) for PME requirements.', 'f0a22c99acd15d68138cf7b3c33a5a325b9219039511a8c35ab97b701f02bf7d', 50, 50, null, 467, null, null, false, null),
  ('5642630c-8f5d-542d-8950-92628553fc9a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', '68Ms serve in MED DETs, field hospitals, and augmentation unit Holistic Health, and Fitness (H2F) positions.', 'b7df3b05c01700c085eb45d25595923774a8b422e545c57177bb54dcd4a0b7fc', 50, 50, null, 468, null, null, false, null),
  ('2fa7e1df-3b83-5794-8d5c-bef6891bcd7b', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Self-development', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Soldiers should begin formulating plans with long-term objectives, concentrating on their military skills while considering civilian education and degree-producing programs. It is also recommended Soldiers complete Army COOL - 68M - Certifications/Licenses. At a minimum, the ServSafe Manager Certification, the Joint Forces Nutrition and Operations Course (JFNOC) and optional American Culinary Federation (ACF) certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'bba4cad20127c16b6757385dea7cec9b6584c9429df6a5747b7c45042d259047', 50, 50, null, 469, null, null, false, null),
  ('c87b139a-48b8-5820-90fd-51de64297fe0', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Additional training', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-6d) and (2-6e).', '7cd54815f52e7795535c2a2a0616c1429545fbc98e4940523dc32948c6d14ac9', 50, 50, null, 470, null, null, false, null),
  ('d5b5274c-b265-552e-9033-c3dc6feaac20', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities Soldiers should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '2c2544455441782fe90358d790aeb5eb6bc6362a3ea50572cb9512ecdbdda650', 50, 50, null, 471, null, null, false, null),
  ('1cb02ee9-2323-5896-ad91-870634cc1f46', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5c).', 'bda5558b772a2f3f63e3177b5b82498729937cfeddb1fc72b3a6f0859e6b0499', 50, 50, null, 472, null, null, false, null),
  ('a8429023-14be-58bd-9fba-a3102f02e178', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', '68M SGTs serve in field hospitals and augmentation unit H2F positions.', 'fc7da1d3b7198a0ad8a5886bb56c80fffd14fa8100a92ee6ea42f45ca4ddf6fb', 50, 50, null, 473, null, null, false, null),
  ('05315055-0c5e-5267-8140-84b34cc0b38a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Self-development', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Although not mandatory SGTs should develop a plan to acquire a degree. It is also recommended SGTs complete the Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (EJPME) I course in addition to Army COOL - 68M - Certifications/Licenses, and the Joint Annual Nutrition and Dietitian (JAND) course. Upon ALC completion, SGTs are recommended to submit attendance request for the Certified Dietary Manager course. Requests are processed through the MEDCoE, Nutrition and Diet Therapy Branch. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '17e1b9d9b48bfe82aca194f55acc1c47ab874c13ad3d63742e45ac815fba3094', 50, 51, null, 474, null, null, false, null),
  ('3dbd69e3-d4d4-5cd9-a03d-0c90422f95a5', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Additional training', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-7d) and (2-7e).', '67b2a68b2bdcb02474d6543b42b5f0287683fe40c70ff8c9fd22a0a546f3e78f', 51, 51, null, 475, null, null, false, null),
  ('25efa6a0-0f29-562f-8594-d8b2a7aafe0c', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Broadening', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Drill Sergeant (DS), Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL), Joint positions, Operations (OPS) NCO, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), Master Resilience Trainer (MRT), Military Entrance Processing Command (MEPCOM) assignments, Recruiter', 'f3e7cf5fea4394386395c7a312b615d8a65b5b962133325edbb2672b431c3eb0', 51, 51, null, 476, null, null, false, null),
  ('05dcddf3-b3a5-5555-968f-f9d30e47be72', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '06ae5df573b7a7877d2fc624b0df05aee488df3f126b66fc4a92fe039e395aba', 51, 51, null, 477, null, null, false, null),
  ('3e5ac46d-4b0f-5a3d-ab07-1e7d3e050007', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5d).', '68f115b341150d1c80533c7f1884b5d6a86d439654185ed8d0bcf0a6c302802f', 51, 51, null, 478, null, null, false, null),
  ('17c49594-a43c-527b-bb7c-3e4f725357ed', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', '68M SSGs serve in field hospitals and augmentation unit H2F positions.', '2a75de8fcada5b59b70dae0a50312ba0002b22b52940af092a6c51dea90f84ef', 51, 51, null, 479, null, null, false, null),
  ('00facebf-030f-58e5-b0a4-17b00d3132f0', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, NCOs should concentrate on acquiring a degree, if not already completed. NCOs with an associate degree should consider pursuing a bachelor''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate "Most Qualified" for promotion. It is also recommended SSGs complete the EJPME I course, in addition to Army COOL - 68M - Certifications/Licenses and the previously listed certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '63378d820628d2e96567913afadcf18a3f058e9434dce0d2275b108e2cb47058', 51, 51, null, 480, null, null, false, null),
  ('24c3356b-d230-52fa-9791-8690a61eaaf5', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-8d) and (2-8e).', 'bd2e311136c5bf63eec37087dcb9e1a83b79717f0b4180344e223ed30cc96730', 51, 51, null, 481, null, null, false, null),
  ('dfe5a692-a485-5fff-8a9b-510165bcc543', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, DS, EOL, Instructor, Instructor/Writer, IG NCO, Joint positions, Observer Coach/Trainer (OC/T), OPS NCO, MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Pregnancy Postpartum Physical Training (P3T) Leader, Recruiter, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response & Prevention Coordinator (SARC), Section/Squad Leader (SL), SHARP Victim Advocate (VA), Small Group Leader (SGL), Soldier Recovery Unit (SRU) SL.', '32663ea20215ac9e457bb19608ce4001abebb339197e5a973c5808e08549f500', 51, 51, null, 482, null, null, false, null),
  ('3eb63c0c-f4d8-58ce-a9b5-5d996deaddf7', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'f55071b398a6906dfc3418f08533f9fd34ffbc29a25fff4cdf464ebdd54e4073', 51, 51, null, 483, null, null, false, null),
  ('414c3258-1d28-54ad-a088-c7c764b0571a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5e).', '2b54649d57c99709a0fb5f4d2e5ccbe3151cf7422840d5dbaf71eb3128378a24', 51, 51, null, 484, null, null, false, null),
  ('7682549b-4c48-5020-9a0a-81d4c6b70324', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'There are currently no 68M SFC TOE assignments.', '7a6768c228096e5c94c83c10def9d7c6038c16f6adf54e9baa489f15d708b67c', 51, 51, null, 485, null, null, false, null),
  ('2cea1e16-4e48-52d3-bb7f-9fa3da6b93e8', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Self-development', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'It is recommended SFC’ complete the EJPME II course in addition to information listed in paragraph (14-6c).', '75425484d3a21c454ca75dbfe81c87930f16d3341d080c200ea03937b61ede11', 52, 52, null, 486, null, null, false, null),
  ('b919b680-a92e-5209-965e-bc8f5fca419f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Additional training', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-9d) and (2-9e).', '4dbd76a5d851c56043a053d34a327f63c242cb1ec07c7995d93b9beafe72be21', 52, 52, null, 487, null, null, false, null),
  ('70dec59d-fe73-5d60-94dc-0ffb63e3a492', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Broadening', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, Detachment Sergeant, DS, EO Advisor (EOA), IG NCO, Instructor, Joint positions, OC/T, NCOIC positions, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, Platoon Sergeant (PSG), MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Senior DS, Senior DS Leader, Senior SGL, SRU PSG, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Training Developer.', '40ca9313ee737b26a75742433cf967826a0ad7292659f488e8c7ce4a497a5086', 52, 52, null, 488, null, null, false, null),
  ('64a3d28d-d997-525f-b35d-f5c23fa5a452', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'f55071b398a6906dfc3418f08533f9fd34ffbc29a25fff4cdf464ebdd54e4073', 52, 52, null, 489, null, null, false, null),
  ('b742d866-f12a-5555-9242-d62121bc2d63', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5f).', '5a880cfc962afbe4a9edb8761a29633f0c97bb69bdaaeddd9015aa4ae60027d4', 52, 52, null, 490, null, null, false, null),
  ('31190aa2-ffd4-5f66-9154-4afca03330df', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'There are currently 68M MSG TOE assignments. However, it is important to note the single most demanding assignment at this level is 1SG and all MSGs are encouraged to compete for assignment selection.', 'caa550a3969dba6a30fa2abc59722f65931764f00b952a568b5839af22516f66', 52, 52, null, 491, null, null, false, null),
  ('2af4ae0d-bc48-50aa-8096-cd9d4d63c42c', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, it is strongly recommended NCOs at this rank pursue the completion of a degree. Sr NCOs should prioritize obtaining a degree if they have not already done so. Those with a bachelor’s degree should consider pursuing a master''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate “Most Qualified" for promotion. Additionally, Sr NCOs should complete the EJPME II course, the Army COOL - Project Management Professional (PMP) certification, and applicable Army COOL - Professional Certifications/Licenses. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'a73ced532ccb21388881c39cb6ef39bad6be6e8726e18cbb4ef39481f72a6471', 52, 52, null, 492, null, null, false, null),
  ('ed2e30b4-8ab7-5939-bde2-c2f6b67ebfec', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-10d) and (2-10e).', '9db3f3182d8a122ebd769d9b5092b1cd5cf6c74498a5d5e44da8a8ac3acb6074', 52, 52, null, 493, null, null, false, null),
  ('ccdde8b6-555d-5e5e-bdc1-88d730ccdf90', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, EOA, IG NCO, Chief Instructor, 1SG, MFT, MRT, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Sr Career Management NCO, Training Developer.', '329467ea7ca2cc508d5d3bd7138664113e80dc3d5e23db20366cd6a600883303', 52, 52, null, 494, null, null, false, null),
  ('43259aa2-8eb2-5943-82f3-de192e3de83a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68M', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 14. 68M – Nutrition Care Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'f55071b398a6906dfc3418f08533f9fd34ffbc29a25fff4cdf464ebdd54e4073', 52, 52, null, 495, null, null, false, null),
  ('8ac7b3d1-facd-5c5d-93be-4f0c92d2e3b5', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'The Radiology Specialist operates fixed and portable radiology equipment or supervises radiology activities. 15–1. Position Titles with MOS, SQI and ASI Codes 68P titles include - 68P1O Radiology Spec; 68P1P Radiology Spec; 68P2O Radiology SGT; 68P2P Radiology SGT; 68P3O Radiology NCO; 68P3OY9 Squad Leader; 68P34 Recruiter; 68P38 Instructor; 68P38 Instructor/Writer; 68P4O Sr Radiology NCO; 68P4O Detachment Sergeant; 68P42 Sr Training Developer; 68P48 Instructor; 68P48 Instructor/Writer; 68P5O Ch Radiology NCO; 68P58 Chief Instructor; 68P5M First Sergeant.', 'b8ac241e592f2e4417f3487ed7a54e4e78ea7d6009385c5ffec7613a427571ab', 53, 53, null, 496, null, null, false, null),
  ('9a472b67-1988-535f-a1cd-f1c91d9c72a4', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'A combination of assignments in both Table of Organization and Equipment (TOE) OF units and Table of Distribution and Allowances (TDA) GF units provide the ideal promotion foundation for normal career progression. TOE assignments provide the basis for training and competence in common tasks, tactical expertise, essential medical support, repair tasks, and leadership. TDA assignments provide more in-depth and specialized training. Although successive assignments and extended TOE or TDA assignment periods are not recommended; it is important to note that limited TOE positions may result in lengthier durations within the TDA. Soldiers should concentrate on developing their medical support technical and leadership skills in these assignments. Advancement recommendations are determined on mastering these skills and displaying the aptitude and attitude consistent with the "whole Soldier" concept.', 'd624cab794ee10e2a0c71cb5327787ab3c7117ac1500645987d1b5520fd08e08', 53, 53, null, 497, null, null, false, null),
  ('49cfceb0-2d7b-5947-b67c-a7905b059648', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'This AIT MOS is a two-phased course; the combined course length is 44- weeks, 2-days. Phase I training is 24-weeks, 2-days and conducted at the JBSA-FSH, METC followed by a phase II 22-week training conducted at a designated MTF, succeeded by an assignment in the newly established specialized skill set. Phase I of the radiography training program provides a comprehensive education on radiographic principles, including radiographic procedures, radiation protection, imaging equipment and techniques, and quality assurance. Foundational topics included are radiation biology, radiation physics, medical terminology, concepts of patient care, radiographic pathology, along with medical ethics and law. This phase also includes laboratory exercises to test theories and concepts, with a focus on developing manual skills prior to clinical application. In phase II, students will receive on-the-job training in the clinical environment performing procedures and exams on actual patients under the guidance of qualified radiographers and radiologists. Emphasis is to acquire competency in performing procedures/exams on actual ill or injured patients. See Ch. 2 (2-5b) for PME requirements.', 'd6b1772778f8f29fd278b957f17eba41b111009971c8f1007dc7250cfc76a5a1', 53, 53, null, 498, null, null, false, null),
  ('a0cec60b-0aa8-5f43-9b6b-e9feebcc68e6', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', '68Ps serve in MED COs, MED DETs, SPT SQDNs, BSBs, and field hospitals.', 'edb2d2a8308b7d48fd0ab376c3cece7b251f62cfe9f1e35db2ccbe947e31d124', 53, 53, null, 499, null, null, false, null),
  ('50011001-4f9d-548e-993b-7a0693f18c70', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Self-development', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Soldiers should begin formulating plans with long-term objectives, concentrating on their military skills while considering civilian education and degree-producing programs. It is also recommended Soldiers complete Army COOL - 68P - Certifications/Licenses, the American Registry of Radiologic Technologists (ARRT): Computed Tomography (CT), Magnetic Resonance Imaging (MRI), Radiography (R), Sonography (S). See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'b6c3164ebf639a1b872fcd2452bf4f57f60d91ea531bb509e2981c7fbe856704', 53, 54, null, 500, null, null, false, null),
  ('b11126f9-8165-5a9f-8c6d-d407980f254b', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Additional training', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-6d) and (2-6e).', '7cd54815f52e7795535c2a2a0616c1429545fbc98e4940523dc32948c6d14ac9', 54, 54, null, 501, null, null, false, null),
  ('9c13c6f0-0c5c-5fcb-98be-aab3ac84cef9', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities Soldiers should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '2c2544455441782fe90358d790aeb5eb6bc6362a3ea50572cb9512ecdbdda650', 54, 54, null, 502, null, null, false, null),
  ('b7a3b070-bc1d-5ab3-ad3d-303c2847b8ff', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5c).', 'bda5558b772a2f3f63e3177b5b82498729937cfeddb1fc72b3a6f0859e6b0499', 54, 54, null, 503, null, null, false, null),
  ('ad2b70ea-17cf-5766-82f4-0bdd0f6b4ff8', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', '68P SGTs serve in MED COs, SPT COs, SPT SQDNs, BSBs, and field hospitals.', '6643d7efdd3ddeec138ff1c62a1af2d1c9dcd991b45db20db751ef79f35b034d', 54, 54, null, 504, null, null, false, null),
  ('c93198a6-08a5-5d32-b18a-194af1a0180a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Self-development', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Although not mandatory SGTs should develop a plan to acquire a degree. It is also recommended SGTs complete the Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (EJPME) I course in addition to Army COOL - 68P - Certifications/Licenses and the previously listed certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'dd5a8e00565c0332dadcf6cda057b3308457738731d565b723edecbf0b46feda', 54, 54, null, 505, null, null, false, null),
  ('514dea49-fa91-55de-bd1d-8c1dffdfe06d', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Additional training', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-7d) and (2-7e).', '67b2a68b2bdcb02474d6543b42b5f0287683fe40c70ff8c9fd22a0a546f3e78f', 54, 54, null, 506, null, null, false, null),
  ('2308069c-2bfb-5580-a084-b4681ba1db43', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Broadening', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Drill Sergeant (DS), Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL), Joint positions, Operations (OPS) NCO, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), Master Resilience Trainer (MRT), Military Entrance Processing Command (MEPCOM) assignments, Recruiter.', 'dd026957cc32756f121fd4f3c41f417898ca6f50ac6adb0a52a58dfd72c15b0e', 54, 54, null, 507, null, null, false, null),
  ('134ced5a-ab64-5ce5-8af3-bd63612b65f2', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, World Class Athlete Program (WCAP) and Special Missions Unit (SMU). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO', '0c97d933033fce38d13dfbd3356eda515be064280cc5a986d80c15497d31845a', 54, 54, null, 508, null, null, false, null),
  ('60b03139-4a16-5944-98f6-4d391be3cce0', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5d).', '68f115b341150d1c80533c7f1884b5d6a86d439654185ed8d0bcf0a6c302802f', 54, 54, null, 509, null, null, false, null),
  ('399c6b4c-540c-5457-96c8-4b6c93cadc0d', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'There are currently no 68P SSG TOE assignments.', '45773777a5b4632d4947cad89f4f7fe29b7b166ee8d26d617cf77090d80dc301', 54, 54, null, 510, null, null, false, null),
  ('908357ba-55be-5d3d-a44f-2173174f6db0', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, NCOs should concentrate on acquiring a degree, if not already completed. NCOs with an associate degree should consider pursuing a bachelor''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate "Most Qualified" for promotion. It is also recommended SSGs complete the EJPME I course, in addition to Army COOL - 68P - Certifications/Licenses and the previously listed certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'e81409e7c6d705802466fba27a734b1c21b672571392f2ab099643e125874872', 54, 54, null, 511, null, null, false, null),
  ('5e3919f8-7b34-5dd5-97ae-c8d0f3f0186f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-8d) and (2-8e).', 'bd2e311136c5bf63eec37087dcb9e1a83b79717f0b4180344e223ed30cc96730', 54, 54, null, 512, null, null, false, null),
  ('57ace996-903d-51fc-9036-b021b361b136', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, DS, EOL, Instructor, Instructor/Writer, IG NCO, Joint positions, Observer Coach/Trainer (OC/T), OPS NCO, MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Pregnancy Postpartum Physical Training (P3T) Leader, Recruiter, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response & Prevention Coordinator (SARC), Section/Squad Leader (SL), SHARP Victim Advocate (VA), Small Group Leader (SGL), Soldier Recovery Unit (SRU) SL.', '32663ea20215ac9e457bb19608ce4001abebb339197e5a973c5808e08549f500', 54, 55, null, 513, null, null, false, null),
  ('ca9cd538-1bca-53fb-97de-4a9e33479d1c', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, Special Missions Unit (SMU) and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', '7bc6cf4654882018316bb81369634e6d252933cfb0f1f982d970525ffd575897', 55, 55, null, 514, null, null, false, null),
  ('509abadb-55c4-5ad1-a245-880f3f84dc0a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5e).', '2b54649d57c99709a0fb5f4d2e5ccbe3151cf7422840d5dbaf71eb3128378a24', 55, 55, null, 515, null, null, false, null),
  ('e8f564b7-3a5e-5389-9a51-46d4d847d913', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', '68P SFC’ serve in field hospitals.', 'ef6ea9f09fc8b1e846c42ba8e838c9aadaad2292dff41f5d80480cfe2ab54dad', 55, 55, null, 516, null, null, false, null),
  ('46e3a27f-4c76-590c-8961-23c49fa53fc1', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Self-development', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'It is recommended SFC’ complete the EJPME II course in addition to information listed in paragraph (15-6c).', '8d03371d78f05eca08e3365c1a5c64f9ee49cadafc7e64c701ee6379629d3632', 55, 55, null, 517, null, null, false, null),
  ('ae5f0fec-6eb5-51a4-925c-87986598b3e9', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Additional training', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-9d) and (2-9e).', '4dbd76a5d851c56043a053d34a327f63c242cb1ec07c7995d93b9beafe72be21', 55, 55, null, 518, null, null, false, null),
  ('898525b7-b51f-58d6-94ec-53669766849f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Broadening', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, Detachment Sergeant, DS, EO Advisor (EOA), IG NCO, Instructor, Joint positions, OC/T, NCOIC positions, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, Platoon Sergeant (PSG), MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Senior DS, Senior DS Leader, Senior SGL, SRU PSG, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Training Developer.', '40ca9313ee737b26a75742433cf967826a0ad7292659f488e8c7ce4a497a5086', 55, 55, null, 519, null, null, false, null),
  ('18230fc5-cc92-54c4-8ccd-bb364f6ddcd7', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, Special Missions Unit (SMU) and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', '7bc6cf4654882018316bb81369634e6d252933cfb0f1f982d970525ffd575897', 55, 55, null, 520, null, null, false, null),
  ('1687040c-9a25-56e2-83f7-9dae0198603a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5f).', '5a880cfc962afbe4a9edb8761a29633f0c97bb69bdaaeddd9015aa4ae60027d4', 55, 55, null, 521, null, null, false, null),
  ('bab88fff-c580-566d-9c50-35723dd6843f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'There are currently no 68P MSG TOE assignments. However, it is important to note the single most demanding assignment at this level is 1SG and all MSGs are encouraged to compete for assignment selection.', '401d9d76e0b28c63d8c96e4b88a0752dbb36bf1dffe974b8bf0bd4acf6b4255f', 55, 55, null, 522, null, null, false, null),
  ('923942f5-ffc5-5a83-ad24-5f2e355bc0c0', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, it is strongly recommended NCOs at this rank pursue the completion of a degree. Sr NCOs should prioritize obtaining a degree if they have not already done so. Those with a bachelor’s degree should consider pursuing a master''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate “Most Qualified" for promotion. Additionally, Sr NCOs should complete the EJPME II course, the Army COOL - Project Management Professional (PMP) certification, and applicable Army COOL - Manager - Certifications/Licenses. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '687d16b4ca458cfd76f61de3f65a8e1822232c74caf2722d954f87189dd618ed', 55, 55, null, 523, null, null, false, null),
  ('00271280-a373-5713-827a-dade62f73d96', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-10d) and (2-10e).', '9db3f3182d8a122ebd769d9b5092b1cd5cf6c74498a5d5e44da8a8ac3acb6074', 55, 55, null, 524, null, null, false, null),
  ('7e6bae6d-eb54-52bf-a25b-133f0f80312e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, EOA, IG NCO, Chief Instructor, 1SG, MFT, MRT, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Sr Career Management NCO, Training Developer.', '329467ea7ca2cc508d5d3bd7138664113e80dc3d5e23db20366cd6a600883303', 56, 56, null, 525, null, null, false, null),
  ('024b8cd1-63c2-564e-8af6-a25ff7f710d6', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68P', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 15. 68P – Radiology Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'f55071b398a6906dfc3418f08533f9fd34ffbc29a25fff4cdf464ebdd54e4073', 56, 56, null, 526, null, null, false, null),
  ('cc0f7249-b79b-5a8c-a52c-3045e8b76eb4', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'The Pharmacy Specialist screens, prepares, controls, and issues pharmaceuticals products under the supervision of a pharmacist or physician, and supervises pharmacy activities. 16–1. Position Titles with MOS, SQI and ASI Codes 68Q titles include - 68Q1O Pharmacy Spec; 68Q2O Pharmacy SGT; 68Q2P Pharmacy SGT; 68Q3O Pharmacy NCO; 68Q3O MTTF Pharmacy OC/T; 68Q34 Recruiter; 68Q34L Recruiter; 68Q38 Instructor; 68Q38P Sr Instructor/Writer; 68Q4O Pharmacy NCO; 68Q42 Sr Training Developer; 68Q48 SGL; 68Q48 Instructor; 68Q5O Sr Pharmacy NCO; 68Q58 Chief Instructor; 68Q5M First Sergeant.', '8270bcd5d415dcfc525c01487f67dbec20abe65c55808db219f8f85526fc512a', 56, 56, null, 527, null, null, false, null),
  ('518a3a32-bfbc-5bdb-95db-b7b5a73ed905', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'A combination of assignments in both Table of Organization and Equipment (TOE) OF units and Table of Distribution and Allowances (TDA) GF units provide the ideal promotion foundation for normal career progression. TOE assignments provide the basis for training and competence in common tasks, tactical expertise, essential medical support, repair tasks, and leadership. TDA assignments provide more in-depth and specialized training. Although successive assignments and extended TOE or TDA assignment periods are not recommended; it is important to note that limited TOE positions may result in lengthier durations within the TDA. Soldiers should concentrate on developing their medical support technical and leadership skills in these assignments. Advancement recommendations are determined on mastering these skills and displaying the aptitude and attitude consistent with the "whole Soldier" concept.', 'd624cab794ee10e2a0c71cb5327787ab3c7117ac1500645987d1b5520fd08e08', 56, 56, null, 528, null, null, false, null),
  ('f48b982e-9f14-535a-b3c5-46436dded7dc', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'The 22-week, 1-day MOS AIT is conducted at the JBSA-FSH, METC followed by an assignment in the newly established specialized skill set. which is followed by an assignment in the newly established specialized skill set. Entry-level pharmacy technician training includes topics related to drugs, their sources, preparation, uses, incompatibilities, and doses; pharmaceutical symbols and terms; drug storage and control procedures; dispensing procedures, and the interpretation of sterile product orders; use of necessary equipment, supplies, and references. The curriculum also explores pharmacy administration, pharmaceutical calculations, chemistry, therapeutics, pharmacology, the characteristics and design of an aseptic work environment, hospital pharmacy practices, and quality control principles and procedures. Students will also receive introductory and reinforcement defense training in Chemical, Biological, Radiological, Nuclear, and Explosives (CBRNE), equipping them to respond to terrorist threats or attacks. Students are supervised by a pharmacy officer or medical corps officer throughout training to ensure they gain the knowledge and skills required to succeed as a pharmacy technician. See Ch. 2 (2-5b) for PME requirements.', 'aa9fc673aa63777cb313c1bb75a466b9cb27e73bd68772cc6554009d7509ea36', 56, 57, null, 529, null, null, false, null),
  ('3066c95b-128e-580d-bc99-0becdf296dfc', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', '68Qs serve in MED COs and field hospitals.', 'cd66a1617cd89c64a8da379ea007cf67df6f899f6097dbd2981e78c38e1a6446', 57, 57, null, 530, null, null, false, null),
  ('f72a8a7f-5647-55a4-a1c3-6b8b10b43f0e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Self-development', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Soldiers should begin formulating plans with long-term objectives, concentrating on their military skills while considering civilian education and degree-producing programs. It is also recommended Soldiers complete Army COOL - 68Q - Certifications/Licenses. At a minimum, the Pharmacy Technician Certification Board (PTCB) Certified Pharmacy Technician (CPhT). See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '626a2358c290c8f1d50cdb3d80481151e3e422b5e4b55105a5cb8bebc1852589', 57, 57, null, 531, null, null, false, null),
  ('7b19909e-1ff7-54f2-87bc-07a6384fcfa0', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-6d) and (2-6e).', '7cd54815f52e7795535c2a2a0616c1429545fbc98e4940523dc32948c6d14ac9', 57, 57, null, 532, null, null, false, null),
  ('110af091-ab81-5034-9f69-ea4477e53869', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities Soldiers should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '2c2544455441782fe90358d790aeb5eb6bc6362a3ea50572cb9512ecdbdda650', 57, 57, null, 533, null, null, false, null),
  ('ee22bab3-66b0-5ad6-8da1-46dac0d3b229', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5c).', 'bda5558b772a2f3f63e3177b5b82498729937cfeddb1fc72b3a6f0859e6b0499', 57, 57, null, 534, null, null, false, null),
  ('e0c5f88d-f2c2-5ad0-ac2e-6e32c76ccf85', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', '68Qs serve in SPT SQDNs, BSBs and field hospitals.', 'efa769bf766e7ff66fbd245e64c54f21ee75eecb0f02f05abc7d7e6d3367e545', 57, 57, null, 535, null, null, false, null),
  ('87298b7f-528a-5bea-8ac4-af2eeed3bfc4', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Self-development', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Although not mandatory SGTs should develop a plan to acquire a degree. It is also recommended SGTs complete the Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (EJPME) I course in addition to Army COOL - 68Q - Certifications/Licenses and the previously listed certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'd6613236354247f2cb17a9a28db880cb9630a5514017f258f28921d14d956871', 57, 57, null, 536, null, null, false, null),
  ('743a9e20-3065-5663-8137-81a2ba0b1ce3', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-7d) and (2-7e).', '67b2a68b2bdcb02474d6543b42b5f0287683fe40c70ff8c9fd22a0a546f3e78f', 57, 57, null, 537, null, null, false, null),
  ('c1808dee-3ae1-544c-bbbc-7cd59bd04f0b', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Broadening', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Drill Sergeant (DS), Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL), Joint positions, Operations (OPS) NCO, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), Master Resilience Trainer (MRT), Military Entrance Processing Command (MEPCOM) assignments, Recruiter.', 'dd026957cc32756f121fd4f3c41f417898ca6f50ac6adb0a52a58dfd72c15b0e', 57, 57, null, 538, null, null, false, null),
  ('7e789896-58fa-5515-ab58-376e8411386e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '06ae5df573b7a7877d2fc624b0df05aee488df3f126b66fc4a92fe039e395aba', 57, 57, null, 539, null, null, false, null),
  ('dcf198bf-5c7a-5b03-ab70-da618b20dfeb', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5d).', '68f115b341150d1c80533c7f1884b5d6a86d439654185ed8d0bcf0a6c302802f', 57, 57, null, 540, null, null, false, null),
  ('ea18526b-8891-523a-ba73-119cc49d921f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', '68Q SSGs serve in field hospitals.', 'd35812a54d47a10034f4f6d3879c5c293c1aade577494bd6b7ab3caf291865f3', 57, 57, null, 541, null, null, false, null),
  ('6c2d818a-eb15-536c-b6aa-a66dccfabe91', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, NCOs should concentrate on acquiring a degree, if not already completed. NCOs with an associate degree should consider pursuing a bachelor''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate "Most Qualified" for promotion. It is also recommended SSGs complete the EJPME I course, in addition to Army COOL - 68Q - Certifications/Licenses and the previously listed certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'e79e26f263eba22cfbce35d399b2ee642fe0bf298cb58d462f35488d43fed11d', 58, 58, null, 542, null, null, false, null),
  ('adac989a-acca-5e48-85fa-02c003c24372', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-8d) and (2-8e).', 'bd2e311136c5bf63eec37087dcb9e1a83b79717f0b4180344e223ed30cc96730', 58, 58, null, 543, null, null, false, null),
  ('e0641cd8-a63a-5bfe-8d1f-f59c8938877b', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, DS, EOL, Instructor, Instructor/Writer, IG NCO, Joint positions, Observer Coach/Trainer (OC/T), OPS NCO, MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Pregnancy Postpartum Physical Training (P3T) Leader, Recruiter, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response & Prevention Coordinator (SARC), Section/Squad Leader (SL), SHARP Victim Advocate (VA), Small Group Leader (SGL), Soldier Recovery Unit (SRU) SL.', '32663ea20215ac9e457bb19608ce4001abebb339197e5a973c5808e08549f500', 58, 58, null, 544, null, null, false, null),
  ('bed59fb7-dda1-51fb-ba02-6a84fc146fbe', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'f55071b398a6906dfc3418f08533f9fd34ffbc29a25fff4cdf464ebdd54e4073', 58, 58, null, 545, null, null, false, null),
  ('c643a546-b45d-522a-8d76-a6a00d93937d', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5e).', '2b54649d57c99709a0fb5f4d2e5ccbe3151cf7422840d5dbaf71eb3128378a24', 58, 58, null, 546, null, null, false, null),
  ('9ab7a3dc-f917-5097-8b6b-be6d20b15a27', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', '68Q SFC’ in MED BNs and field hospitals.', '3bc52e5455853d8dcfc1bff95c3c845eb540424aad5c9ada1a56ee4242fd8264', 58, 58, null, 547, null, null, false, null),
  ('2654f65f-95a7-53d8-bf76-b3e4577e67d9', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Self-development', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'It is recommended SFC’ complete the EJPME II course in addition to information listed in paragraph (16-6c).', '95a79d42f09f81819fc36a4f37342f66188e00c125246e4768a00b6cadb42c6e', 58, 58, null, 548, null, null, false, null),
  ('3311673d-4622-5887-bec5-d79d6c618569', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-9d) and (2-9e).', '4dbd76a5d851c56043a053d34a327f63c242cb1ec07c7995d93b9beafe72be21', 58, 58, null, 549, null, null, false, null),
  ('959ddc96-721c-57f2-88bc-2ea5362fad21', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Broadening', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, Detachment Sergeant, DS, EO Advisor (EOA), IG NCO, Instructor, Joint positions, OC/T, NCOIC positions, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, Platoon Sergeant (PSG), MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Senior DS, Senior DS Leader, Senior SGL, SRU PSG, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Training Developer.', '40ca9313ee737b26a75742433cf967826a0ad7292659f488e8c7ce4a497a5086', 58, 58, null, 550, null, null, false, null),
  ('d2b23415-b41c-5d2f-a70e-ab69de8d9494', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'f55071b398a6906dfc3418f08533f9fd34ffbc29a25fff4cdf464ebdd54e4073', 58, 58, null, 551, null, null, false, null),
  ('93edd49e-adb2-5171-89fb-1d1f16ab0136', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5f).', '5a880cfc962afbe4a9edb8761a29633f0c97bb69bdaaeddd9015aa4ae60027d4', 58, 58, null, 552, null, null, false, null),
  ('50deffc7-a3de-550a-8a6c-09b3d0ff2998', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', '68Q MSGs serve in MEDCOMs. It is important to note the single most demanding assignment at this level is 1SG and all MSGs are encouraged to compete for assignment selection.', '0442f32623660fcca1b098e377ebdff70d7f08d9839a82dd84525f9e6ee4ab8f', 59, 59, null, 553, null, null, false, null),
  ('52323d5b-0023-533f-aa6f-51679aad6f83', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, it is strongly recommended NCOs at this rank pursue the completion of a degree. Sr NCOs should prioritize obtaining a degree if they have not already done so. Those with a bachelor’s degree should consider pursuing a master''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate “Most Qualified" for promotion. Additionally, Sr NCOs should complete the EJPME II course, the Army COOL - Project Management Professional (PMP) certification, and applicable Army COOL - Manager - Certifications/Licenses. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '687d16b4ca458cfd76f61de3f65a8e1822232c74caf2722d954f87189dd618ed', 59, 59, null, 554, null, null, false, null),
  ('77046fc7-b97d-58b9-812b-43c5ea1c0bb2', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-10d) and (2-10e).', '9db3f3182d8a122ebd769d9b5092b1cd5cf6c74498a5d5e44da8a8ac3acb6074', 59, 59, null, 555, null, null, false, null),
  ('d91d7088-91c8-5ddd-a4d5-4844a91d0c07', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, EOA, IG NCO, Chief Instructor, 1SG, MFT, MRT, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Sr Career Management NCO, Training Developer.', '329467ea7ca2cc508d5d3bd7138664113e80dc3d5e23db20366cd6a600883303', 59, 59, null, 556, null, null, false, null),
  ('2c03cd0f-fbf1-5892-88e2-2e06683672a3', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Q', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 16. 68Q – Pharmacy Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'f55071b398a6906dfc3418f08533f9fd34ffbc29a25fff4cdf464ebdd54e4073', 59, 59, null, 557, null, null, false, null),
  ('3ff33268-8cc5-5362-a11f-a3d3435b7765', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'The Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist inspects or supervises the inspection of meat, poultry, water foods, eggs, dairy products, operational rations, fresh fruits and vegetables in depots, supply points, and on military installations to assure a safe, high quality food supply for DOD personnel in all environments with emphasis on the field wartime environment. 17–1. Position Titles with MOS, SQI and ASI Codes 68R titles include - 68R1O Food Inspector. 68R2O Food Inspection SGT; 68R3O Food Inspection NCO; 68R34 Recruiter; 68R34 VR Recruiter; 68R34L Recruiter; 68R38 Instructor/Writer; 68R38 Instructor; 68R3P Food Inspection NCO; 68R3X Drill Sergeant; 68R4O Detachment Sergeant; 68R4O Food Insp NCO; 68R4O Platoon Sergeant; 68R4O Sr Food Insp NCO; 68R4O Vet Svc NCO; 68R4O1H Victim Advocate; 68R4O2S Sr Food Insp NCO; 68R42 Sr Training Dev/Writer; 68R48 Instructor; 68R48 Instructor/Writer; 68R5O Ch Veterinary NCO; 68R5O Sr Veterinary NCO; 68R5O Veterinary Service NCO; 68R5O2S Sr Veterinary NCO; 68R58 Chief Instructor; 68R5M First Sergeant.', '66406c833aeb3cc709767a8e94d0e611c51a2c7f76abfd0eb60f988c807e5533', 59, 59, null, 558, null, null, false, null),
  ('400078a9-9ae2-5f7f-b213-375da65d58d7', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'A combination of assignments in both Table of Organization and Equipment (TOE) OF units and Table of Distribution and Allowances (TDA) GF units provide the ideal promotion foundation for normal career progression. TOE assignments provide the basis for training and competence in common tasks, tactical expertise, essential medical support, repair tasks, and leadership. TDA assignments provide more in-depth and specialized training. Although successive assignments and extended TOE or TDA assignment periods are not recommended; it is important to note that limited TOE positions may result in lengthier durations within the TDA. Soldiers should concentrate on developing their medical support technical and leadership skills in these assignments. Advancement recommendations are determined on mastering these skills and displaying the aptitude and attitude consistent with the "whole Soldier" concept.', 'd624cab794ee10e2a0c71cb5327787ab3c7117ac1500645987d1b5520fd08e08', 60, 60, null, 559, null, null, false, null),
  ('25629f49-c67f-5b5b-ad6f-9e28955d4303', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'The 8-week MOS AIT is conducted at the JBSA-FSH, METC followed by an assignment in the newly established specialized skill set. This training program emphasizes the competencies required to perform food inspection responsibilities effectively and equips students with a working knowledge of techniques used to determine identity, condition, and quantity in various food groups, such as red meats (including pork), water-foods, poultry, eggs, dairy products, semi- perishables, fresh fruits, and vegetables. Included subjects covered are, animal medicine and selected military subjects, sampling procedures, forms, contract administration, basic food inspection procedures (including sensory evaluation), basic food establishment sanitation, food safety and quality assurance, surveillance inspection, and veterinary preventive medicine. See Ch. 2 (2-5b) for PME requirements.', '7796a36ad4b87290b4cc0c94644c2e5630a9328b8b8e9db7a48850c3bcded52b', 60, 60, null, 560, null, null, false, null),
  ('f794bef0-91a5-5253-ad99-44e8b022d58b', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', '68Rs serve in MED DET veterinary service support positions and in MED BN preventive medicine sections.', 'eb7d53318465a715530c9c22aa8955e45db5a55da37cc8c645b694612899ad04', 60, 60, null, 561, null, null, false, null),
  ('9714881e-6969-5314-a798-d961312afcc8', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Self-development', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Soldiers should begin formulating plans with long-term objectives, concentrating on their military skills while considering civilian education and degree-producing programs. It is also recommended Soldiers complete Army COOL - 68R - Certifications/Licenses, at a minimum, the serv safe manager certification, Certified in Comprehensive Food Safety (CCFS), and the Food Safety and Quality Auditor Certification (CFSQA). The following courses should also be considered: the advanced food technology course (SPC & SGT only), installation food vulnerability assessment course (SPC/P - SFC only), installation veterinary services course (SPC & above), and surveillance food laboratory course. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, cool certifications, DL, and army e-learning courses.', '6384faf829ad3ac2c0583634a9f3de87f5b3a94ee8c1cf3b008090de6caa3b24', 60, 60, null, 562, null, null, false, null),
  ('2b47d456-c8a4-5371-bd2a-1070603533f4', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Additional training', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-6d) and (2-6e).', '7cd54815f52e7795535c2a2a0616c1429545fbc98e4940523dc32948c6d14ac9', 60, 60, null, 563, null, null, false, null),
  ('f12b31dd-ee1e-5c46-944d-5016f263c7ea', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities Soldiers should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '2c2544455441782fe90358d790aeb5eb6bc6362a3ea50572cb9512ecdbdda650', 60, 60, null, 564, null, null, false, null),
  ('94072b18-874f-5346-b5c1-5e8375c295e2', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5c).', 'bda5558b772a2f3f63e3177b5b82498729937cfeddb1fc72b3a6f0859e6b0499', 60, 60, null, 565, null, null, false, null),
  ('c06954e3-8908-50c3-920e-f4d496f4368d', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', '68R SGTs serve in MED DET food procurement and laboratory teams (FPLT) and veterinary service support teams, and in MED LAB occupational and environmental health sections.', '2eb74b4c4b74056d9d117ca7b84f733a28d95b8fd9836ab8997aa63f4d964866', 60, 60, null, 566, null, null, false, null),
  ('d0e515c0-19d1-5871-8186-eade8917c5a1', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Self-development', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Although not mandatory SGTs should develop a plan to acquire a degree. It is also recommended SGTs complete the Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (EJPME) I course in addition to Army COOL - 68R - Certifications/Licenses, at a minimum, the servsafe manager certification. The following courses should also be considered if not yet completed: the advanced food technology course (SPC and SGT only), installation food vulnerability assessment course (SPC/P - SFC only), installation veterinary services course (SPC and above), and surveillance food laboratory course. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e- Learning courses.', 'e72c492a15263e36205afe50447a8e041273ec2c58e05635f3e2a812a7ec64a3', 61, 61, null, 567, null, null, false, null),
  ('c44c99fd-ba80-5a83-9a6a-b39e654086e1', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Additional training', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-7d) and (2-7e).', '67b2a68b2bdcb02474d6543b42b5f0287683fe40c70ff8c9fd22a0a546f3e78f', 61, 61, null, 568, null, null, false, null),
  ('2864dd79-54ec-5d93-badf-d15ea1fbc13d', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Broadening', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Drill Sergeant (DS), Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL), Joint positions, Operations (OPS) NCO, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), Master Resilience Trainer (MRT), Military Entrance Processing Command (MEPCOM) assignments, Recruiter.', 'dd026957cc32756f121fd4f3c41f417898ca6f50ac6adb0a52a58dfd72c15b0e', 61, 61, null, 569, null, null, false, null),
  ('2e1e192b-5df2-5d5f-b008-f06d09a41b1d', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, World Class Athlete Program (WCAP) and Special Missions Unit (SMU). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD- EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '3a72b042c88f7abed06e643628fc712e54c53cc60cae0795d271bd7a1bc83c41', 61, 61, null, 570, null, null, false, null),
  ('48ab69b4-957c-5825-8008-c2ceb3ce9953', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5d).', '68f115b341150d1c80533c7f1884b5d6a86d439654185ed8d0bcf0a6c302802f', 61, 61, null, 571, null, null, false, null),
  ('db00dd9a-8c77-5d34-9c22-8b25ff9da638', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', '68R SSGs serve in MED DET FPLTs and veterinary service support teams, and in SBDEs, BDE surgeon section positions.', '38c53ee69c1fe0b10a8ed9c33896d0feac1ee31ff2469bd81f24b9ec568eb676', 61, 61, null, 572, null, null, false, null),
  ('85328fd7-abdf-5867-af50-191643ae4ea2', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, NCOs should concentrate on acquiring a degree, if not already completed. NCOs with an associate degree should consider pursuing a bachelor''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate “Most Qualified" for promotion. It is recommended If not yet completed, SSGs complete the EJPME I course in addition to Army COOL - 68R - Certifications/Licenses. The following courses should also be considered if not yet completed: the installation food vulnerability assessment course (SPC/P - SFC only), installation veterinary services course (SPC and above), and surveillance food laboratory course. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '1f0a637a252131b4de96480273f7a6fc5232661bbf5e2d8e4f623a9e345f7ba5', 61, 61, null, 573, null, null, false, null),
  ('b177c37f-ec26-5609-b15a-e374809495b9', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-8d) and (2-8e). Certified Quality Auditor; HACCP Auditor; Certified Quality Inspector from American Society for Quality.', '9d165ba28bc40bd142a704fbd3eb3353b21171d4f91abd801cf3d212e0905636', 61, 61, null, 574, null, null, false, null),
  ('80eca3ff-83fb-593a-9117-15d89ccf6e99', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, DS, EOL, Instructor, Instructor/Writer, IG NCO, Joint positions, Observer Coach/Trainer (OC/T), OPS NCO, MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Pregnancy Postpartum Physical Training (P3T) Leader, Recruiter, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response & Prevention Coordinator (SARC), Section/Squad Leader (SL), SHARP Victim Advocate (VA), Small Group Leader (SGL), Soldier Recovery Unit (SRU) SL).', '56f2bc5aa60ebe79b09afdb1b5a185dc9e9d22a1c7a62d02c089b1c8a446d4d2', 61, 61, null, 575, null, null, false, null),
  ('5e1b222f-a5be-564f-a340-4fe1e729912e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, Special Missions Unit (SMU) and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', '7bc6cf4654882018316bb81369634e6d252933cfb0f1f982d970525ffd575897', 61, 61, null, 576, null, null, false, null),
  ('6e264a32-f800-50f8-8780-7fe13762b7e4', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5e).', '2b54649d57c99709a0fb5f4d2e5ccbe3151cf7422840d5dbaf71eb3128378a24', 62, 62, null, 577, null, null, false, null),
  ('252d121b-5e1e-5118-9d54-8d6bbda9f3c5', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', '68R SFC’ serve in MED BN preventive medicine sections.', '555259b1c7961c9ffcdc17cfead920b5d5f67ee68a4c753068a81876cb106c79', 62, 62, null, 578, null, null, false, null),
  ('553e9fcb-f83b-55dc-9c93-2286e3185885', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Self-development', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'It is recommended SFC’ complete the EJPME II course in addition to information listed in paragraph (17-6c).', 'c2d95f4747f436487f378ed4729d0e1a548cc11de5c7e10f44c93fd5a7ceae42', 62, 62, null, 579, null, null, false, null),
  ('930dfab6-39f6-5066-bff0-91aee7b2855b', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Additional training', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-9d) and (2-9e).', '4dbd76a5d851c56043a053d34a327f63c242cb1ec07c7995d93b9beafe72be21', 62, 62, null, 580, null, null, false, null),
  ('9e9f3d0a-2243-562e-883a-10abe1a15514', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Broadening', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, Detachment Sergeant, DS, EO Advisor (EOA), IG NCO, Instructor, Joint positions, OC/T, NCOIC positions, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, Platoon Sergeant (PSG), MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Senior DS, Senior DS Leader, Senior SGL, SRU PSG, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Training Developer.', '40ca9313ee737b26a75742433cf967826a0ad7292659f488e8c7ce4a497a5086', 62, 62, null, 581, null, null, false, null),
  ('046824ce-7546-540d-8f61-f53ca2b2077d', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, Special Missions Unit (SMU) and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', '7bc6cf4654882018316bb81369634e6d252933cfb0f1f982d970525ffd575897', 62, 62, null, 582, null, null, false, null),
  ('b2995f0b-0260-5f53-a457-5cf05c9085c6', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5f).', '5a880cfc962afbe4a9edb8761a29633f0c97bb69bdaaeddd9015aa4ae60027d4', 62, 62, null, 583, null, null, false, null),
  ('408d492c-cf8d-59f8-9f7a-b083e806e746', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', '68R MSGs serve in MED DET, HQs NCO positions. It is important to note the single most demanding assignment at this level is 1SG and all MSGs are encouraged to compete for assignment selection.', '06e85ec61d2aa678e6f0ecd4400d1da269278f65186a5845933cb5824f2dafb3', 62, 62, null, 584, null, null, false, null),
  ('733225b5-8912-5c90-a3e0-03a9bebb27f5', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, it is strongly recommended NCOs at this rank pursue the completion of a degree. Sr NCOs should prioritize obtaining a degree if they have not already done so. Those with a bachelor’s degree should consider pursuing a master''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate “Most Qualified" for promotion. Additionally, Sr NCOs should complete the EJPME II course, the Army COOL - Project Management Professional (PMP) certification, and applicable Army COOL - Manager - Certifications/Licenses. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '687d16b4ca458cfd76f61de3f65a8e1822232c74caf2722d954f87189dd618ed', 62, 62, null, 585, null, null, false, null),
  ('73e579dc-cb2c-5a6c-80c1-08f8dba88c67', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-10d) and (2-10e).', '9db3f3182d8a122ebd769d9b5092b1cd5cf6c74498a5d5e44da8a8ac3acb6074', 62, 62, null, 586, null, null, false, null),
  ('5dfa1a0f-a691-5ffd-b1b2-87ab1f07cc2c', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, EOA, IG NCO, Chief Instructor, 1SG, MFT, MRT, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Sr Career Management NCO, Training Developer.', '329467ea7ca2cc508d5d3bd7138664113e80dc3d5e23db20366cd6a600883303', 62, 62, null, 587, null, null, false, null),
  ('acf8b246-e0b2-533a-8852-a705da598902', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68R', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 17. 68R – Veterinary Food Inspection Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: Merit-based indicators of consideration for SGM may include; a pattern of consistent NCOERs reflecting exceptional duty performance in challenging assignments with the potential to succeed in higher levels of responsibility; successful service in valid MSG/1SG positions within MOS/ASI career track; minimum requirement having met or exceeded NCOPDS course standards earning any of the following: Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Leadership Award, or Commandant''s List placement are given noteworthy consideration for the merit of their achievement, and continued learning opportunities through military and civilian education are highly valued.', 'be0c9948d1c989ff35eab93c44b330c9621e80b477a8110396ceafac672fafe0', 62, 63, null, 588, null, null, false, null),
  ('de4996b1-ce3a-5509-84d2-6f07e074e1d8', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'The Preventive Medicine Specialist conducts or assists with preventive medicine inspections, surveys, control operations, and preventive medicine laboratory procedures, supervises preventive medicine facilities, or serves on preventive medicine staff. 18–1. Position Titles with MOS, SQI and ASI Codes 68S titles include - 68S1O Prev Med Spec; 68S1ON4 Health Physics Spec; 68S1ON4 Prev Med Spec; 68S2O Prev Med NCO; 68S2ON4 Health Physics NCO; 68S2P Prev Med NCO; 68S2U Prev Med NCO; 68S3O Health Physics NCO; 68S3O Prev Med NCO; 68S3ON4 Health Physics NCO; 68S3ON4 Health Physics NCO; 68S34 Recruiter; 68S34L Recruiter; 68S38 Instructor; 68S38N4 Instructor; 68S3P Prev Med NCO; 68S3S Prev Med NCO; 68S3U Prev Med NCO; 68S3X Drill Sergeant; 68S4O Prev Med NCO; 68S4O Cams Crs Mgt NCO/Instr; 68S4O Detachment Sergeant; 68S4O2S Prev Med NCO; 68S4ON4 Health Physics NCO; 68S42 Sr Training Dev/Writer; 68S48 Instructor; 68S48 Prev Med Spec; 68S48N4 Instructor; 68S48P Sr Crs Mgt NCO Instructor; 68S4P Prev Med NCO; 68S5O Prev Med NCO; 68S4S Prev Med NCO; 68S58 Instructor; 68S5M First Sergeant.', '73ed300addeefb86d2a0f7859984114c7d8fd901a892d38d9c218905cee9e170', 63, 63, null, 589, null, null, false, null),
  ('18a2e44d-9a07-576f-a1b4-4306f809c358', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'A combination of assignments in both Table of Organization and Equipment (TOE) OF units and Table of Distribution and Allowances (TDA) GF units provide the ideal promotion foundation for normal career progression. TOE assignments provide the basis for training and competence in common tasks, tactical expertise, essential medical support, repair tasks, and leadership. TDA assignments provide more in-depth and specialized training. Although successive assignments and extended TOE or TDA assignment periods are not recommended; it is important to note that limited TOE positions may result in lengthier durations within the TDA. Soldiers should concentrate on developing their medical support technical and leadership skills in these assignments. Advancement recommendations are determined on mastering these skills and displaying the aptitude and attitude consistent with the "whole Soldier" concept. ASI-(N4) Health Physics Specialist is restricted to (PFC-SSG) with 24-months or less Time in Service (TIS). Soldiers are recommended to serve 12-months in their primary MOS before applying for ASI training. See DA Pam 611–21, table 12-2 for additional ASI information.', 'e1fef04e2247cd4e455a8b4b47a5509102abeb53e583d32225ed3e36be227b32', 63, 63, null, 590, null, null, false, null),
  ('0437cd6a-79cc-5e30-8b6b-a99064eeab78', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'The 16-week, 1-day MOS AIT is conducted at the JBSA-FSH, METC followed by an assignment in the newly established specialized skill set. This program prepares students to thoroughly inspect and evaluate the sanitation and safety of living quarters, food service facilities, water supplies, industrial operations, and other facilities and operations as needed. Students will also be equipped to evaluate the adequacy of wastewater and solid waste disposal operations, perform essential entomological functions to support insect and rodent control programs, and aid in collecting data for communicable and occupational disease investigations. With this comprehensive training, students will be able to help maintain a clean and safe environment for all. See Ch. 2 (2-5b) for PME requirements.', '3f484eaead1e42c2c21fb88a035247ff9f5116192fc2b343e17a5e6dce49d94b', 64, 64, null, 591, null, null, false, null),
  ('2edf2d8c-7e84-5e26-8110-0db4c42bf375', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', '68Ss serve in MED LAB Chemical, Biological, Radiological, Nuclear and Explosives (CBRNE) sections, endemic disease sections, and occupational and environmental health sections; in MED DET preventive medicine teams; in military police (MP) BN preventive medicine sections; and in field hospital supply and services sections.', '1d06994e05c0ebe44efef773d6ff27a8bd90db42d89e7442434ab814e82f66e6', 64, 64, null, 592, null, null, false, null),
  ('cee5466d-d004-5d27-92e7-a7a718b0405b', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Self-development', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Soldiers should begin formulating plans with long-term objectives, concentrating on their military skills while considering civilian education and degree-producing programs. It is also recommended Soldiers complete Army COOL - 68S - Certifications/Licenses, Registered Environmental Health Specialist/Registered Sanitarian (REHS/RS) and Associate- Infection Prevention and Control (a-PIC). SPC/CPLs should consider ASI-(N4) training. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '984691e7ee18b537ef0fcc18e81a8649038431d1aae8f4df324b14979aba35c0', 64, 64, null, 593, null, null, false, null),
  ('94b3e724-b0fb-5a70-b800-d54c99a218c6', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Additional training', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-6d) and (2-6e).', '7cd54815f52e7795535c2a2a0616c1429545fbc98e4940523dc32948c6d14ac9', 64, 64, null, 594, null, null, false, null),
  ('a4de5b77-d8c0-5b7a-8744-6966c1dfe640', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities Soldiers should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '2c2544455441782fe90358d790aeb5eb6bc6362a3ea50572cb9512ecdbdda650', 64, 64, null, 595, null, null, false, null),
  ('5b5b0cc3-5ec4-5018-a05a-7a19f1dd5e89', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5c).', 'bda5558b772a2f3f63e3177b5b82498729937cfeddb1fc72b3a6f0859e6b0499', 64, 64, null, 596, null, null, false, null),
  ('19e46349-be22-5f69-82f7-5f6f2d879aa1', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', '68S SGTs serve in MED LAB occupational and environmental health sections, and endemic disease sections, 75th Ranger regiment medical support sections; MP BN prev med sections; SPT CO, SPT SQDN, and BSB preventive medicine teams.', 'bbbed21a43c932f9695a4aa1425ab924785a310ba273e89170b527ac87139fcd', 64, 64, null, 597, null, null, false, null),
  ('5224a06c-27bd-5de8-8397-a010dbdfc126', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Self-development', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Although not mandatory SGTs should develop a plan to acquire a degree. It is also recommended SGTs complete the Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (EJPME) I course in addition to Army COOL - 68S - Certifications/Licenses. SGTs should consider ASI-(N4) training if not yet acquired. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '172f0f8071095689120fe05f417afca3b836f5eed7f28eb0d8e4447352c24b0d', 64, 64, null, 598, null, null, false, null),
  ('25240994-ac89-5f60-b074-5b119f5f5507', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Additional training', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-7d) and (2-7e).', '67b2a68b2bdcb02474d6543b42b5f0287683fe40c70ff8c9fd22a0a546f3e78f', 64, 64, null, 599, null, null, false, null),
  ('1a9ffbdc-847a-518b-b028-45225c2d39c7', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Broadening', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Drill Sergeant (DS), Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL), Joint positions, Operations (OPS) NCO, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), Master Resilience Trainer (MRT), Military Entrance Processing Command (MEPCOM) assignments, Recruiter.', 'dd026957cc32756f121fd4f3c41f417898ca6f50ac6adb0a52a58dfd72c15b0e', 64, 64, null, 600, null, null, false, null),
  ('501a9517-f99e-5659-b4b8-61f5c8edf6db', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, World Class Athlete Program (WCAP), Special Missions Unit (SMU) and Uniformed Services University of the Health Sciences (USUHS) assignment. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', 'b86054d8a7de89096e4724fe24449a6a256f54dc6a26ad778f1bd81be6944f9d', 64, 64, null, 601, null, null, false, null),
  ('3cbe61ae-8046-57bf-9b34-09564521ab44', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5d).', '68f115b341150d1c80533c7f1884b5d6a86d439654185ed8d0bcf0a6c302802f', 65, 65, null, 602, null, null, false, null),
  ('fabb75b5-f9d6-5f51-a65f-07382f1619af', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', '68S SSGs serve in MED DET and MED BN prev med teams and sections; in Civil Affairs (CA) BN medical sections; Special Forces Group (SFG) unit medical sections; and the 75th Ranger Regiment medical support sections.', 'f55ae1612526112bc9ebc79bd65433f321ae50dd235016c7565d2f8f76c28532', 65, 65, null, 603, null, null, false, null),
  ('0a01dbc7-1d0c-5c60-aa80-f93abdd109e2', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, NCOs should concentrate on acquiring a degree, if not already completed. NCOs with an associate degree should consider pursuing a bachelor''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate “Most Qualified" for promotion. It is recommended If not yet completed, SSGs complete the EJPME I course in addition to Army COOL - 68S - Certifications/Licenses. SSGs should consider ASI N4-Health Physics Specialist training if not yet acquired. ASI N4 is restricted to (SPC-SFC) and is applied for through normal channels. Descriptions, qualifications, and restrictions are found in DA Pam 611–21, table 12-2. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '55468589a9ff7832cfe9c137a9ce627a7abaf7920a784f536a71b5e8e065387d', 65, 65, null, 604, null, null, false, null),
  ('78671820-e3a3-54c3-98a2-cf41a208b97a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-8d) and (2-8e).', 'bd2e311136c5bf63eec37087dcb9e1a83b79717f0b4180344e223ed30cc96730', 65, 65, null, 605, null, null, false, null),
  ('91e5eb00-c0e3-5183-b27d-2d64c0fe41c4', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, DS, EOL, Instructor, Instructor/Writer, IG NCO, Joint positions, Observer Coach/Trainer (OC/T), OPS NCO, MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Pregnancy Postpartum Physical Training (P3T) Leader, Recruiter, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response & Prevention Coordinator (SARC), Section/Squad Leader (SL), SHARP Victim Advocate (VA), Small Group Leader (SGL), Soldier Recovery Unit (SRU) SL.', '32663ea20215ac9e457bb19608ce4001abebb339197e5a973c5808e08549f500', 65, 65, null, 606, null, null, false, null),
  ('db1b66b2-8988-5388-9074-3074bd581e34', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, Defense Threat Reduction Agency (DTRA) assignment, the Golden Knights, Special Missions Unit (SMU), Uniformed Services University of the Health Sciences (USUHS) assignment and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'be46d8be6bcdf769be5fd207cdec2ebb26d992007255f8b0b87125fd264b5e53', 65, 65, null, 607, null, null, false, null),
  ('f622dae4-e4b5-5943-939d-615ddf16d6f7', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5e).', '2b54649d57c99709a0fb5f4d2e5ccbe3151cf7422840d5dbaf71eb3128378a24', 65, 65, null, 608, null, null, false, null),
  ('1e8f0bac-ba51-5aed-a256-0518e5695875', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', '68S SFC’ serve in MED DET HQs; MED BDE Clin Ops sections; SBDE, BDE surgeon section positions; CBRNE CMD nuclear disablement teams; CA BDE medical sections and medical training positions; and SFG unit surgeon section positions.', 'f9b316fd8daef0c7f66a51c6b15a94de2bd4a79ad905818cc1a561883e51111f', 65, 65, null, 609, null, null, false, null),
  ('a942f0f6-2855-56a7-a1d6-8396d528ac55', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Self-development', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'It is recommended SFC’ complete the EJPME II course in addition to information listed in paragraph (18-6c). SFC’ should also consider ASI N4-Health Physics Specialist training if not yet acquired. ASI N4 is restricted to (SPC - SFC) and is applied for through normal channels. Descriptions, qualifications, and restrictions are found in DA Pam 611–21, table 12-2. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '279781ee9f968eac81aa81d1357adb3b9128444ac2f5b99cc39d4e3a6b57367a', 65, 65, null, 610, null, null, false, null),
  ('96607304-6437-54e5-8fc3-b9d06dadfc8f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Additional training', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-9d) and (2-9e).', '4dbd76a5d851c56043a053d34a327f63c242cb1ec07c7995d93b9beafe72be21', 65, 65, null, 611, null, null, false, null),
  ('8b294cbd-b837-5385-ab48-db8b9a143217', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Broadening', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, Detachment Sergeant, DS, EO Advisor (EOA), IG NCO, Instructor, Joint positions, OC/T, NCOIC positions, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, Platoon Sergeant (PSG), MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Senior DS, Senior DS Leader, Senior SGL, SRU PSG, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Training Developer.', '40ca9313ee737b26a75742433cf967826a0ad7292659f488e8c7ce4a497a5086', 66, 66, null, 612, null, null, false, null),
  ('29ff5758-4891-5904-b342-59140d0f7f19', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, DTRA assignment, the Golden Knights, Special Missions Unit (SMU) and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD- EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'c68dbb9a22293b8b200f78b9aa1897a0dfd0a4d06556a038595d0e17532c28d3', 66, 66, null, 613, null, null, false, null),
  ('0a517207-ecbb-5809-99ca-edde36804429', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5f).', '5a880cfc962afbe4a9edb8761a29633f0c97bb69bdaaeddd9015aa4ae60027d4', 66, 66, null, 614, null, null, false, null),
  ('e04a40cd-a76f-57d0-b810-7db0c73a4457', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', '68S MSGs serve in the 18th MEDCOM prev med sections. It is important to note the single most demanding assignment at this level is 1SG and all MSGs are encouraged to compete for assignment selection.', 'e1a7f2a6d7db7bf560514ef6dafe880f55e24171700a59959df11dfe49bed4fa', 66, 66, null, 615, null, null, false, null),
  ('dcf0a9ee-2be9-54e1-ab3d-3c69d08b0915', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, it is strongly recommended NCOs at this rank pursue the completion of a degree. Sr NCOs should prioritize obtaining a degree if they have not already done so. Those with a bachelor’s degree should consider pursuing a master''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate “Most Qualified" for promotion. Additionally, Sr NCOs should complete the EJPME II course, the Army COOL - Project Management Professional (PMP) certification, and applicable Army COOL - Manager - Certifications/Licenses. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '687d16b4ca458cfd76f61de3f65a8e1822232c74caf2722d954f87189dd618ed', 66, 66, null, 616, null, null, false, null),
  ('28814b77-bf85-564d-84e9-141c647bd684', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-10d) and (2-10e).', '9db3f3182d8a122ebd769d9b5092b1cd5cf6c74498a5d5e44da8a8ac3acb6074', 66, 66, null, 617, null, null, false, null),
  ('2c5e9fb7-21e3-5d63-9a92-fe9da16a2969', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, EOA, IG NCO, Chief Instructor, 1SG, MFT, MRT, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Sr Career Management NCO, Training Developer.', '329467ea7ca2cc508d5d3bd7138664113e80dc3d5e23db20366cd6a600883303', 66, 66, null, 618, null, null, false, null),
  ('c5a24e23-3435-5fdb-8cd9-6ad63d4aa34c', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68S', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 18. 68S – Preventive Medicine Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: Some of the merit-based indicators of consideration for SGM are: Pattern of consistent NCOERs that reflect outstanding duty performance in a variety of challenging assignments and potential to excel at higher levels of responsibility; served successfully in any of the valid MSG/1SG positions of MOS/ASI career track; minimum requirement of having met or exceeded all course standards of NCOES courses attended, with Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Leadership Award recipients, or those earning Commandant’s List placement being given noteworthy consideration for the merit of their achievement; continued learning through military and civilian educational opportunities.', '85f71a6fc3ade2df3465790b365973be4e3be07a759ab9cc99c0a56738b051fc', 66, 66, null, 619, null, null, false, null),
  ('9710f27e-e217-5f50-a1aa-8b559b25f101', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'The Animal Care Specialist is responsible for the supervision or provision of care, management, treatment, and maintenance of sanitary conditions for animals with a primary focus on the prevention and control of diseases that can be transmitted from animals to humans. 68Ts also provide comprehensive care for government-owned animals. 19–1. Position Titles with MOS, SQI and ASI Codes 68T titles include - 68T1O Animal Care Spec; 68T1O Lab Animal Tech; 68T2O Animal Care NCO; 68T2O Lab Animal Tech; 68T2L Animal Care SGT; 68T2P Animal Care Spec; 68T2S Animal Care SGT; 68T3O Animal Care NCO; 68T3O Veterinary Ops NCO; 68T34 Recruiter; 68T34 AMEDD Rctg NCO; 68T38 Instructor; 68T38P Sr Instructor/Writer; 68T3U Animal Care NCO; 68T4O Sr Animal Care NCO; 68T4O Ch, Vet Svc NCO; 68T4O Veterinary Ops NCO; 68T4O Detachment Sergeant; 68T4O2S Veterinary Ops NCO; 68T42 Sr Training Dev/Writer; 68T48 Instructor; 68T48 Instructor/Writer.', '7de45f8127662b05cb68ebb7356bca9556ce9444e8e0b8e503a154e1a4481b8c', 67, 67, null, 620, null, null, false, null),
  ('1bd6052b-d15c-521c-a0bf-127ee2a55c46', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'A combination of assignments in both Table of Organization and Equipment (TOE) OF units and Table of Distribution and Allowances (TDA) GF units provide the ideal promotion foundation for normal career progression. TOE assignments provide the basis for training and competence in common tasks, tactical expertise, essential medical support, repair tasks, and leadership. TDA assignments provide more in-depth and specialized training. Although successive assignments and extended TOE or TDA assignment periods are not recommended; it is important to note that limited TOE positions and the technical nature of this MOS, may result in lengthier durations within the TDA and is not uncommon through the rank of SFC. 68Ts convert to 68Rs upon promotion to MSG. Soldiers should concentrate on developing their medical support technical and leadership skills in these assignments. Advancement recommendations are determined on mastering these skills and displaying the aptitude and attitude consistent with the "whole Soldier" concept.', '59eedc3bbb877af73c78e45146094cf77dc14e619ae4d3c03000e83baa48f119', 67, 67, null, 621, null, null, false, null),
  ('045317a7-3264-5ef2-b74f-e25b6f3d5c85', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'The 11-week MOS AIT is conducted at the JBSA-FSH, METC followed by an assignment in the newly established specialized skill set. This comprehensive training program equips students with the necessary skills to provide military support for animal care, management, and treatment. Training subjects include veterinary administrative procedures, basic sciences, anatomy, physiology, pharmacology, pathology, toxicology, mathematics, diagnostic laboratory procedures, radiology, laboratory animal care and handling, anesthesiology, surgical procedures and support, emergency medical care, and large animal management and handling. 68Ts work under the supervision of Veterinary Corps Officers and NCOs. See Ch. 2 (2-5b) for PME requirements.', '983d78f78ba3c4455185c6ff388b1e82b3472eec12cc8f1cf37226059aeaf9c0', 67, 67, null, 622, null, null, false, null),
  ('836b372b-8c31-5b5d-849f-7be210ca9c45', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', '68Ts serve in MED DET veterinary service support teams and veterinary medical and surgical teams; and engineer (ENG) DET, ENG canine squads.', '087195da628ab87941beca122d8e94eeeefba069c0752622366abaca8be86e50', 67, 67, null, 623, null, null, false, null),
  ('56f82c6e-9cf9-5e22-9809-930e661d9d5a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'Soldiers should begin formulating plans with long-term objectives, concentrating on their military skills while considering civilian education and degree-producing programs. It is also recommended Soldiers complete Army COOL - 68T - Certifications/Licenses, the American Association of Veterinary State Boards (AAVSB), and Veterinary Technician National Exam (VTNE). See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e- Learning courses.', '92e22e73ae569fae69bafa04304d7d6dcdd2a3eb98112ab422a5f389fd521797', 67, 68, null, 624, null, null, false, null),
  ('6ffc42e6-01fe-5027-a79f-541e5ab76a8e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-6d) and (2-6e).', '7cd54815f52e7795535c2a2a0616c1429545fbc98e4940523dc32948c6d14ac9', 68, 68, null, 625, null, null, false, null),
  ('e646ebb2-2f96-5f89-bbdb-6bdc0d495cda', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, and Uniformed Services University of the Health Sciences (USUHS) assignment (SPCs only) World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities Soldiers should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', 'ba109577d30468518ec9194ce896a5d15e536ac5bd52beaa81b66e7e39307eb9', 68, 68, null, 626, null, null, false, null),
  ('750703dd-80bb-5d33-b0b1-80db18c22e44', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5c).', 'bda5558b772a2f3f63e3177b5b82498729937cfeddb1fc72b3a6f0859e6b0499', 68, 68, null, 627, null, null, false, null),
  ('285db190-627d-5c4a-a430-baaf979ea150', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', '68T SGTs serve in MED DET veterinary medical and surgical teams; ENG DET, HQ section positions; and Special Forces Group (SFG) unit surgeon section positions and combatting terrorism tracking (CbT) detachment positions.', '8e7c0e5273415cbff1a4c7f1dadc486ba0b3e16f17b8a5f485964e326cbe55f4', 68, 68, null, 628, null, null, false, null),
  ('2382d142-e6d3-5911-95e1-aaa02f996035', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'Although not mandatory SGTs should develop a plan to acquire a degree. It is also recommended SGTs complete the Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (EJPME) I course in addition to Army COOL - 68T - Certifications/Licenses and the previously listed certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'd1dfcfb7ef33c71f096242de534ddab9ee75ba9757390435cb4d4bfb11f45e12', 68, 68, null, 629, null, null, false, null),
  ('6ffe2fc9-6e5b-5de0-81a5-eb647b4a6c9f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'SGTs should consider ASI-(N4) training in addition to Ch 2. (2-7d) and (2-7e).', '90e1ca550a2da101d960c5412214ee4471e1ec797c61a698533d855ca6248fb2', 68, 68, null, 630, null, null, false, null),
  ('cabfa2dc-2566-5e07-b7a7-a97b2b3745c3', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Broadening', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Drill Sergeant (DS), Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL), Joint positions, Operations (OPS) NCO, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), Master Resilience Trainer (MRT), Military Entrance Processing Command (MEPCOM) assignments, Recruiter.', 'dd026957cc32756f121fd4f3c41f417898ca6f50ac6adb0a52a58dfd72c15b0e', 68, 68, null, 631, null, null, false, null),
  ('50d6d318-e17c-57b1-948d-7ec02b567722', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, World Class Athlete Program (WCAP) and USUHS assignment. Not all positions mentioned are considered all- inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO', '522140fb8440f74b672d3a56587bc9349f4f746419f00ebd4120ecf03011fdaf', 68, 68, null, 632, null, null, false, null),
  ('99166a47-6258-5cdf-83e0-b811e0a15509', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5d).', '68f115b341150d1c80533c7f1884b5d6a86d439654185ed8d0bcf0a6c302802f', 68, 68, null, 633, null, null, false, null),
  ('e5e8dea5-ca6a-5adc-a436-0c281e0ef001', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', '68T SSGs serve in The Old Guard, Caisson plt and the 75th Ranger Regiment HQs, medical plts, medical sections.', '38e37e8b3d886c70c3385c10e14ab56106d7dd7097aeb791dd563863d1be35ad', 68, 68, null, 634, null, null, false, null),
  ('3a424466-596c-554e-ae20-4fd343a2f800', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, NCOs should concentrate on acquiring a degree, if not already completed. NCOs with an associate degree should consider pursuing a bachelor''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate "Most Qualified" for promotion. It is also recommended SSGs complete the EJPME I course, in addition to Army COOL - 68T - Certifications/Licenses and the previously listed certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '0557860f4769deb7668af5b1d4e83d92d82701eed315c6cfd7fc24ce03248367', 68, 68, null, 635, null, null, false, null),
  ('73a8a472-0461-546f-a76c-fc418c4f4500', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-8d) and (2-8e).', 'bd2e311136c5bf63eec37087dcb9e1a83b79717f0b4180344e223ed30cc96730', 68, 68, null, 636, null, null, false, null),
  ('131b6888-0465-55b6-b227-b26f60599ff7', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, DS, EOL, Instructor, Instructor/Writer, IG NCO, Joint positions, Observer Coach/Trainer (OC/T), OPS NCO, MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Pregnancy Postpartum Physical Training (P3T) Leader, Recruiter, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response & Prevention Coordinator (SARC), Section/Squad Leader (SL), SHARP Victim Advocate (VA), Small Group Leader (SGL), Soldier Recovery Unit (SRU) SL.', '32663ea20215ac9e457bb19608ce4001abebb339197e5a973c5808e08549f500', 69, 69, null, 637, null, null, false, null),
  ('a7a6439c-a86a-5326-95e0-20296ec28122', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, USUHS assignment and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', '7bb14e5203d62b08d8bf107aae540ef833d49f7db4e34ea2b8a4b20c3741e2ed', 69, 69, null, 638, null, null, false, null),
  ('0c4af41f-034d-55a7-bb92-9b455b03a1f3', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5e).', '2b54649d57c99709a0fb5f4d2e5ccbe3151cf7422840d5dbaf71eb3128378a24', 69, 69, null, 639, null, null, false, null),
  ('12755502-db48-5170-8e1c-6124fd5d2caa', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', '68T SFC’ serve in MED DET HQs positions.', '88f3c39acb787443882abd7360d8c35e292f2ba65026d19f7cbb71edd3ccb27e', 69, 69, null, 640, null, null, false, null),
  ('6ed4957e-d629-5313-88e9-abb247073e47', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Self-development', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'It is recommended SFC’ complete the EJPME II course in addition to information listed in paragraph (19-6c).', '06dbf96fa53c6262a0874ad6cbf0f580b5a9cedf983879f5428107418c87b89c', 69, 69, null, 641, null, null, false, null),
  ('3462b0ee-bc02-5ba7-ab82-85bfcda4ea43', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Additional training', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-9d) and (2-9e).', '4dbd76a5d851c56043a053d34a327f63c242cb1ec07c7995d93b9beafe72be21', 69, 69, null, 642, null, null, false, null),
  ('55ef82a0-1bd4-58dc-92ea-1871102a0947', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Broadening', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, Detachment Sergeant, DS, EO Advisor (EOA), IG NCO, Instructor, Joint positions, OC/T, NCOIC positions, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, Platoon Sergeant (PSG), MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Senior DS, Senior DS Leader, Senior SGL, SRU PSG, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Training Developer.', '40ca9313ee737b26a75742433cf967826a0ad7292659f488e8c7ce4a497a5086', 69, 69, null, 643, null, null, false, null),
  ('0c4d0c21-b326-5d41-a247-e511917711b1', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68T', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 19. 68T – Animal Care Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, USUHS assignment and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', '7bb14e5203d62b08d8bf107aae540ef833d49f7db4e34ea2b8a4b20c3741e2ed', 69, 69, null, 644, null, null, false, null),
  ('42160358-8693-5cd6-bef0-a9d4c11c3891', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', 'The Respiratory Specialist provides valuable assistance to physicians in the care, examination and treatment of acute and chronic diseases of the respiratory and cardiac region and/or assists with the management of respiratory care areas in both general and intensive care settings. 20–1. Position Titles with MOS, SQI and ASI Codes 68V titles include - 68V2O Respiratory SGT; 68V3O Respiratory NCO; 68V34 Recruiter; 68V38 Instructor; 68V4O Respiratory NCO; 68V48 Instructor; 68V48 Instructor/Writer; 68V48 SGL.', '0c994e29a75cc3455809df10a102a7aba1deadf97df417c73f2c0156e4ca0498', 69, 70, null, 645, null, null, false, null),
  ('7b085c80-1d81-503c-a716-2fe98ce12cc6', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', 'A combination of assignments in both Table of Organization and Equipment (TOE) OF units and Table of Distribution and Allowances (TDA) GF units provide the ideal promotion foundation for normal career progression. TOE assignments provide the basis for training and competence in common tasks, tactical expertise, essential medical support, repair tasks, and leadership. TDA assignments provide more in-depth and specialized training. Although successive assignments and extended TOE or TDA assignment periods are not recommended; it is important to note that limited TOE positions and the technical nature of this MOS, may result in lengthier durations within the TDA and it is not uncommon through the rank of SFC. 68Vs begin at SGT and convert to 68Ws upon promotion to MSG. Soldiers should concentrate on developing their medical support technical and leadership skills in these assignments. Advancement recommendations are determined on mastering these skills and displaying the aptitude and attitude consistent with the "whole Soldier" concept.', '5d7e1d3df738a4f64cd0f68ec3500390610f9194419d24f7adc833243f7f5bb6', 70, 70, null, 646, null, null, false, null),
  ('ef8c6f00-4c6a-5ccb-9a47-88a4c4f63314', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', 'This AIT MOS is a two-phased course; the combined course length is 37- weeks 4-days. Phase I training is 22-weeks and conducted at the JBSA-FSH, METC followed by a phase II 15-week, 4-day training conducted at the San Antonio Military Medical Center, succeeded by an assignment in the newly established specialized skill set. The Respiratory Therapy program is an Interservice Training Review Organization (ITRO) course. Program instruction is delivered through combined lecture (didactic), demonstration and application. In phase I, students receive specialized training in the theory and practice of respiratory care. Program subjects include general medical orientation, medical terminology, anatomy, physiology, microbiology, growth and development, health communication, patient assessment, and basic life support. In phase II, students apply their knowledge and skills on a wide variety of patients and conditions in clinical rotations, which encompass surgical, medical, and neonatal intensive care units, medical wards, pulmonary function lab, and other clinical environments. See Ch. 2 (2-5c).', '304a51827c38b5da68b35e1cd4ae2189a8ca7abfd9218fa5d032dd198d56882d', 70, 70, null, 647, null, null, false, null),
  ('5073a395-b543-56b6-b391-794ad9b5800e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', '68V SGTs serve in MED DET and field hospital anesthesia service section positions.', '0226ae04dd928f5ff32ff88cd35fd1f6331667e22a109a31030931aef23e0c6b', 70, 70, null, 648, null, null, false, null),
  ('9bd744ea-3e11-50da-9416-fbbb60209d61', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Self-development', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', 'All 68V course graduates receive an Associate of Science (AS) in Health Sciences degree with a concentration in Respiratory Therapy from the College of Allied Health Sciences (CAHS), Uniformed Services University (USU). 68Vs may challenge the Therapist Multiple Choice examination in order to obtain the Certified Respiratory Therapist (CRT) credential and qualify to challenge the Clinical Simulation Exam (CSE) for the Registered Respiratory Therapist (RRT) credential. Refer to The National Board for Respiratory Care (NBRC). Although not mandatory SGTs should develop a plan to acquire a bachelor''s degree. It is also recommended SGTs complete the Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (EJPME) I course in addition to Army COOL - 68V - Certifications/Licenses. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '3e79e521195b45b897d71bd0637d51feb40411e828e03c0e14220b29cbb9f8c4', 70, 70, null, 649, null, null, false, null),
  ('d12a150e-7a02-5e81-bb04-465f5498380a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Additional training', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-7d) and (2-7e).', '67b2a68b2bdcb02474d6543b42b5f0287683fe40c70ff8c9fd22a0a546f3e78f', 70, 70, null, 650, null, null, false, null),
  ('499253dc-1921-5987-b39c-193d4d1b8c36', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Broadening', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Drill Sergeant (DS), Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL), Joint positions, Operations (OPS) NCO, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), Master Resilience Trainer (MRT), Military Entrance Processing Command (MEPCOM) assignments, Recruiter.', 'dd026957cc32756f121fd4f3c41f417898ca6f50ac6adb0a52a58dfd72c15b0e', 70, 70, null, 651, null, null, false, null),
  ('ad03ce7b-2c87-5921-b8e2-d44948c101aa', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '06ae5df573b7a7877d2fc624b0df05aee488df3f126b66fc4a92fe039e395aba', 71, 71, null, 652, null, null, false, null),
  ('55a131f4-b52c-5a04-a747-135536e81363', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5d).', '68f115b341150d1c80533c7f1884b5d6a86d439654185ed8d0bcf0a6c302802f', 71, 71, null, 653, null, null, false, null),
  ('86d6ec60-df96-58f6-b26e-33e9fcc386a4', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', '68V SSGs serve in MED DET and field hospital anesthesia service section positions.', '8a11c4b69e8f0d12c2141f6e0d7ecc9e0fa9a4b7af452cd3da313771f5ae43e4', 71, 71, null, 654, null, null, false, null),
  ('292ed7e8-2600-5423-b95b-47c04c25a903', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', 'All 68V course graduates receive an AS in Health Sciences degree with a concentration in Respiratory Therapy from the CAHS, USU. 68Vs may challenge the Therapist Multiple Choice examination in order to obtain the CRT credential and qualify to challenge the CSE for the RRT credential. Refer to the NBRC. Although not required for promotion, NCOs should concentrate on acquiring a bachelor''s degree, if not already completed. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate "Most Qualified" for promotion. It is recommended If not yet completed, SSGs complete the EJPME I course in addition to Army COOL - 68V - Certifications/Licenses. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '0849212bc0299f6ebff3a2a820cfb72c9f06e0e9656a62dcafa699515ab17ddf', 71, 71, null, 655, null, null, false, null),
  ('990dfe20-5dd2-5ae1-bfe5-2279529aedb9', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-8d) and (2-8e).', 'bd2e311136c5bf63eec37087dcb9e1a83b79717f0b4180344e223ed30cc96730', 71, 71, null, 656, null, null, false, null),
  ('cd25b64e-8cde-56f9-9148-a579cd97c75e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68V', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 20. 68V – Respiratory Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, DS, EOL, Instructor, Instructor/Writer, IG NCO, Joint positions, Observer Coach/Trainer (OC/T), OPS NCO, MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Pregnancy Postpartum Physical Training (P3T) Leader, Recruiter, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response & Prevention Coordinator (SARC), Section/Squad Leader (SL), SHARP Victim Advocate (VA), Small Group Leader (SGL), Soldier Recovery Unit (SRU) SL.', '32663ea20215ac9e457bb19608ce4001abebb339197e5a973c5808e08549f500', 71, 71, null, 657, null, null, false, null),
