8W4O2S Med OC/T; 68W4O2S Plans NCO; 68W4O2S MN Med PSG OC/T; 68W4O2S Ops NCO; 68W4O2S Plans NCO; 68W4O2S PSG; 68W4O2S Test and Eval NCO; 68W4O2S TF Med OC/T; 68W4OF2 AVN Medevac OC/T; 68W4OF2 Sr Medic; 68W4OF2 Det Sergeant; 68W4OF2 Evac PSG; 68W4OF2 Med Trng O/CT; 68W4OW1 Medic NCO; 68W4OW1 PSG; 68W4OY8 Imm/Allergy NCO; 68W4OY9 PSG; 68W42 Sr Trng Dev/Writer; 68W42 Trng Developer; 68W43 Health Care NCO; 68W43 Ops NCO; 68W48 Emergency Med Care NCO; 68W48 Health Care Spec; 68W48 Instructor; 68W48 SGL; 68W48 SLC SGL; 68W48 Sr Instructor; 68W48 Sr Trng Dev/Writer; 68W48 SSGL; 68W48 SSGL/PSG; 68W48F2 Instructor; 68W48VW1 Instructor/Writer; 68W48Y8 Instructor/Writer; 68W48Y9 Instructor; 68W4B IG NCO; 68W4F Health Care NCO; 68W4F PSG; 68W4F2S Med Trainer OC/T; 68W4F8F2 Instructor; 68W4FF2 AVN FI OC/T; 68W4FF2 BDE Flight Medic OC/T; 68W4FF2 Det Sergeant; 68W4FF2 Evac Ops NCO; 68W4FF2 1SG; 68W4FF2 Health Care NCO; 68W4FF2 Sr Med Instructor; 68W4FF2 PSG; 68W4L Health Care NCO; 68W4L8 Sr Trng Mgr Instr; 68W4MF2 1SG; 68W4P Det Sergeant; 68W4P Emergency Med Care NCO; 68W4P Health Care NCO; 68W4P INF BN Med Plt OC/T; 68W4P Instructor; 68W4P Med NCO OC/T; 68W4P Ops NCO; 68W4P Plans NCO; 68W4P PSG; 68W4P2S BSB Med Amb Plt OC/T;68W4P2S Health Care NCO; 68W4P2S Med NCO OC/T; 68W4P2S Ops NCO; 68W4P8W1 Health Care NCO; 68W4PW1 Det Sergeant; 68W4PW1 Health Care NCO; 68W4PW2 CA Med Ops NCO; 68W4Q EOA; 68W4Q SHARP Pgm Mgr; 68W4SF2S Flight Medic Instr; 68W4SF2S Ops/Trng NCO; 68W4SFW1 Emergency Med Care NCO; 68W4SFW1 Health Care NCO; 68W4SFW1 Ops NCO; 68W4SFW1 Sr Flight Medic; 68W4SW1 Health Care NCO; 68W4SW1 Plans NCO; 68W4SW1 Ops NCO; 68W4U PSG; 68W4UW1 Emergency Med Care NCO; 68W4UW1 Health Care NCO; 68W4UW1 Ops NCO; 68W4UW1 Plans NCO; 68W4UW1 PSG; 68W4V Advisor; 68W4V Emergency Med Care NCO; 68W4X Sr DS. 68W5O Sr Health Care NCO; 68W5O Intelligence Med NCO; 68W5O Ldr Dev NCO; 68W5O Med Ops NCO; 68W5O MTTF Sr Clinical OC/T; 68W5O MTTF Sr Med NCO OC/T; 68W5O Plans NCO; 68W5O Sr Ops NCO; 68W5O Sr Talent Mgt NCO; 68W5O2S BSB Txt OC/T; 68W5O2S Intelligence Med NCO; 68W5O2S Ops NCO; 68W5O2S Plans NCO; 68W5O2S Sr Health Care NCO; 68W5O2S Sr Med NCO OC/T; 68W5O2S Sr Ops NCO; 68W52 Sr Trng Dev/Writer; 68W52 Trng Developer; 68W522S Sr Trng Dev/Writer; 68W53 Sr Health Care NCO; 68W58 Ch Instructor; 68W58 Health Care NCO; 68W58 Sr Instructor; 68W582S Instructor; 68W5B IG NCO; 68W5F Sr Evac Ops NCO; 68W5M 1SG; 68W5M2S 1SG; 68W5MF2 1SG; 68W5MP 1SG; 68W5PM 1SG; 68W5P CA Med Ops NCO; 68W5P Ops NCO; 68W5P Sr Enl Med Advisor; 68W5P2S Ops NCO; 68W5PLW4 Sr Enl Med Advisor; 68W5Q EOA; 68W5SF Sr Advisor; 68W5SF Sr Health Care NCO; 68W5SF2S Sr Enl Med Advisor; 68W5U Sr Health Care NCO; 68W5V BDE Sr Medic.', '3cfb7a6631cf6ae3df9a7f03b43b014a714d3204d816081c982dcb963489f3ee', 72, 73, null, 665, null, null, false, null),
  ('a32977c8-9160-5a0f-8cd6-ea24980fa037', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'A combination of assignments in both Table of Organization and Equipment (TOE) OF units and Table of Distribution and Allowances (TDA) GF units provide the ideal promotion foundation for normal career progression. TOE assignments provide the basis for training and competence in common tasks, tactical expertise, essential medical support, repair tasks, and leadership. TDA assignments provide more in-depth and specialized training. 68Ws hold a majority of the enlisted CMF TOE authorizations. Successive assignments and extended TOE or TDA assignment periods are not recommended; however, limited TOE positions may result in lengthier durations within the TDA. Soldiers should concentrate on developing their technical medical support and leadership skills in these assignments. Advancement recommendations are determined on mastering these skills and displaying the aptitude and attitude consistent with the "whole Soldier" concept. For information regarding 68W SSG mandatory (Critical Leadership Development) CLD positions/assignments, see para. (21-6). ASI-(3P) Nationally Registered Paramedic, is awarded to 68Ws who attend and complete an approved National Registry of Emergency Medical Technician Paramedic (NREMT-P) course. It is important to note that state level paramedic certifications do not meet the requirements for (3P). ASI- (F2) Critcal Care Flight Paramedic, is awarded to 68Ws who attend and complete the Combat Paramedic and Critical Care Paramedic course at Joint Base San Antonio and the AMEDD Fort Rucker Aviation Crewmember course. ASI-(W1) Special Operations Combat Medic and ASI-(Q5) Special Forces Diving Medical Technician, is awarded to 68Ws who attend and complete John F. Kennedy Special Warfare Center and School (JFKSWC), Special Operations Center of Excellence courses. 68Ws with ASI (F2) or (W1) are ineligible for (3P) unless ASI (F2) or (W1) is deleted/removed from Soldiers personnel records. ASI-(Y8) Allergy and Immunology Specialist, is awarded to 68Ws who attend and complete the Walter Reed National Military Medical Center (WRNMMC) Immunology and Allergy Specialty course.', 'f65860e4696e2ae40c33dbf262e0ad5f5c3dceec8bc63042f2f8b430c1ca4bf7', 74, 74, null, 666, null, null, false, null),
  ('ce8c94a5-6198-575a-a687-8a3811e9802d', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'The 16-week MOS AIT is conducted at the JBSA-FSH, METC followed by an assignment in the newly established specialized skill set. The rigorous Combat Medic Specialist course is designed to train and equip students with the necessary skills and knowledge to become effective Soldiers and provide comprehensive medical care in combat and military operations other- than-war casualty care. This program covers, inpatient and outpatient care; aircraft and ground evacuation; emergency and minor acute care; tactical combat casualty care; casualty triage and processing; basic Force Health Protection (FHP), deployable medical systems, as well as the management of patients exposed to weapons of mass destruction (Chemical, Biological, Radiological, and Nuclear - CBRN). Soldiers receive National Registered Emergency Medical Technician (NREMT) certification upon completion. See Ch. 2 (2-5b) for PME requirements.', '2096d12296304b4926a843e045594a8559e1628eff629e0ec554e445a3bea028', 74, 74, null, 667, null, null, false, null),
  ('d42950d3-fe55-5b6f-b6d4-0f0bfda37869', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', '68Ws serve as para. (21-1) titles within but not limited to include combat arms DIVs and below in minimal care wards, ERs, MED PLTs, MED COs, BSBs, MTFs, and field hospitals.', '48aa6f5cecf18d627985c7425b459030928223f2107d9908e7e926e1a6fcd4dd', 74, 74, null, 668, null, null, false, null),
  ('8d87103e-c8ce-5260-b428-22ced06cba5d', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Self-development', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Soldiers should begin formulating plans with long-term objectives, concentrating on their military skills while considering civilian education and degree-producing programs. It is also recommended Soldiers complete Army COOL - 68W - Certifications/Licenses. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses. Additionally, EMT training is available through civilian agencies for Advanced EMT and Paramedic certifications, which offer advanced training, and also award promotion points for SGT and SSG.', 'fb0e68af3e3871e3a700e81d9d0f223c3bbff31af90ae6505867fdd166641394', 74, 74, null, 669, null, null, false, null),
  ('c41c298c-b4a7-5814-9d06-c464f04493bf', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Additional training', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'PFCs and SPCs/CPLs should consider ASI training see para. (21-3), which ranges from 4-38 weeks. Follow-on assignments as a ASI-(F2) for at least 27-months is required to maintain this ASI. Additionally, see Ch 2. (2-6d) and (2-6e).', '17d75d94c4cd6999ee491d33de89919a468c2056d0ecaa63c8d8493f10da5c3d', 74, 74, null, 670, null, null, false, null),
  ('281ea4ce-66c7-558e-b1d8-30fc911b5837', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities Soldiers should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '2c2544455441782fe90358d790aeb5eb6bc6362a3ea50572cb9512ecdbdda650', 75, 75, null, 671, null, null, false, null),
  ('7b8ce01b-6f9b-52f0-a9b1-598f912fd119', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5c).', 'bda5558b772a2f3f63e3177b5b82498729937cfeddb1fc72b3a6f0859e6b0499', 75, 75, null, 672, null, null, false, null),
  ('ac158a79-8b2c-5564-9b5f-f33d23a2c733', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', '68W SGTs serve as para. (21-1) titles within but not limited to include: MED PLT SLs; ASI-(W1) serve in Spec Ops and CA communities. ASI-(Y8) serve in', '7c382332d5249f277cbe638f7bf7a5646357d7005845d0a1ff301dac428c6bc9', 75, 75, null, 673, null, null, false, null),
  ('5b5fae65-2f62-5382-b32f-990a9b28c072', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Self-development', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Although not mandatory SGTs should develop a plan to acquire a degree. It is also recommended SGTs complete the Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (EJPME) I course in addition to Army COOL - 68W - Certifications/Licenses and Advanced EMT (A-EMT) and Paramedic certifications. Additionally, A-EMTs and NREMT-Ps offer advanced training available through civilian agencies, which also award promotion points for SSG. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self- improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'e74b87c66edf04e00929c894b44cb0dc11c8259d07730109a691535c370bc020', 75, 75, null, 674, null, null, false, null),
  ('b3f43332-3b32-5eb0-81a3-b4c71095a26f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Additional training', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-7d) and (2-7e).', '67b2a68b2bdcb02474d6543b42b5f0287683fe40c70ff8c9fd22a0a546f3e78f', 75, 75, null, 675, null, null, false, null),
  ('3e7a49e5-1018-5c39-bb3a-6ffb0b3ff521', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Broadening', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Drill Sergeant (DS), Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL), Joint positions, Operations (OPS) NCO, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), Master Resilience Trainer (MRT), Military Entrance Processing Command (MEPCOM) assignments, Recruiter. Additionally, highly motivated and interested NCOs can request assignments within the Security Forces Assistance Brigade (SFAB) and Special Operations (Spec Ops) community.', '043979a2ebbe2b57fee80cc8c99c83e5279f6144b9fa4032b82fa7315146be4e', 75, 75, null, 676, null, null, false, null),
  ('95391e23-ae7c-5d64-bdf6-a48181166756', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, World Class Athlete Program (WCAP), Special Missions Unit (SMU), and Uniformed Services University of the Health Sciences (USUHS) assignment. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', 'a6ff6f2be0a7ccc03f289ed46f7bcf46094cec4a0fa855de678730f18c897cac', 75, 75, null, 677, null, null, false, null),
  ('1f83d0e4-39ab-5eee-a9f3-5c89bacd0f3e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5d).', '68f115b341150d1c80533c7f1884b5d6a86d439654185ed8d0bcf0a6c302802f', 75, 75, null, 678, null, null, false, null),
  ('85356e71-80a4-5e7e-9df9-584d5e4b6a59', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', '68W SSGs serve as para. (21-1) titles within but not limited to, include: MED PLTs,NCOs, Emergency Room NCOICs, Troop Medical Clinics (TMC) NCOICs, MEDCENs Training NCOs; Clinic NCOICs based on ASIs. ASI-(W1) serve in Spec Ops and CA communities.', 'eabaa6d6879f01bdd2750e4e45993e7a6a4fdfbc10dac6b139fcce138252eb16', 75, 75, null, 679, null, null, false, null),
  ('5769a800-2a9b-5e34-bce7-283645ff9d5c', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, NCOs should concentrate on acquiring a degree, if not already completed. NCOs with an associate degree should consider pursuing a bachelor''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate "Most Qualified" for promotion. It is also recommended SSGs complete the EJPME I course, in addition to Army COOL - 68W - Certifications/Licenses and the previously listed certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'ed33d644bc474d01a9a94eefa38810214f34bd889d8148f62e9661ec428cf07f', 75, 75, null, 680, null, null, false, null),
  ('0d0bc23b-6bb4-53e6-8bef-1f9ba3b47d55', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Critical Leader Development (CLD)', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'In efforts to enhance the technical and tactical performance and knowledge at the SSG level, SSGs are required to serve in and complete a minimum of 24-months rated time in CLD positions IOT build the requisite Knowledge, Skills, and Behaviors in preparation for success as Senior NCOs. While the proponent recommends all 68W SSGs serve a minimum of 24- months in Squad Leader/Section Leader equivalent assignments prior to SFC promotion consideration, Army priorities may require SSGs to move prior to fulfilling this requirement. CLD assignments include positions under the following unit types, position and title: (subject to change). 68W CLD IDENTIFIED SECTION LDR / SQUAD LDR EQUIVALENT POSITIONS 75TH RANGER REGT STB, AMB SQD EMERGENCY CARE SGT COMMUNITY HOSPITAL ADULT OUTPNT NEURO HEALTHCARE SGT BTRY HQ HEALTHCARE SGT MEDDAC ADMIN HEALTHCARE SGT BCT CENTER OF EXCELLENCE MED SPT UNIT EMERGENCY CARE NCO MEDCEN ACUTE CARE HEALTHCARE SGT COMBAT AVN BDE SUSTAINMENT BDE MCAS AREA SPT MED TM HEALTHCARE SGT', 'eae2538739390df9954893f1a68dec5030aec0d19768ab2fa7340d4eee701a88', 75, 76, null, 681, null, null, false, null),
  ('2f10c747-d178-587f-8832-88eeaeaf918b', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-8d) and (2-8e).', 'bd2e311136c5bf63eec37087dcb9e1a83b79717f0b4180344e223ed30cc96730', 77, 77, null, 682, null, null, false, null),
  ('88a2be59-95f8-52f1-a5ee-a78ce11639cb', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Active Component / Reserve Component (AC/RC) Advisor, Battle Staff NCO, DS, EOL, Instructor, Instructor/Writer, IG NCO, Joint positions, OPS NCO, MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Pregnancy Postpartum Physical Training (P3T) Leader, Recruiter, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response & Prevention Coordinator (SARC), Section/Squad Leader (SL), SHARP Victim Advocate (VA), Small Group Leader (SGL), Soldier Recovery Unit (SRU) SL. Additionally, highly motivated and interested NCOs can request assignments within the SFAB and Spec Ops community.', '20780eac672b124d6c78669f79605ad54b8275f3181eb99b47d6f53b56051783', 77, 77, null, 683, null, null, false, null),
  ('a1140739-3c5d-5dad-832c-59d51b1a9a34', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, Security Assistance Training Management Organization (SATMO) NCO, Special Missions Unit (SMU), USUHS assignment, WCAP and White House Military Office (WHMO) assignment. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', '62aebea5b54f0ad380c7abe06776e07715ee1a13c188cd202db552d82d7c65e1', 77, 77, null, 684, null, null, false, null),
  ('c0cc1a1e-103c-565b-9ca1-da4bc35fd04e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5e).', '2b54649d57c99709a0fb5f4d2e5ccbe3151cf7422840d5dbaf71eb3128378a24', 77, 77, null, 685, null, null, false, null),
  ('4d024927-ccc8-5707-b5a4-dff769f12466', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', '68W SFC’ serve as MED PLT PSGs, MTF NCOICs, Det Sergeants, MED BDE and Regional MEDCOM Ops NCOs; and fulfill positions with the Spec Ops and CA communities for SFC’ with W1 and W4 ASIs.', 'a561866bb2784fe942c22118df010babcd8f102e23af94af0d80bbbe83ec07ab', 77, 77, null, 686, null, null, false, null),
  ('e13fb667-b5ec-5982-ac2f-b771d23b0471', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Self-development', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'It is recommended SFC’ complete the EJPME II course in addition to information listed in paragraph (21-6c).', '34ffbb36d6bf4ad333d9db8443d43d42da9e9bb669684a93334653d1a6ac5b82', 77, 77, null, 687, null, null, false, null),
  ('622047c5-3286-5a02-afdb-865acacb98bc', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Additional training', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-9d) and (2-9e).', '4dbd76a5d851c56043a053d34a327f63c242cb1ec07c7995d93b9beafe72be21', 77, 77, null, 688, null, null, false, null),
  ('efc676a1-7d78-54fa-bc0c-84c6934954ff', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Broadening', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include AC/RC Advisor, Battle Staff NCO, Detachment Sergeant, EO Advisor (EOA), IG NCO, Instructor, Joint positions, NCOIC positions, OC/T (Project Warrior), OPS NCO, Plans NCO, Platoon Sergeant (PSG), MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Senior SGL, SRU PSG, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Training Developer. Additionally, highly motivated and interested NCOs can request assignments within the SFAB and Spec Ops community.', '7cd2d4fae9f42a07b4a590cc1e4322e29cfa4f9859ef14ef151653acdd0aab82', 77, 77, null, 689, null, null, false, null),
  ('c322ebeb-e4fd-5654-bfce-654515d3544f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, Defense Threat Reduction Agency (DTRA) assignment, the Golden Knights, Health Services Branch PDNCO, SATMO NCO, Special Missions Unit (SMU), USUHS assignment WCAP and White House Military Office (WHMO) assignment. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', '92495c230403371f54e5726f5217207bc36be42a2b774fdbcc3292de0c409b67', 77, 78, null, 690, null, null, false, null),
  ('fc60a52f-8cd6-5134-9459-6ec4db8b2d7d', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5f).', '5a880cfc962afbe4a9edb8761a29633f0c97bb69bdaaeddd9015aa4ae60027d4', 78, 78, null, 691, null, null, false, null),
  ('3ad13483-2332-55ef-8a63-45e5f793c198', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Spec Ops MSG equivalent leadership positions is the Sr Enlisted Medical Advisor (SEMA) at the BDE and DIV level. Spec Ops, consecutive MSG TDA assignments may not be avoided based on the needs of USASOC. It is important to note the single most demanding assignment at this level is 1SG and all MSGs are encouraged to compete for assignment selection.', '698c3190ba9ed697ab1aaa732b070d465cf4b566a08c3d9f0d83f92cd63d3dc1', 78, 78, null, 692, null, null, false, null),
  ('700b31c6-b740-5028-b0d8-57276ef56338', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'self_development', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, it is strongly recommended NCOs at this rank pursue the completion of a degree. Sr NCOs should prioritize obtaining a degree if they have not already done so. Those with a bachelor’s degree should consider pursuing a master''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate “Most Qualified" for promotion. Additionally, Sr NCOs should complete the EJPME II course, the Army COOL - Project Management Professional (PMP) certification, and applicable Army COOL - Manager - Certifications/Licenses. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '687d16b4ca458cfd76f61de3f65a8e1822232c74caf2722d954f87189dd618ed', 78, 78, null, 693, null, null, false, null),
  ('852998c9-8951-56af-bc0f-53608ed645cd', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'training', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-10d) and (2-10e).', '9db3f3182d8a122ebd769d9b5092b1cd5cf6c74498a5d5e44da8a8ac3acb6074', 78, 78, null, 694, null, null, false, null),
  ('5d40322e-ccf0-5241-82fa-50e2f3546794', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include 1SG, AC/RC Advisor, Battle Staff NCO, Chief Training Developer/Instructor Writer, EOA, IG NCO, MFT, MRT, OC/T (Project Warrior), OPS NCO, Plans NCO, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Sr Career Management NCO. Additionally, highly motivated and interested NCOs can request assignments within the SFAB and Spec Ops community.', '3c9b98ab5adbfe4214a5d1d209568683f4c939a4551af7754d046bc1ccad4883', 78, 78, null, 695, null, null, false, null),
  ('18266596-cb47-5f26-810e-4a05e6b83a09', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68W', null, 'assignments', 'E-8', null, 'Master Sergeant (MSG) / First Sergeant (1SG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 21. 68W – Combat Medic Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: Merit-based indicators of consideration for SGM may include; a pattern of consistent NCOERs reflecting exceptional duty performance in challenging assignments with the potential to succeed in higher levels of responsibility; successful service in valid MSG/1SG positions within MOS/ASI career track; minimum requirement having met or exceeded NCOPDS course standards earning any of the following: Distinguished Honor Graduate, Honor Graduate, Leadership Award, or Commandant''s List placement are given noteworthy consideration for the merit of their achievement, and continued learning opportunities through military and civilian education are highly valued.', 'be0c9948d1c989ff35eab93c44b330c9621e80b477a8110396ceafac672fafe0', 78, 78, null, 696, null, null, false, null),
  ('dc53ebe8-5cc8-5c8b-acd8-3feac7e9814f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'The Behavioral Health Specialist, under the supervision of a psychiatrist, social worker, psychiatric nurse or psychologist, assists with the management and treatment of inpatient and outpatient behavioral health (BH) activities, during peace time or mobilization; collects and records psychosocial and physical data; counsels and treats patients with personal, behavioral or mental health problems. 22–1. Position Titles with MOS, SQI and ASI Codes 68X titles include - 68X1O Behavioral Health Spec; 68X1P Behavioral Health Spec; 68X2O Behavioral Health NCO; 68X2O Team Chief; 68X2P Behavioral Health NCO; 68X2S Behavioral Health NCO; 68X3O Behavioral Health NCO; 68X3OY9 Squad Leader; 68X34 RCTR ; 68X34L RCTR ; 68X38 Instructor; 68X3P Behavioral Health NCO; 68X3S Behavioral Health NCO; 68X3U Behavioral Health NCO; 68X3X Drill Sergeant. 68X4O Behavioral Health NCO; 68X4O Detachment Sergeant; 68X48 Instructor; 68X4P Behavioral Health NCO.', '62cb16c4c2156c1b6e4d4d4ea138bb578cd41437d668ac11c79874a49a49070b', 79, 79, null, 697, null, null, false, null),
  ('cfffebe1-dbf0-5f8f-b72f-04018540f232', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'A combination of assignments in both Table of Organization and Equipment (TOE) OF units and Table of Distribution and Allowances (TDA) GF units provide the ideal promotion foundation for normal career progression. TOE assignments provide the basis for training and competence in common tasks, tactical expertise, essential medical support, repair tasks, and leadership. TDA assignments provide more in-depth and specialized training. Although successive assignments and extended TOE or TDA assignment periods are not recommended; it is important to note that limited TOE positions and the technical nature of this MOS, may result in lengthier durations within the TDA and is not uncommon through the rank of SFC. 68Xs convert to 68Ws upon promotion to MSG. Soldiers should concentrate on developing their medical support technical and leadership skills in these assignments. Advancement recommendations are determined on mastering these skills and displaying the aptitude and attitude consistent with the "whole Soldier" concept.', 'f097db77ce6d9aaef550551b80f9ac2c1b3a08a9c41e7c741f6ca4f7b39f933e', 79, 79, null, 698, null, null, false, null),
  ('bc573c38-20f4-52f8-b7bd-899b5b9e4420', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'The 17-week, 4-day MOS AIT is conducted at the JBSA-FSH, METC followed by an assignment in the newly established specialized skill set. The Behavioral Health Specialist course equips students with the knowledge, skills, and communication techniques required to assess/evaluate military personnel and their families in need of behavioral health care. Topics covered include human development, psychopathological disorders, psychological testing, consultation, interviewing, and counseling. Course curriculum is delivered through combined didactic classroom instruction, closely supervised practical exercises, and an intensive clinical practicum to ensure a comprehensive understanding of communication skills, testing, assessment procedures, and counseling approaches. See Ch. 2 (2-5b) for PME requirements.', '6905102f3b5da504074d71cf9996a44c154974c873adcd1d1ddbbcd7ecf371da', 79, 79, null, 699, null, null, false, null),
  ('b00604d3-696e-5839-99b4-5640c4b6fdaf', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', '68Xs serve in MP Group BH sections; MED DET specialty clinic sections, main support and forward support sections; MED CO, SPT CO, SPT SQDN, and BSB mental health sections; BDE BH sections, medical treatment teams, medical sections, BDE surgeon sections.', '70aaf01089c3a091a130b088c61bbbb26706cd61d00c22242bf727294caeab08', 79, 79, null, 700, null, null, false, null),
  ('8600f80b-dfc5-5058-9050-952760989726', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Self-development', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'Soldiers should begin formulating plans with long-term objectives, concentrating on their military skills while considering civilian education and degree-producing programs. It is also recommended Soldiers complete Army COOL - 68X - Certifications/Licenses. At a minimum, the Registered Behavior Technician (RBT). See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self- improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '22e1d23f932f02871b722f0c075828ca1b5a458e826c0400207547e5025b27a0', 79, 79, null, 701, null, null, false, null),
  ('d4a13a91-b1d1-5024-aea0-cf34577c9781', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Additional training', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'All Soldiers should attend any and all military schools offered to them such as All Soldiers should attend 68X functional courses offered to them such as Individual and Group Drug and Alcohol Rehab Training, Combat and Operation Stress Control (COSC) and Traumatic Event Management. Additionally, see Ch 2. (2-6d) and (2-6e).', 'eb301147dda0683e2b866dbe90e0e3c0ad39080413e6d56ebf822ee6a24f999e', 80, 80, null, 702, null, null, false, null),
  ('93191c81-d57b-5d94-864e-3760f62e8377', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities Soldiers should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '2c2544455441782fe90358d790aeb5eb6bc6362a3ea50572cb9512ecdbdda650', 80, 80, null, 703, null, null, false, null),
  ('5a5a343d-85b7-549f-8936-44e37af1eeea', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5c).', 'bda5558b772a2f3f63e3177b5b82498729937cfeddb1fc72b3a6f0859e6b0499', 80, 80, null, 704, null, null, false, null),
  ('9711c267-048a-5c94-a2d4-eed2f04e553a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', '68X SGTs serve in MP Group BH sections; MED DET forward support and main support sections; SPT CO, SPT SQDN mental health sections; BSB mental health sections; BDE BH sections, sustainment surgeon sections, medical sections and treatment teams, MED BDE Clin Ops sections; and Special Forces Group (SFG) unit surgeon sections.', 'd6bbd7b0421538b32004abb5519a16a38c7f8d3e1252dc52b3a44b97c648d3b6', 80, 80, null, 705, null, null, false, null),
  ('b32e57d4-c4a4-5ebc-b2e3-a2c93e31e00b', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Self-development', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'Although not mandatory SGTs should develop a plan to acquire a degree. It is also recommended SGTs complete the Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (EJPME) I course in addition to Army COOL - 68X - Certifications/Licenses and previously listed certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'e1a6f5ea2be35127ba5aae4ecd55afc1d75e0d0edc2cdd657fce2a0f24e8f381', 80, 80, null, 706, null, null, false, null),
  ('2bf58672-0cc1-569c-9ae5-76b528af45e8', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Additional training', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'All Soldiers should attend any and all available military schools offered to them such as Airborne, Air Assault, SERE, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), and Master Resiliency Training (MRT). All Soldiers should attend 68X functional courses offered to them such as Individual and Group Drug and Alcohol Rehab Training, Behavioral Science Consultation Team Training (BSCT), Combat and Operation Stress Control (COSC) and Traumatic Event Management. All CMF 68 Soldiers should compete for the Expert Field Medical Badge (EFMB). It is not only an honor to hold the EFMB, but it may become a discriminator in selection for promotion.', 'ba677e27d3e7b4c94cf117c50d225d31110278c17e3b42cca2a28f4482cb95b8', 80, 80, null, 707, null, null, false, null),
  ('76acdb06-f3a9-5f28-a5b7-55c5e05c859a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Broadening', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Drill Sergeant (DS), Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL), Joint positions, Operations (OPS) NCO, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), Master Resilience Trainer (MRT), Military Entrance Processing Command (MEPCOM) assignments, Recruiter.', 'dd026957cc32756f121fd4f3c41f417898ca6f50ac6adb0a52a58dfd72c15b0e', 80, 80, null, 708, null, null, false, null),
  ('08d5ffc6-6647-5105-b545-2b8446862e27', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, World Class Athlete Program (WCAP) and Special Missions Unit (SMU). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD- EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '3a72b042c88f7abed06e643628fc712e54c53cc60cae0795d271bd7a1bc83c41', 80, 80, null, 709, null, null, false, null),
  ('fc93bd43-097e-515d-a1b7-dabb5ab0130d', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5d).', '68f115b341150d1c80533c7f1884b5d6a86d439654185ed8d0bcf0a6c302802f', 80, 80, null, 710, null, null, false, null),
  ('7165bf08-45d4-5310-9062-72ad0d12b5dd', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', '68X SSGs serve in MED DET forward support and main support sections; MED BN mental health sections; 160th Aviation Regiment (Special Operations) mental health sections; and 75th Ranger Regiment units mental health sections.', '0f4162161990b681adb8fc4605e541240fe615934ad864a9c89e27cdbd0c71cb', 80, 80, null, 711, null, null, false, null),
  ('4a2aeed8-7509-51cb-8be7-b7327d3290f1', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, NCOs should concentrate on acquiring a degree, if not already completed. NCOs with an associate degree should consider pursuing a bachelor''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate "Most Qualified" for promotion. It is also recommended SSGs complete the EJPME I course, in addition to Army COOL - 68X - Certifications/Licenses and the previously listed certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'd95463ea516a759cf0eee168c2bc2251e23fbe44657ce97bb32a82d2b0496dda', 80, 81, null, 712, null, null, false, null),
  ('c52a4b5f-abcb-5c09-b35b-7ffe2b1595c6', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-8d) and (2-8e).', 'bd2e311136c5bf63eec37087dcb9e1a83b79717f0b4180344e223ed30cc96730', 81, 81, null, 713, null, null, false, null),
  ('eaa1eda8-4e9a-5141-b057-bdcd2694623c', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, DS, EOL, Instructor, Instructor/Writer, IG NCO, Joint positions, Observer Coach/Trainer (OC/T), OPS NCO, MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Pregnancy Postpartum Physical Training (P3T) Leader, Recruiter, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response & Prevention Coordinator (SARC), Section/Squad Leader (SL), SHARP Victim Advocate (VA), Small Group Leader (SGL), Soldier Recovery Unit (SRU) SL.', '32663ea20215ac9e457bb19608ce4001abebb339197e5a973c5808e08549f500', 81, 81, null, 714, null, null, false, null),
  ('fb308ec4-384c-586f-a96f-f785239e0373', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, Special Missions Unit (SMU) and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', '7bc6cf4654882018316bb81369634e6d252933cfb0f1f982d970525ffd575897', 81, 81, null, 715, null, null, false, null),
  ('e68f6fe8-3b86-594f-8121-f3c2407bf18b', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5e).', '2b54649d57c99709a0fb5f4d2e5ccbe3151cf7422840d5dbaf71eb3128378a24', 81, 81, null, 716, null, null, false, null),
  ('3c7b7642-8c58-5a25-968a-91e5795f896f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', '68X SFC’ serve in MED DET Detachment Sergeant positions; MED BN mental health sections; and MED BDE Clin Ops sections.', '83cfc897f1ca56e7391ac057f2ce6903dd0b499fa2ff6130468a1b7ae86ef106', 81, 81, null, 717, null, null, false, null),
  ('510b7237-b8df-5b62-bb2f-3c6b1a91896b', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Self-development', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'It is recommended SFC’ complete the EJPME II course in addition to information listed in paragraph (22-6c).', 'ff8a8fa25ef8bde645994638378ecffbecf6263779f42062d35033f6bf6a385b', 81, 81, null, 718, null, null, false, null),
  ('2ece53e4-1cbe-5849-9577-8b1bd681533f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Additional training', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-9d) and (2-9e).', '4dbd76a5d851c56043a053d34a327f63c242cb1ec07c7995d93b9beafe72be21', 81, 81, null, 719, null, null, false, null),
  ('fa8fc59d-c070-5aca-a3f1-f740ab8deb26', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Broadening', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, Detachment Sergeant, DS, EO Advisor (EOA), IG NCO, Instructor, Joint positions, OC/T, NCOIC positions, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, Platoon Sergeant (PSG), MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Senior DS, Senior DS Leader, Senior SGL, SRU PSG, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Training Developer.', '40ca9313ee737b26a75742433cf967826a0ad7292659f488e8c7ce4a497a5086', 81, 81, null, 720, null, null, false, null),
  ('bfdfa785-57aa-5918-8b4a-3b423e946617', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68X', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 22. 68X – Behavioral Health Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, Special Missions Unit (SMU) and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', '7bc6cf4654882018316bb81369634e6d252933cfb0f1f982d970525ffd575897', 81, 81, null, 721, null, null, false, null),
  ('0e81c6c7-7f5e-5b8c-bca8-127b3f98e164', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'The Eye Specialist assumes a pivotal role in overseeing or performing routine diagnostic tests and providing assistance to Optometrists and Ophthalmologists in the provision of care and treatment for patients with ophthalmological or optometric conditions. 23–1. Position Titles with MOS, SQI and ASI Codes 68Y titles include - 68Y1O Eye Spec; 68Y2O Eye SGT; 68Y3O Eye SGT; 68Y3O Medical NCO; 68Y38 Instructor; 68Y38 Instructor/Writer; 68Y4O Eye NCO; 68Y4O Detachment SGT; 68Y48 Instructor; 68Y48 Instructor/Writer.', '6511a9e79597012ef734010d4cf0d9da333635c4e4613d01d93890285edbe8b7', 82, 82, null, 722, null, null, false, null),
  ('c7bed1c9-808f-595d-8520-f3447b5affb7', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'A combination of assignments in both Table of Organization and Equipment (TOE) OF units and Table of Distribution and Allowances (TDA) GF units provide the ideal promotion foundation for normal career progression. TOE assignments provide the basis for training and competence in common tasks, tactical expertise, essential medical support, repair tasks, and leadership. TDA assignments provide more in-depth and specialized training. Although successive assignments and extended TOE or TDA assignment periods are not recommended; it is important to note that limited TOE positions and the technical nature of this MOS, may result in lengthier durations within the TDA and is not uncommon through the rank of SFC. 68Ys convert to 68Ws upon promotion to MSG. Soldiers should concentrate on developing their medical support technical and leadership skills in these assignments. Recommendations for promotion advancement are determined on mastering these skills and displaying the aptitude and attitude consistent with the "whole Soldier" concept.', '24c41eb34ab554efd30cbe6a50bf9344732cf0f563f5e653bfa49f20cb7799e2', 82, 82, null, 723, null, null, false, null),
  ('0f363b47-74f4-585f-b266-26be8782d52c', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'This AIT MOS is a two-phased course; the combined course length is 13- weeks, 4-days. Phase I training is 8-weeks, 2-days and conducted at the JBSA-FSH, METC followed by a phase II 5-week, 2-day training conducted at a designated MTF, succeeded by an assignment in the newly established specialized skill set. The comprehensive Eye Specialist course curriculum offers a learning experience that includes classroom instruction, hands-on demonstrations, computer labs, and practical exercises. Phase I provides a solid foundation in the necessary subjects to assist ophthalmologists and optometrists in military eye clinics. These subjects include medical terminology, anatomy and physiology of the eye, vision and diagnostic testing, pathological conditions, sterilization of eye equipment and instruments, optical procedures, minor surgery, history taking, administrative procedures, supply management, and medical record ordering, and safeguarding. In phase II, students receive on-the-job training in the clinical environment. See Ch. 2 (2-5b) for PME requirements.', '6b46f4b52b760b027172d02175656c2c3858a128cac2cc6b9975ceb5cab702fe', 82, 82, null, 724, null, null, false, null),
  ('6caa8127-c226-5a3f-923d-54055d5aa6bb', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', '68Ys serve in MED DET optometry teams.', '7792c3866dd6a76a92f13ca383b1edbc8df9044b33fd1484fb190186a84341d6', 82, 82, null, 725, null, null, false, null),
  ('07dbdfec-3d91-5aca-be6b-06326d5bb741', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Self-development', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'Soldiers should begin formulating plans with long-term objectives, concentrating on their military skills while considering civilian education and degree-producing programs. It is also recommended Soldiers complete Army COOL - 68Y - Certifications/Licenses. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '58ef78e323338c4b4f0977a17aa5a5420af963ad05023a5ae0e3bfe9f6e0e5c9', 82, 82, null, 726, null, null, false, null),
  ('19ba4ef8-0573-5267-8bf2-3959ffed0180', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Additional training', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-6d) and (2-6e).', '7cd54815f52e7795535c2a2a0616c1429545fbc98e4940523dc32948c6d14ac9', 82, 82, null, 727, null, null, false, null),
  ('371ee3d7-99ac-565d-8a57-d166afb85fa3', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private (PVT) – Specialist (SPC) / Corporal (CPL) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities Soldiers should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '2c2544455441782fe90358d790aeb5eb6bc6362a3ea50572cb9512ecdbdda650', 82, 83, null, 728, null, null, false, null),
  ('0099e2e1-ebdc-5d36-aec8-0a5abeb2bf31', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5c).', 'bda5558b772a2f3f63e3177b5b82498729937cfeddb1fc72b3a6f0859e6b0499', 83, 83, null, 729, null, null, false, null),
  ('1d96cdd6-0392-58c7-a0f5-c908831dcdf7', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', '68Y SGTs serve in MED DET head and neck teams.', 'aa0bc97e6b90402ba11e6be62ee87a82840544dd892a299d6c56855bab45ecf4', 83, 83, null, 730, null, null, false, null),
  ('de7307cb-ab70-5837-b6b7-2805462a7261', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Self-development', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'Although not mandatory SGTs should develop a plan to acquire a degree. It is also recommended SGTs complete the Enlisted Joint Professional Military Education (EJPME) I course in addition to Army COOL - 68Y - Certifications/Licenses and the following certifications: Certified Ophthalmic Assistant (COA) and Certified Ophthalmic Technician (COT). See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', 'a99a081f173c3cafb3041643c1d493e8391534909ca69cfd388f3739afb9e8d1', 83, 83, null, 731, null, null, false, null),
  ('2d93ccef-6b15-5489-b355-b28767ecc3c9', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Additional training', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-7d) and (2-7e).', '67b2a68b2bdcb02474d6543b42b5f0287683fe40c70ff8c9fd22a0a546f3e78f', 83, 83, null, 732, null, null, false, null),
  ('66beccb5-1db4-551b-8253-a25ad5ecdefc', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Broadening', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Drill Sergeant (DS), Equal Opportunity Leader (EOL), Joint positions, Operations (OPS) NCO, Master Fitness Trainer (MFT), Master Resilience Trainer (MRT), Military Entrance Processing Command (MEPCOM) assignments, Recruiter.', 'dd026957cc32756f121fd4f3c41f417898ca6f50ac6adb0a52a58dfd72c15b0e', 83, 83, null, 733, null, null, false, null),
  ('a89dea3f-3224-5452-81c3-451a30918d07', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant (SGT) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include the Golden Knights, and World Class Athlete Program (WCAP). Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO.', '436437aab9bbdc5901be9794f7a7571032da84bf2af1b33b73ea398e53e1b17f', 83, 83, null, 734, null, null, false, null),
  ('1dd59f91-137b-57e8-b901-9415acfc445e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5d).', '68f115b341150d1c80533c7f1884b5d6a86d439654185ed8d0bcf0a6c302802f', 83, 83, null, 735, null, null, false, null),
  ('3533c2bf-68d6-5890-a9d6-bf77dff776a8', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', '68Y SSGs serve in MED DET optometry teams.', '67f6aa48dd9ad0caf9262fc3447f94eaf27613c9701537fa49fd421a2a0cd6da', 83, 83, null, 736, null, null, false, null),
  ('3319ce5c-347b-5ee3-9f03-4c721b14b631', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'self_development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Self-development', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'Although not required for promotion, NCOs should concentrate on acquiring a degree, if not already completed. NCOs with an associate degree should consider pursuing a bachelor''s degree. It is important to note that civilian education could be used as a self-improvement indicator for promotion consideration and selection. Education is not a substitute for challenging assignments and by itself, does not indicate "Most Qualified" for promotion. It is also recommended SSGs complete the EJPME I course, in addition to Army COOL - 68Y - Certifications/Licenses and the previously listed certifications. See Ch. 2 for detailed information on self-improvement, COOL certifications, DL, and Army e-Learning courses.', '7fbb667e989ef986a104c8af96cf968f69b21257b33687a922c66a8a9a238d83', 83, 83, null, 737, null, null, false, null),
  ('1ae98a02-4445-5fd7-98d9-af115e74b28a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Additional training', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-8d) and (2-8e).', 'bd2e311136c5bf63eec37087dcb9e1a83b79717f0b4180344e223ed30cc96730', 83, 83, null, 738, null, null, false, null),
  ('a82fb2ac-b2c6-54ff-a24c-38a9010a5b52', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Broadening', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, DS, EOL, Instructor, Instructor/Writer, IG NCO, Joint positions, Observer Coach/Trainer (OC/T), OPS NCO, MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Pregnancy Postpartum Physical Training (P3T) Leader, Recruiter, Sexual Harassment/Assault Response & Prevention Coordinator (SARC), Section/Squad Leader (SL), SHARP Victim Advocate (VA), Small Group Leader (SGL), Soldier Recovery Unit (SRU) SL.', '32663ea20215ac9e457bb19608ce4001abebb339197e5a973c5808e08549f500', 83, 83, null, 739, null, null, false, null),
  ('3e330025-929c-5491-a891-9113d9ebc730', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant (SSG) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'f55071b398a6906dfc3418f08533f9fd34ffbc29a25fff4cdf464ebdd54e4073', 83, 84, null, 740, null, null, false, null),
  ('4e4b5d2a-505e-5761-baca-c24eae29872e', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5e).', '2b54649d57c99709a0fb5f4d2e5ccbe3151cf7422840d5dbaf71eb3128378a24', 84, 84, null, 741, null, null, false, null),
  ('1b5deadd-9efb-56e7-b441-78b6c6e56883', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'There are currently no 68Y SFC TOE assignments.', '4cd8b378a67be6e00802001873df237bbd79754b471f52a6e77f3aa0fbba589e', 84, 84, null, 742, null, null, false, null),
  ('8580e76a-5beb-5b09-8b8e-521c2c4f30de', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'self_development', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Self-development', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'It is recommended SFC’ complete the EJPME II course in addition to information listed in paragraph (23-6c).', 'f6280e7e37be342f5a91cd4df75afa87d5e14a709622f07e81a3950f450a04b6', 84, 84, null, 743, null, null, false, null),
  ('1c713f4b-aa89-5cf4-aca4-8a49b30165d1', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'training', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Additional training', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'See Ch 2. (2-9d) and (2-9e).', '4dbd76a5d851c56043a053d34a327f63c242cb1ec07c7995d93b9beafe72be21', 84, 84, null, 744, null, null, false, null),
  ('dd5aa483-3533-51f6-9ffb-e5f985965135', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Broadening', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'Broadening opportunities and assignments include Battle Staff NCO, Detachment Sergeant, DS, EO Advisor (EOA), IG NCO, Instructor, Joint positions, OC/T, NCOIC positions, OPS NCO, Plans NCO, Platoon Sergeant (PSG), MFT, MRT, MEPCOM assignments, Senior DS, Senior DS Leader, Senior SGL, SRU PSG, P3T Leader, SARC, SHARP Master Advocate, Training Developer.', '40ca9313ee737b26a75742433cf967826a0ad7292659f488e8c7ce4a497a5086', 84, 84, null, 745, null, null, false, null),
  ('cd231ec0-95d4-5a86-8c61-c52549949a8a', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Y', null, 'assignments', 'E-7', null, 'Sergeant First Class (SFC) — Special/Nominative opportunities', 'Chapter 23. 68Y – Eye Specialist', 'Special/Nominative opportunities and assignments include Attaché, the Golden Knights, and WCAP. Not all positions mentioned are considered all-inclusive, for information regarding assignment opportunities NCOs should contact the HRC, HSD-EB, Broadening/Nominative assignments Sr Talent Management NCO. *Note: See CMF-68-board-brief combined with DA PAM 600-25 and PDM milestones for Sr NCO promotion selection indicators of consideration.', 'f55071b398a6906dfc3418f08533f9fd34ffbc29a25fff4cdf464ebdd54e4073', 84, 84, null, 746, null, null, false, null),
  ('863202fd-bbe0-5329-846d-c73d61a3ca15', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'development', null, null, 'Overview', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'The chief medical NCO at the rank of SGM caps CMF 68 MOSs. The duties performed by the SGM of these former MOSs are supervisory and leadership duties of the 68Z-SGM. The Chief Medical NCO serves as the principal NCO and Sr advisor to CDRs, directors, departments chiefs, and staff agencies regarding all enlisted personnel matters within multifunctional MTFs and medical staff activities, or TOE and TDA medical units. Chief Medical NCOs must have a comprehensive understanding of technical mission sets, responsibilities, and operations of all medical functional activities, including DIV-level and higher levels of medical special, general, and joint staff sections, MEDCENs, large and medium-sized hospitals, MEDDACs, MTFs, health centers/clinics, BTRY, CO, and TRP size units, and all medical organization levels of echelons including all major commands. Chief Medical NCOs must also possess the expertise and experience needed to plan, coordinate, and supervise unit organizations, training, technical, and tactical operations. 24–1. Position Titles with MOS, SQI and ASI Codes 68Z/00Z titles include - 00Z6O8C CSM; 00Z6O8D CSM; 00Z6O8E CSM; 68Z6O6C CSM; 68Z6O6P MTTF CSM; 68Z6O7C CSM; 68Z6O7C CSM; 68Z6O7P CSM; 68Z6O7S CSM; 68Z6P5W CSM; 68Z6O7P Commandant; 68Z6O6S Ops SGM; 68Z6O6U Ops SGM; 68Z6O6X Ops SGM; 68Z6O7S Ops SGM; 68Z6O7S SGM; 68Z6O7S SHARP SGM; 68Z6O7X G1/4/6 SGM; 68Z6O7X G3/5/7 SGM; 68Z6O7X Ops SGM; 68Z6P5W Ops SGM; 68Z6P7S Med Ops SGM; 68Z6O6K Chief Medical NCO; 68Z6O6S Chief Medical NCO; 68Z6O6X Chief Medical NCO; 68Z6O7S Chief Medical NCO; Sr Med NCO; 68Z6O7S Talent MGR; 68Z6O7X Chief Medical NCO; 68Z6O7X Sr Medical NCO; 68Z686X Chief Medical NCO; 68Z687S Chief Medical NCO; 68Z687S Chief Instructor; 68Z6B7S Assistant IG; 68Z6P5W Chief Medical NCO.', 'dec204811600b434f5f0458b19bedfa548ca8473671d6eea80dfbd548bb9e12c', 84, 85, null, 747, null, null, false, null),
  ('7211e668-43eb-5a85-8b1b-4f6bceb269b5', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'The career development plans preceding this MOS will assist NCOs arrive at this level. Normal career progression at this rank should include successively higher levels of TOE and TDA assignments. Most 68Z positions are in the TDA. Although, consecutive assignments and/or extended TOE or TDA periods are not recommended; it is important to note that repetitive assignments and extended TOE or TDA durations may occur based on the needs of the Army. SGM/CSMs should complete Army COOL - 68Z - Certifications/Licenses and applicable, Army COOL - Manager - Certifications/Licenses.', '54f85860e26d057da8d6d136714ccf5a73ab2362d574fa1101c287404c6633f4', 85, 85, null, 748, null, null, false, null),
  ('665001c1-14b7-578e-bad5-59a907633f40', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'training', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5e).', '2b54649d57c99709a0fb5f4d2e5ccbe3151cf7422840d5dbaf71eb3128378a24', 85, 85, null, 749, null, null, false, null),
  ('9f200e5a-61a9-5b71-b934-c453abc4d37c', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) — OF assignments', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'Positions include Sr NCO for BN, BDE, DIV, Corps, Direct Reporting Units (DRU), Army Service Component Commands (ASCC), Army Commands (ACOM) level sustainment and surgeons section/div; Sr medical, clinical, dental, medlog, prevmed, hospital nutrition care services, medlab services, veterinary services, biomed equipment repair, Ops/Plans positions; MED BN FHP cell positions; MED BDE S3/Clin Ops positions; MEDCEN and MED LAB HQs positions.', 'f66d3e31e067d56f27957d137f9a2c82cd32bb7c32903474558d8343aa76484c', 85, 85, null, 750, null, null, false, null),
  ('b4540529-332a-59e4-8e72-7917456cf8d4', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) — GF assignments', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'Positions include SGM for directorates, MEDDAC and MEDCEN departments of nursing and clinical staff; Regional/MSC-level Ops SGMs; Chief medical NCO for special duty assignments, large clinics, MEDDACs, and TRP CMDs.', 'acb9842a4e7eb71383f96f1b01f74772018a93ebf38ca7a789a996055beb724c', 85, 85, null, 751, null, null, false, null),
  ('7810aae1-652b-5633-9a42-8f16ff1c4888', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'self_development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) — Self-development', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'SGMs should have completed an associate degree by the end of the USASMC. See Ch. 2 (2-5g) and (2-11). Additionally, SGMs should seek appointment to CSM and/or assignments of increasing responsibility and levels of command. CSMs are selected from SGM candidates or those serving as SGMs, based on their experience, training and desire to serve as a CSM and the needs of Army. SGMs should complete Army COOL - 68Z - Certifications/Licenses and applicable, Army COOL - Manager - Certifications/Licenses.', '107b889613f31a930658b36836e48202f05adadcced7060eb39a05cf84e91dbe', 85, 85, null, 752, null, null, false, null),
  ('7ce5021d-bb37-5d02-9b86-fff95286feb2', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major (SGM) — Special assignments', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'IG SGM, SHARP SGM, Talent MGR, Congressional liaison.', '9f066d2062bc0b6dd00e5de9ebaca32b8eedccdd60d3dbe8e5a5a4ebfb28c76a', 85, 85, null, 753, null, null, false, null),
  ('44306bd7-f2a5-57d4-8ced-2f8deef07689', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'training', 'E-9', null, 'Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — Institutional training', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'See Ch. 2 (2-5g).', 'ca68ffdd227144ca14e170d8307faff9a027fff015b07dd590c9bfc78f0d2587', 85, 85, null, 754, null, null, false, null),
  ('f914a16a-cec8-5a45-9fc0-a4906f80d831', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — OF assignments', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'Positions range from medical and non-medical BN, BDE, and hospital center command positions.', '6ddbdff37d617cf8a18d5f787d7503e88439eb47a66fa88eced5b18db5504096', 85, 85, null, 755, null, null, false, null),
  ('cd7b6d26-9b83-5200-b5d2-3d4896203cb1', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — GF assignments', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'Most 68Z CSM positions are in medical units. CSM opportunities outside the medical force include CSL positions allowing 68Z, NCO Academy and garrison CSMs.', '7eaf823c0f91056b7839d52ab468b587ead812d861a9cac679878d7ab9fbf284', 85, 85, null, 756, null, null, false, null),
  ('e57a400c-1582-5ad1-b0c8-f62ff53a1914', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'self_development', 'E-9', null, 'Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — Self-development', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'CSMs should have completed an associate degree by the end of the USASMC. A bachelor’s degree completion is recommended but not required. See (2-5g) and (2-11). Additionally, CSMs should complete Army COOL - 68Z - Certifications/Licenses and applicable Army COOL - Manager - Certifications/Licenses.', 'fcef416c213448306daf1a362eec094c7dfbccb420338a1df5196f0aa94fab27', 85, 85, null, 757, null, null, false, null),
  ('270fea09-2664-57c2-8832-513598ee888f', 'db8eb8c8-2262-5526-95a5-fc552904297b', 'Army', 'enlisted', '68Z', null, 'assignments', 'E-9', null, 'Command Sergeant Major (CSM) — Special Assignments', 'Chapter 24. 68Z – Chief Medical Noncommissioned Officer', 'None.', '903ea500e7ccf842c1312b6c2f964e3e98ff146456cecec717e9a0e122bf735f', 86, 86, null, 758, null, null, false, null);
commit;

