(f) GI to Jobs. See GI to Jobs COOL Website.', 'd380e2fae4677aaf8bb4a414b4c0f71a2053359972b1a909988b1b147a1fab24', 31, 31, null, 233, null, null, false, null),
  ('453f5d60-0a1d-5fa9-b77f-832478432aa2', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92R', null, 'development', 'E-9', null, 'Sergeant Major/Command Sergeant Major — overview', 'Chapter 19. MOS 92R Parachute Rigger', 'Sergeant Majors/Command Sergeant Majors with the MOS 92A, 92Y,92F, 92G, 92M, 92R, and 92S convert to MOS 92Z, Senior Noncommissioned Logistician, See section 10-92Z. MOS 92Z—Senior Noncommissioned Logistician, CMF 92 within Smartbook DA Pam 611-21 located at https://www.milsuite.mil/.', 'd84bb937819d1fe4087b8d71a1db1541a57b55cc39a2d7d2471016b86ccd538a', 31, 31, null, 234, null, null, false, null),
  ('3965e887-dfec-5dda-9716-a986df74bb31', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'development', null, null, 'Goals for development', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'Shower and Laundry Specialists must focus and become proficient in the skill of their MOS and continue to broaden their knowledge that will in turn reflect on them positively later in their careers. Warrior Tasks and Battle Drills cannot be overlooked; the Quartermaster Soldier should enhance the tactical skills needed to survive on the battlefield and strive for excellence during the ACFT and weapons qualification.', 'ea0c0d13400da094e565d078b139fe571f6b057ec4fc1589afb3c374ad94fde6', 32, 32, null, 235, null, null, false, null),
  ('8f951d54-26b2-5d94-91e5-0e5228a07bbe', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Institutional Training', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'IET, Reclassification, BLC.', 'c6928b19702683dec69a36de32ae85d8c7df282809988d9e3ce2afcebaa88215', 32, 32, null, 236, null, null, false, null),
  ('d0ddd7b5-2026-543c-a3f3-910f5aa16f7a', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'Assignments in Operational Army units as a Shower and Laundry Specialist and Vehicle Driver.', '9a5d20de9fb3d553a8114546313c6f065fdaa39e41ef01f2bd80a03012f8908a', 32, 32, null, 237, null, null, false, null),
  ('661448bb-e62f-5a17-8c3b-5afcf04f0c54', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'Soldiers selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one (1) three-year tour. TDA assignments include Shower and Laundry Specialist.', '4cbcdd64ab99f82217717a9d480f47eca83a6cf33e093c9f7b9c77f4cf7c78a6', 32, 32, null, 238, null, null, false, null),
  ('c5943f6e-6e8a-5dc1-8664-1075b161f546', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'self_development', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Self-development', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to chapter 3; Army Career Tracker (ACT) at https://actnow.army.mil; TC 7-22.7; Army Training Information System (ATIS) at https://www.pdmatis.army.mil/.', '7345beb1d9eab7bc9ff4d40e11cfed7f7dc794420c71074b13e9a2d06abd0275', 32, 32, null, 239, null, null, false, null),
  ('d099b10e-45dc-56cf-8d32-c25071fd1519', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'training', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Additional Training', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'Combatives 1, Combat Lifesaver, Field Sanitation, Airborne, Air Assault, Ranger, and Advanced Culinary Skills Course.', 'd3ff02bbc0adfcca0eb9bf07b2d5685269a2a87ff3ec943359c0278c524c75b0', 32, 32, null, 240, null, null, false, null),
  ('0fd38345-d9e8-54ac-9141-3968df61bdf4', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'assignments', 'E-1..E-4', null, 'Private E-1–Specialist/Corporal — Special assignments', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'Special assignments 1) Broadening Assignments: None 2) MOS Enhancing: Ranger Battalion or Special Operations assignments.', '93d1fc920a5680021602d57275a0850dda6b00e179cc5213a28f4433f17ab3c2', 32, 32, null, 241, null, null, false, null),
  ('037b429d-b05f-5bf7-8642-588cef72515a', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'ALC and Reclassification.', 'cf63d356c621c858c25193d29febe2bcb14d92ae16c3f8e8fcc8fd8e148accdf', 32, 32, null, 242, null, null, false, null),
  ('bd4de5d2-6a83-5b29-801b-d2ec653b4909', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'The critical developmental assignment for an MOS 92S Sergeant as a Shower and Laundry NCO for 24 months. Although the proponent recommends all MOS 92S Sergeants serve a minimum of 12 months as a Team Chief prior to being assigned to other leadership duties in operational units, unit strengths, operational requirements, and unit priorities may require Commanders and Command Sergeant Majors to move Sergeants prior to meeting this requirement. Assignment in Operational Army units as a Team Chief and Shower/Laundry NCO.', '703dbe10bc33223ea5453fde9f9e74b13acf5778ddbaa9273a8581d4bc1871c1', 32, 32, null, 243, null, null, false, null),
  ('217e46c3-074d-538f-a073-e310ac2a5160', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'Sergeants selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one three-year tour, with the exception of those personnel required to complete a broadening tour in support of Army requirements. TDA assignments include Shower and Laundry NCO, and Field Services NCO (DSTE).', 'e98ca281c9d52f554e6775084b9c5fe1f9545ff264349ca10f2c8aaa2561dee7', 32, 32, null, 244, null, null, false, null),
  ('b217d49d-091d-5fc6-93af-d071fd979dff', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'self_development', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Self-development', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'For additional information on self-development, refer to chapter 3; Army Career Tracker (ACT) at https://actnow.army.mil; TC 7-22.7; Army Training Information System (ATIS) at https://www.pdmatis.army.mil/.', '7345beb1d9eab7bc9ff4d40e11cfed7f7dc794420c71074b13e9a2d06abd0275', 32, 32, null, 245, null, null, false, null),
  ('7e10dde5-bbc0-5b17-8ef7-e76b83842568', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'training', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Additional training', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', ', Airborne, Jumpmaster, Contracting Officer Representative (COR), Master Fitness Trainer, Master Resiliency Trainer, Enlisted Aide Training Course, Air Assault, Ranger, Unit Prevention Leader (UPL), Unit Retention NCO and Equal Opportunity Leader.', 'ef7e36bacb479716060b9ee5917dbcf5522b778815e345260535c7e32fb81790', 32, 32, null, 246, null, null, false, null),
  ('4d430f0d-a1a2-50a0-9fc8-dea5c5ed1a79', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'assignments', 'E-5', null, 'Sergeant — Special assignments', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', '1) Broadening Assignments: Recruiter, Enlisted Aide and Drill Sergeant. 2) MOS Enhancing: Ranger Battalion or Special Operations assignments.', '6c4188306d10130f2b16e4192726b97678cf5eccf0d58adf21d323e5758fddb4', 33, 33, null, 247, null, null, false, null),
  ('198f6d3b-4b86-5ee7-8cb9-03cbd52ef268', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'training', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Institutional training', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'SLC and Reclassification.', '89465a136a1bc1d444b6ef3a5cb30f668f135a6ec2e7ca121e3e36965ce77e32', 33, 33, null, 248, null, null, false, null),
  ('70221ed1-ebee-5fd2-a94d-c2e51136641d', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'assignments', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — Operational assignments', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'The critical developmental assignment for an MOS 92S Staff Sergeant as a Section Chief for 24 months or serving on staff for 24 months. Although the proponent recommends all MOS 92S Staff Sergeants serve a minimum of 24 months as a Section Chief prior to being assigned to other leadership duties in operational units, unit strengths, operational requirements, and unit priorities may require Commanders and Command Sergeant Majors to move Staff Sergeants prior to meeting this requirement. Assignments in Operational Army units as a Section Chief and Senior Shower/Laundry NCO.', 'd4f8289e88ed66c54a915b391a6e0199a766a8d11b0ee4f43493a533304e9243', 33, 33, null, 249, null, null, false, null),
  ('9fa3fdc2-1c27-5e48-8804-74401ea551e0', '7bb00f17-9863-5757-a81f-7038b54c0dc1', 'Army', 'enlisted', '92S', null, 'development', 'E-6', null, 'Staff Sergeant — TDA assignments', 'Chapter 22. MOS 92S Shower/Laundry Specialist', 'Staff Sergeants selected for TDA gain a different perspective of the unique challenges other than the operational Army. They will receive specialized training and, in some cases, access credentialing. These tours should be limited to one three-year tour, with the exception of those personnel required to complete a broadening tour in support of Army requirements. TDA assignments include Drill Sergeant, Observer Controller/Trainer, SGL, Recruiter, Instructor, and Operations Sergeant. (d) Self-development. For additional information on self-development, refer to TC 7-22.7 The NCO Guide. ACT https://actnow.army.mil.', '4a893e416c9606cd3c153d3bd990b3b5fe4fd7f25be905b3f46301d5d0de654d', 33, 33, null, 250, null, null, false, null),
