(h) Budget Execution, HQDA-BUO
(i) Budget Integration, HQDA-BUI', 'b6e15bc47d02fe5ee95e80fa1849e443c24691f2be3e8c35b122d1fe6084b331', 5, 5, '5', 15, null, null, false, null),
  ('f4a1d442-873b-5453-9bec-ec8decf32157', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'self_development', 'O-3', 'active', 'Captain — Self-developmental', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Captains must complete DoD FM Certification Level 2. Captains should strive to obtain their CDFM and complete a graduate degree. FC captains should also seek additional FC functional training, including, but not limited to, Fiscal Law, PPBE, GFEBS Cost Management, Training with Industry, Joint Staff Fellowship Program, Congressional Fellowship Program, Intermediate Data Analytics Course (IDAC), GFEBS Intermediate Course, BOBJ and the Army Comptroller Course (ACC) to enhance professional development. In addition, FC captains can compete for ACS, TWI, internships, fellowships, and other broadening programs.', '0bfc943fec49d7e090b89d93dc60137ac474a1031844d4b3a480891796ae5544', 5, 5, '5', 16, null, null, false, null),
  ('a691f10f-300f-5d97-92c2-52c757f55834', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'rank_duties', 'O-3', 'active', 'Captain — Desired Experience', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Captains must attain basic technical and tactical skills in the application of FC core competencies and information systems, MDMP, Army doctrine (see Fig.2), and unit training management. Obtaining knowledge and experience in all FC core competencies as a captain is critical to personal and professional growth. Captains must gain a basic knowledge of U.S government operations, geopolitics, fiscal law, PPBE, force structure and characteristics.', 'feaaf6b63715581bb0cffb2a033e85bbf79dfe7a7e26addc78fbe7c512316229', 5, 5, '5', 17, null, null, false, null),
  ('54009c0d-05d9-502e-9ef5-bc6e99426bce', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'training', 'O-4', 'active', 'Major — Education', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Completion of ILE prior to the 13th year of commissioned service is critical to officer professional development and the foundation in preparing for KD assignments.', '6158f68fb0497698539d32f8f5a151be8de96f2719f1fc6ff9a23157bf8db5be', 5, 5, '5', 18, null, null, false, null),
  ('6ca80d42-30f5-5a9d-91ed-e952b2da3b2c', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'assignments', 'O-4', 'active', 'Major — Key Developmental Assignments', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Majors should serve in a KD position for 18 to 24 months.
(a) Battalion Executive Officer
(b) Battalion S3
(c) 2-Star Command Deputy G–8/Comptroller
(d) 1-Star Command G–8/Comptroller
(e) Group/Regiment Comptroller
(f) Finance Support Unit Commander', '9b9408b243a71771d44ec1337497e4d3acea2cf63ee02ce5a8b725fbb33b27e6', 5, 5, '5', 19, null, null, false, null),
  ('9f13eb74-325f-5ed8-b5f6-32639536cab7', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'assignments', 'O-4', 'active', 'Major — Broadening Assignments', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Any job not listed as KD is considered broadening: “Purposeful expansion of an individual’s capabilities and understanding…that are gained through experiences in different organizational cultures and interest…” AR 600-3.
(a) Corps/ASCC/ACOM/DA/USAFMCOM Staff
(b) 3–4 Star Command Budget Officer
(c) FC School Staff
(d) Joint Assignment
(e) Office of Chief Legislative Liaison (OCLL)
(f) Inspector General
(g) ASA (FM&C) Staff
(h) AFMC Disbursing Officer
(i) AFMC Chief of Internal Control', '4074889d326c3feec9d20069898a28c3d0641a8039732add52eeeb8f08cda4ac', 6, 6, '6', 20, null, null, false, null),
  ('d64663cc-c7d7-59b5-8fa0-4ec437cd68dc', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'self_development', 'O-4', 'active', 'Major — Self-Development', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Majors must complete DoD FM Certification Level 2. They should strive to attain CDFM–A certification and complete a graduate degree or begin postgraduate or higher study. Majors should seek FC functional training, including, but not limited to, Fiscal Law, GFEBS Cost Management, GFEBS Intermediate Course, IDAC, Advanced Business Analytics Course (ABAC), the Defense Decision Support Course (DDSC), the Defense Financial Management Course (DFMC), or the Executive Comptroller Course (ECC) to enhance professional development. In addition, majors can compete for ACS, TWI, internships, fellowships, and other broadening programs.', '6016ccadb36bef9b933032d88ec20c796d5dd7c37784030b93992cf18fda03d2', 6, 6, '6', 21, null, null, false, null),
  ('0aa2b9e4-4226-556f-b346-7f781fa2099d', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'rank_duties', 'O-4', 'active', 'Major — Desired Experience', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Majors must attain immediate technical and tactical skills in the application of FC core competencies and information systems, MDMP, Army doctrine (see Fig.2), and unit training management. They must gain immediate knowledge of U.S Government operations, geopolitics, DIME (Diplomacy, Information, Military, Economic), PMESII-PT (Political, Military, Economic, Social, Infrastructure, Information, Physical Environment, and Time), ‘How the Army Runs’, Fiscal Law, PPBE, force structure, and characteristics. Majors should continue institutional, operational, and self- development efforts to expand their expertise in all aspects of FC.', 'b5e22558a27c73ccaf760d2b36ea2e24d27eabc0001c9d9381e73d04492f4fc3', 6, 6, '6', 22, null, null, false, null),
  ('a7d40bcc-1156-570f-9137-7341832d66b3', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'training', 'O-5', 'active', 'Lieutenant Colonel — Education', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Lieutenant colonels must have completed ILE as a major.', '40cea1465d07b0f2b980fd96f8c6acfde90499e7fab4500cb2fcf4730ba9ede9', 6, 6, '6', 23, null, null, false, null),
  ('53a6f6fa-270f-544c-8fe9-afa7a5fd5235', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'assignments', 'O-5', 'active', 'Lieutenant Colonel — Key Developmental Assignments', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'Lieutenant Colonels should serve in a KD position for 24 months. To count for KD, the position must come from the Centralized Selection List (CSL).
(a) Battalion Command (CSL)
(b) G–8/Comptroller (CSL)', '5407c28446823b632f79bc35011adc76279e5a9a2677561b3a2dd218a9c393a3', 6, 6, '6', 24, null, null, false, null),
  ('aea754dd-87b2-5a89-b5f2-d8e947f40c87', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'assignments', 'O-5', 'active', 'Lieutenant Colonel — Broadening Assignments', '3. Finance and Comptroller Regular Army Officer Development', 'All non-CSL positions are considered broadening: “Purposeful expansion of an individual’s capabilities and understanding…that are gained through experiences in different organizational cultures and interest…” AR 600-3.
(a) ASCC/ACOM/OSD/DA/USAFMCOM Staff
(b) FC School Director of Training
