  ('261651f3-ff5a-5adf-8f4d-78eebaebfd10', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'assignments', 'O-6', 'guard', 'Field Grade — Broadening assignments for colonels (see Fig 3)', '6. Finance and Comptroller Army National Guard Officer Development', '(a) DA/Joint Staff Officer
(b) ASA(FM&C) Staff Officer
(c) ARNG USPF&O', '55d8f9b631b9c7e10f39b0a24b3549194ccbd7a4bd717e64d1f8ab27fd8ef64e', 15, 15, '15', 63, null, null, false, null),
  ('3632156a-a23d-51e2-82cc-53293710b38b', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'self_development', 'O-4..O-6', 'guard', 'Field Grade — Additional Training', '6. Finance and Comptroller Army National Guard Officer Development', 'Field grade officers must obtain and maintain their mandated DoD Financial Management program certification at Level III. Additionally, field grade officers should obtain a professional credential. Examples include CDFM, CGFM, CGAP, or CPFO. ARNG field grade officers should also seek additional Financial Management functional training to ensure they are well-rounded. See Figure 1 for recommended functional training. ARNG field grade officers should also possess a graduate degree from an accredited academic institution.', '40a0593f9300e0daa2b0c8f7d7685b45065118ba943d888707a08461cc102628', 15, 15, '15', 64, null, null, false, null),
  ('a6b72e9a-2785-5fa3-af27-8ddcad4ff50d', 'a6b40ab7-9883-5645-a496-0e2393fba45b', 'Army', 'officer', '36A', 'Finance and Comptroller Officer', 'prerequisites', null, 'guard', 'Branch Code 36A Requirements', '6. Finance and Comptroller Army National Guard Officer Development', 'The officer can request a branch transfer by completing the requirements listed below in section (1) and one or more of the requirements in sections (2) to (5):
(1) Officers who have completed an AOC or CCC in a different branch may satisfy branch code 36A by completing the ATIS courses Disbursing Operations Course, Accounts Payable Administration Course, and; the following ATRRS courses: GFEBS Cost Management and Army PPBE.
(2) A minimum of 2 years in a Finance position in a state or territory.
(3) Civilian position equivalent with tasks associated to CMF 36.
(4) Utilization assignment within the states, territories, and ARNG HQs.
(5) Complete the Defense Comptrollership Program. Branch Transfer for Army National Guard Officers. ARNG officers seeking branch transfer to BC 36A must apply through their State/Territory and ARNG HQ G1. State Officer Personnel Managers (OPMs) and ARNG HRH-O must have maximum flexibility in awarding officers BC 36A. Requests should not come to the Finance and Comptroller School Proponent. All branch transfer requests for officers in an ARNG Title 10 status must also go through the ARNG HQ G8. Refer to NGR 600-100 for additional information.', '7fdeb0484f076ce186cc87897fa1db34306870bf9068b6b9fafd13c7a0f96966', 15, 15, '15', 65, null, null, false, null);
